<section id="S1" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">1. </span>Introduction</h2>

<div id="S1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We consider the defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equation</p>
<table id="S1.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(1)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\partial_{t}u+\Delta u-|u|^{p-1}u=0,\qquad(t,x)\in[0,T)\times\mathbb{R}^{d}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\partial_{t}u+\Delta u-|u|^{p-1}u=0,\qquad(t,x)\in[0,T)\times\mathbb{R}^{d}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The scaling symmetry <math id="S1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{\lambda}(t,x)=\lambda^{\frac{2}{p-1}}u(\lambda^{2}t,\lambda x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{\lambda}(t,x)=\lambda^{\frac{2}{p-1}}u(\lambda^{2}t,\lambda x)</annotation></semantics></math> leaves the homogeneous Sobolev norm <math id="S1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{H}^{s_{c}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{H}^{s_{c}}</annotation></semantics></math> invariant, where</p>
<table id="S1.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{c}=\frac{d}{2}-\frac{2}{p-1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{c}=\frac{d}{2}-\frac{2}{p-1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">The energy supercritical regime corresponds to <math id="S1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{c}&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{c}&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, or equivalently <math id="S1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&gt;1+\frac{4}{d-2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&gt;1+\frac{4}{d-2}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math>. In this range, the scaling critical regularity lies above the energy regularity, and conservation of mass and energy does not provide an a priori bound on the critical Sobolev norm. Throughout the paper, we restrict to <math id="S1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(d,p)\in\{(3,27),(4,9),(5,7)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>27</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>9</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(d,p)\in\{(3,27),(4,9),(5,7)\}</annotation></semantics></math>, all in the energy supercritical regime. Our main result constructs finite-time, asymptotically self-similar blow-up solutions from smooth, radial, compactly supported initial data.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.Thmthm1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_thm">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S1.Thmthm1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 1.1</span></span><span id="S1.Thmthm1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S1.Thmthm1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.Thmthm1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.Thmthm1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For every <math id="S1.Thmthm1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(d,p)\in\{(3,27),(4,9),(5,7)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>27</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>9</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(d,p)\in\{(3,27),(4,9),(5,7)\}</annotation></semantics></math>, there are radial initial data
<math id="S1.Thmthm1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{0}\in C_{c}^{\infty}(\mathbb{R}^{d};\mathbb{C})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>ℂ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{0}\in C_{c}^{\infty}(\mathbb{R}^{d};\mathbb{C})</annotation></semantics></math> whose corresponding solution
of (<a href="#S1.E1" title="In 1. Introduction ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) blows up at some finite time <math id="S1.Thmthm1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. The solution belongs to
<math id="S1.Thmthm1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C([0,T);H^{m}(\mathbb{R}^{d};\mathbb{C}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>ℂ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C([0,T);H^{m}(\mathbb{R}^{d};\mathbb{C}))</annotation></semantics></math> for every integer <math id="S1.Thmthm1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Moreover, there are <math id="S1.Thmthm1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="S1.Thmthm1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, and a smooth radial self-similar profile <math id="S1.Thmthm1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>, such that, with
<math id="S1.Thmthm1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=\log\frac{T}{T-t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=\log\frac{T}{T-t}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S1.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\left\|(T-t)^{\frac{1}{p-1}}e^{i\Omega\tau}u\left(t,\sqrt{T-t}\,\cdot\right)-Q\right\|_{L^{\infty}}=O((T-t)^{\mu})\quad\text{as }t\uparrow T." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.392em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>μ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">as </mtext><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|(T-t)^{\frac{1}{p-1}}e^{i\Omega\tau}u\left(t,\sqrt{T-t}\,\cdot\right)-Q\right\|_{L^{\infty}}=O((T-t)^{\mu})\quad\text{as }t\uparrow T.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.Thmthm1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.Thmthm1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consequently,</span></p>
<table id="S1.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(2)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|u(t)\|_{L^{\infty}}=\frac{\|Q\|_{L^{\infty}}+O((T-t)^{\mu})}{(T-t)^{\frac{1}{p-1}}}\quad\text{as }t\uparrow T," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>μ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup></mfrac></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">as </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|u(t)\|_{L^{\infty}}=\frac{\|Q\|_{L^{\infty}}+O((T-t)^{\mu})}{(T-t)^{\frac{1}{p-1}}}\quad\text{as }t\uparrow T,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.Thmthm1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.Thmthm1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and</span></p>
<table id="S1.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{t\uparrow T}\|u(t)\|_{\dot{H}^{s_{c}}}=\infty." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></msup></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{t\uparrow T}\|u(t)\|_{\dot{H}^{s_{c}}}=\infty.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S1.Thmthm2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_rem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S1.Thmthm2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark 1.2</span></span><span id="S1.Thmthm2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="S1.Thmthm2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.Thmthm2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Merle, Raphaël, Rodnianski and Szeftel <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib52" title="" class="ltx_ref">52</a>]</cite> constructed smooth, well localized radial solutions blowing up in finite time for <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(d,p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(d,p)</annotation></semantics></math> equal to <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(5,9)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>9</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(5,9)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(6,5)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(6,5)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(8,3)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(8,3)</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(9,3)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(9,3)</annotation></semantics></math>. Theorem <a href="#S1.Thmthm1" title="Theorem 1.1. ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a> extends the existence of finite time blow-up to dimensions three and four, which were left open in their work, and to the nonlinearity <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=7</annotation></semantics></math> in dimension five. The blow-up dynamics in dimension five are also different. Their construction is governed at leading order by a self-similar compressible Euler flow, with quantum pressure treated as a perturbation, and yields a blow-up rate which breaks the NLS scaling. In contrast, our solutions are asymptotically self-similar at the NLS scaling and obey the rate (<a href="#S1.E2" title="In Theorem 1.1. ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S1.Thmthm3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_rem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S1.Thmthm3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark 1.3</span></span><span id="S1.Thmthm3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="S1.Thmthm3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.Thmthm3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The choice of the three pairs in Theorem <a href="#S1.Thmthm1" title="Theorem 1.1. ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a> is related to the computer-assisted profile construction. As explained in the proof of Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmthm10" title="Lemma 3.10 (Computer-assisted bounds). ‣ 3.4. Computer-assisted proof of the matching conditions ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.10</span></a>, the profile ODE is numerically easier to solve for large <math id="S1.Thmthm3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, we first locate a profile in that regime and then use a continuation method in <math id="S1.Thmthm3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(d,p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(d,p)</annotation></semantics></math> to the desired pair. We selected <math id="S1.Thmthm3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(3,27)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>27</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(3,27)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S1.Thmthm3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(4,9)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>9</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(4,9)</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S1.Thmthm3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(5,7)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(5,7)</annotation></semantics></math> because this continuation and the subsequent estimates close with enough margin for these cases. Our nonrigorous shooting experiments find profiles for many other energy-supercritical parameters, although the rigorous construction in this paper is restricted to the stated cases.</p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="S1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">1.1. </span>Historical background</h3>

<div id="S1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The flow (<a href="#S1.E1" title="In 1. Introduction ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) conserves the mass and energy functionals</p>
<table id="S1.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(3)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M(u)=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}|u|^{2}\,dx,\qquad E(u)=\frac{1}{2}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}|\nabla u|^{2}\,dx+\frac{1}{p+1}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}|u|^{p+1}\,dx," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M(u)=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}|u|^{2}\,dx,\qquad E(u)=\frac{1}{2}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}|\nabla u|^{2}\,dx+\frac{1}{p+1}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}|u|^{p+1}\,dx,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and it is invariant under the scaling <math id="S1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{\lambda}(t,x)=\lambda^{\frac{2}{p-1}}u(\lambda^{2}t,\lambda x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{\lambda}(t,x)=\lambda^{\frac{2}{p-1}}u(\lambda^{2}t,\lambda x)</annotation></semantics></math>, which preserves the homogeneous norm <math id="S1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{H}^{s_{c}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{H}^{s_{c}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The Cauchy problem is locally well-posed in <math id="S1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>H</mi><mi>s</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{s}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S1.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\geq s_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\geq s_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> by Strichartz estimates <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">33</a>, <a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>, <a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">16</a>]</cite>, and the conservation laws yield global well-posedness in the mass subcritical and energy subcritical ranges. At the critical levels, the conserved quantities control precisely the scaling invariant norm, and the defocusing problem is by now completely understood: global well-posedness and scattering hold in the energy-critical case <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>, <a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">35</a>, <a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">23</a>, <a href="#bib.bib59" title="" class="ltx_ref">59</a>, <a href="#bib.bib73" title="" class="ltx_ref">73</a>]</cite> and in the mass-critical case <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib66" title="" class="ltx_ref">66</a>, <a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">41</a>, <a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">27</a>, <a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">28</a>, <a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">29</a>]</cite>. In the energy supercritical regime <math id="S1.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{c}&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{c}&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math> considered here, no conservation law controls the critical norm, and the available results are conditional. Using the concentration compactness and rigidity method of Kenig–Merle <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">37</a>, <a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">38</a>, <a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">39</a>, <a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">40</a>]</cite>, Killip–Visan <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">42</a>]</cite> and Li–Li <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib45" title="" class="ltx_ref">45</a>]</cite> proved that a solution which remains bounded in <math id="S1.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{H}^{s_{c}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{H}^{s_{c}}</annotation></semantics></math> is global and scatters; see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">50</a>]</cite> for the most recent extension of the admissible exponents in high dimensions and <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>]</cite> for blow-up criteria below the scaling regularity. In particular, the maximal solution issued from smooth data either is global or its <math id="S1.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{H}^{s_{c}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{H}^{s_{c}}</annotation></semantics></math> norm blows up in finite time. An analogous conditional scattering result for the defocusing <math id="S1.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{H}^{1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{H}^{1/2}</annotation></semantics></math>-critical equation in dimensions <math id="S1.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq 4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq 4</annotation></semantics></math> was proved by Murphy <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib55" title="" class="ltx_ref">55</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">This collection of facts led to the belief that the a priori bound on the critical norm should always hold. Bourgain <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>]</cite> explicitly conjectured that the defocusing energy supercritical Schrödinger and wave equations are globally well-posed and scatter; see also the discussions in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">40</a>, <a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">42</a>]</cite>. Numerical simulations of Colliander–Simpson–Sulem <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">24</a>]</cite> supported this belief. Global regularity was proved for logarithmically supercritical wave equations <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib63" title="" class="ltx_ref">63</a>, <a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">25</a>]</cite> and for a supercritical wave equation in two dimensions <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib61" title="" class="ltx_ref">61</a>]</cite>, and large global solutions were constructed for supercritical wave equations in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">43</a>]</cite> and for the energy supercritical NLS in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite>. Indications in the opposite direction were the finite time blow-up constructed by Tao <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib64" title="" class="ltx_ref">64</a>, <a href="#bib.bib65" title="" class="ltx_ref">65</a>]</cite> for defocusing wave and Schrödinger <em id="S1.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">systems</em> sharing the same scaling and conservation laws as (<a href="#S1.E1" title="In 1. Introduction ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>), and the norm inflation results at low supercritical regularity of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">22</a>, <a href="#bib.bib69" title="" class="ltx_ref">69</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The conjecture was disproved by Merle–Raphaël–Rodnianski–Szeftel <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib52" title="" class="ltx_ref">52</a>]</cite>, who constructed <math id="S1.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> well localized radial initial data leading to finite time blow-up of (<a href="#S1.E1" title="In 1. Introduction ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) for <math id="S1.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(d,p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(d,p)</annotation></semantics></math> equal to <math id="S1.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(5,9)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>9</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(5,9)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S1.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(6,5)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(6,5)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S1.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(8,3)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(8,3)</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="S1.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(9,3)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(9,3)</annotation></semantics></math>. Their mechanism is hydrodynamical. Through the Madelung transform <math id="S1.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u=\sqrt{\rho}\,e^{i\psi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>ρ</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u=\sqrt{\rho}\,e^{i\psi}</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib51" title="" class="ltx_ref">51</a>]</cite>, equation (<a href="#S1.E1" title="In 1. Introduction ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) becomes the compressible Euler system with adiabatic exponent <math id="S1.SS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=\frac{p+1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=\frac{p+1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, forced by a quantum pressure term proportional to <math id="S1.SS1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla\big(\Delta\sqrt{\rho}/\sqrt{\rho}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>ρ</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mi>ρ</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla\big(\Delta\sqrt{\rho}/\sqrt{\rho}\big)</annotation></semantics></math>. In the blow-up regime of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib52" title="" class="ltx_ref">52</a>]</cite>, the quantum pressure is a perturbation. The leading order dynamics are those of compressible Euler, and the blow-up profiles are the smooth radial imploding self-similar profiles constructed in the companion paper <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib53" title="" class="ltx_ref">53</a>]</cite>; see also <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib54" title="" class="ltx_ref">54</a>]</cite> for the corresponding singularity formation for the compressible Euler and Navier–Stokes equations. The Eulerian regime requires the self-similar blow-up speed <math id="S1.SS1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> to exceed <math id="S1.SS1.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>, which is only possible when <math id="S1.SS1.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq 5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq 5</annotation></semantics></math>, and the existence of blow-up solutions in dimensions <math id="S1.SS1.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=3,4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=3,4</annotation></semantics></math> was left open <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib52" title="" class="ltx_ref">52</a>, Section 1.4]</cite>. The solutions obtained in this way are of type II, meaning that they blow up at a rate different from the self-similar one and break scaling. Building on their non-radial implosion construction for compressible fluids <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite>, Cao-Labora–Gómez-Serrano–Shi–Staffilani <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>]</cite> extended this construction to non-radial data for <math id="S1.SS1.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(d,p)=(8,3)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(d,p)=(8,3)</annotation></semantics></math>, with smooth periodic initial data on <math id="S1.SS1.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{T}^{8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝕋</mi><mn>8</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{T}^{8}</annotation></semantics></math> and with smooth initial data on <math id="S1.SS1.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>8</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{8}</annotation></semantics></math> which do not vanish at infinity. The hydrodynamical formulation of (<a href="#S1.E1" title="In 1. Introduction ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) with the quantum pressure retained has also been studied on its own in the theory of quantum fluids; see Antonelli–Marcati <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">1</a>, <a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>]</cite> and Carles–Danchin–Saut <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">15</a>]</cite> for finite energy weak solutions and for the precise relation with (<a href="#S1.E1" title="In 1. Introduction ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Exact self-similar solutions <math id="S1.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u(t,x)=(T-t)^{-\frac{1}{p-1}}e^{-i\Omega\tau}Q(x/\sqrt{T-t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u(t,x)=(T-t)^{-\frac{1}{p-1}}e^{-i\Omega\tau}Q(x/\sqrt{T-t})</annotation></semantics></math> are the basic blow-up objects of the focusing mass supercritical NLS. Their existence was observed numerically; see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>, <a href="#bib.bib58" title="" class="ltx_ref">58</a>]</cite> and the book <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib62" title="" class="ltx_ref">62</a>]</cite>, and rigorous constructions are recent: Bahri–Martel–Raphaël <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>]</cite> in the slightly supercritical regime, Dahne–Figueras <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">26</a>]</cite> far from the critical exponent, including the three dimensional cubic case, Donninger–Schörkhuber <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">31</a>]</cite> and Donninger–Lichtnecker <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">30</a>]</cite> for the cubic and nearly cubic three dimensional equations, and Cao-Labora–Gómez-Serrano–Shi–Staffilani <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>]</cite> for the hydrodynamic formulation. Their finite codimensional stability was established by Li <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">46</a>]</cite>; see also <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">47</a>, <a href="#bib.bib48" title="" class="ltx_ref">48</a>]</cite>. In the defocusing case, on the contrary, admissible self-similar solutions were expected not to exist <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib52" title="" class="ltx_ref">52</a>, Section 1.3]</cite>. Self-similar solutions with finite energy are indeed excluded by energy conservation and scaling, see (<a href="#S2.E7" title="In 2. Self-similar profile equation ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>) below. Theorem <a href="#S1.Thmthm1" title="Theorem 1.1. ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a> shows that, once the finite energy requirement on the profile is dropped, smooth radial self-similar profiles of the defocusing equation exist for <math id="S1.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(d,p)\in\{(3,27),(4,9),(5,7)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>27</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>9</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(d,p)\in\{(3,27),(4,9),(5,7)\}</annotation></semantics></math>, and that they govern the blow-up of smooth, compactly supported initial data at the self-similar rate (<a href="#S1.E2" title="In Theorem 1.1. ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>). In the profile equation (<a href="#S2.E6" title="In 2. Self-similar profile equation ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>) the Laplacian and the nonlinearity enter at the same order, so the quantum pressure is not a perturbation and no compressible Euler regime is involved. To the best of our knowledge, this is the first construction of finite time blow-up for the defocusing NLS in dimensions three and four.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">One of the fundamental pillars of the proof relies on a computer-assisted argument. The main paradigm is to replace floating-point numbers on a computer with rigorous bounds. These bounds are then propagated through every operation performed by the computer, taking into account any error made throughout the process. We refer the reader to the books <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib70" title="" class="ltx_ref">70</a>, <a href="#bib.bib56" title="" class="ltx_ref">56</a>]</cite> and to the survey <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">34</a>]</cite> for a general treatment of computer-assisted proofs in PDE. In our case, the computer certifies that the solution regular at the origin and the solution with a pure slow tail at infinity can be matched at an intermediate radius, following the shooting and matching strategy of Dahne–Figueras <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">26</a>]</cite>. Closest to our setting, van den Berg–Groothedde–Williams <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib71" title="" class="ltx_ref">71</a>]</cite> proved the existence of a localized radial solution of a singular Ginzburg–Landau ordinary differential equation. They rewrite the equation as an integral equation by means of a Green function, and prove with computer assistance that the resulting map is a contraction around a numerical approximation. Computer-assisted constructions of self-similar blow-up profiles have appeared in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>, <a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>]</cite> for compressible Euler, in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>, <a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">18</a>, <a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>]</cite> for the Hou–Luo model, the Boussinesq and the incompressible Euler equations, and in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">26</a>, <a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">31</a>]</cite> for the focusing NLS. Our implementation uses the Arb library <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">36</a>]</cite> and the code is available at <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">1.2. </span>Strategy of the proof</h3>

<div id="S1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We explain the main steps in the proof of Theorem <a href="#S1.Thmthm1" title="Theorem 1.1. ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a>. The construction consists of finding a smooth self-similar profile with prescribed behavior at infinity, and then producing solutions with localized initial data which converge to this profile in rescaled variables. The first step is computer-assisted and the second follows from spectral estimates and a finite-codimensional nonlinear stability argument.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We seek a radial profile <math id="S1.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> and a frequency <math id="S1.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</p>
<table id="S1.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u(t,x)=(T-t)^{-\frac{1}{p-1}}e^{-i\Omega\tau}Q(y),\qquad\tau=\log\frac{T}{T-t},\qquad y=\frac{x}{\sqrt{T-t}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>x</mi><msqrt><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u(t,x)=(T-t)^{-\frac{1}{p-1}}e^{-i\Omega\tau}Q(y),\qquad\tau=\log\frac{T}{T-t},\qquad y=\frac{x}{\sqrt{T-t}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">solves (<a href="#S1.E1" title="In 1. Introduction ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>). This gives the profile equation (<a href="#S2.E6" title="In 2. Self-similar profile equation ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>), in which dispersion and the nonlinearity both enter at leading order. After fixing the constant phase, regularity at the origin leaves two real shooting parameters, <math id="S1.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(0)=A&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(0)=A&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S1.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="S1.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\prime}(0)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\prime}(0)=0</annotation></semantics></math>. At infinity, the linearized equation has two distinct asymptotic modes,</p>
<table id="S1.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="Q_{\mathrm{slow}}(r)\sim C_{s}r^{-\frac{2}{p-1}+2i\Omega},\qquad Q_{\mathrm{fast}}(r)\sim C_{f}e^{-ir^{2}/4}r^{-d+\frac{2}{p-1}-2i\Omega}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>slow</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>fast</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi><mi>r</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{\mathrm{slow}}(r)\sim C_{s}r^{-\frac{2}{p-1}+2i\Omega},\qquad Q_{\mathrm{fast}}(r)\sim C_{f}e^{-ir^{2}/4}r^{-d+\frac{2}{p-1}-2i\Omega}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Since the second mode has a factor with a quadratic phase, each derivative introduces a growing factor. A nonzero fast mode has derivatives outside of <math id="S1.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> at every integer order <math id="S1.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j&gt;s_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j&gt;s_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>, whereas the slow mode has derivatives in <math id="S1.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> at those orders. We therefore impose <math id="S1.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{f}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{f}=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S1.SS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{s}\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{s}\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, as required by the stability argument.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">To construct such a profile, we match a solution regular at the origin to a solution with a pure slow tail at infinity, following the shooting approach of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">26</a>]</cite>. Near the origin, a finite Taylor expansion and a contraction argument give an enclosure of the exact solution. At infinity, we construct a finite asymptotic expansion and control its remainder again using a contraction argument. To do this we obtain a right inverse built from the two linear modes at infinity. This gives an exact solution at infinity with the prescribed slow coefficient and no fast component, together with an expansion to every algebraic order. At an intermediate radius, we match these two solutions. These are three real conditions in the three parameters <math id="S1.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(A,\Omega,K)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(A,\Omega,K)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S1.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=|C_{s}|^{p-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=|C_{s}|^{p-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. A zero of the matching map joins the solutions up to a constant phase and yields the global profile of Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmthm1" title="Theorem 3.1. ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The need for computer assistance arises in connecting the two endpoint constructions. For the fixed pairs <math id="S1.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(d,p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(d,p)</annotation></semantics></math> in Theorem <a href="#S1.Thmthm1" title="Theorem 1.1. ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a>, our argument has no small parameter which controls the intermediate nonlinear regime. The local expansions alone therefore do not establish that the matching conditions can be satisfied. We overcome this difficulty by deriving explicit bounds for the endpoint remainders, the propagation of errors on finite intervals, and the parameter derivatives of the shooting problem. Interval arithmetic then verifies a finite collection of strict inequalities near an approximate matching zero. Brouwer’s fixed-point theorem subsequently gives an exact zero. All computational assertions are collected in Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmthm10" title="Lemma 3.10 (Computer-assisted bounds). ‣ 3.4. Computer-assisted proof of the matching conditions ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.10</span></a> and the code can be found in the supplementary material and at <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The resulting profile has infinite energy because of its slow tail, so the exact self-similar solution does not yet give Theorem <a href="#S1.Thmthm1" title="Theorem 1.1. ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a>. To localize it, we use a finite-codimensional stability argument and write the rescaled solution as <math id="S1.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V=Q+v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V=Q+v</annotation></semantics></math>. We work in the radial space</p>
<table id="S1.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}_{s}=\dot{H}^{s}_{\mathrm{rad}}(\mathbb{R}^{d};\mathbb{C})\cap\dot{H}^{k_{\star}}_{\mathrm{rad}}(\mathbb{R}^{d};\mathbb{C}),\qquad s_{c}&lt;s&lt;d/2,\qquad k_{\star}\in\mathbb{N}\text{ sufficiently large}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>rad</mi><mi>s</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>ℂ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>rad</mi><msub><mi>k</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>ℂ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> sufficiently large</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}_{s}=\dot{H}^{s}_{\mathrm{rad}}(\mathbb{R}^{d};\mathbb{C})\cap\dot{H}^{k_{\star}}_{\mathrm{rad}}(\mathbb{R}^{d};\mathbb{C}),\qquad s_{c}&lt;s&lt;d/2,\qquad k_{\star}\in\mathbb{N}\text{ sufficiently large}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.SS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p">This space contains <math id="S1.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>, embeds into <math id="S1.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math>, and is a Banach algebra. Moreover, cutting off the slow tail produces an arbitrarily small perturbation in <math id="S1.SS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>. Our spectral analysis follows the strategy of obtaining dissipativity modulo a compact perturbation; see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib52" title="" class="ltx_ref">52</a>, <a href="#bib.bib54" title="" class="ltx_ref">54</a>, <a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>, <a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">21</a>]</cite>. To apply complex spectral theory, we use the matrix formulation and the associated <math id="S1.SS2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{J}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{J}</annotation></semantics></math>-invariance argument as in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib60" title="" class="ltx_ref">60</a>, <a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">46</a>]</cite>. The decay of the profile and its derivatives gives quadratic spatial decay for the potential coefficients of the linearized operator. An energy estimate, together with compact-perturbation theory, shows that the essential growth bound of the linearized semigroup is negative. After removing the finitely many neutral and unstable generalized eigenspaces, the linearized semigroup decays exponentially on the remaining stable subspace; see Proposition <a href="#S4.Thmthm7" title="Proposition 4.7. ‣ 4.2. Spectral theory for the linearized operator ‣ 4. Self-similar blow-up ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.7</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">The nonlinear remainder is at least quadratic in <math id="S1.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> in the <math id="S1.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> norm. We establish nonlinear stability using the standard Lyapunov–Perron construction; see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib67" title="" class="ltx_ref">67</a>, Section 9.2]</cite>. A contraction argument selects the neutral and unstable components of the initial perturbation as functions of its stable component, so that <math id="S1.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> decays exponentially in self-similar time. This defines a finite-codimensional manifold of initial data for <math id="S1.SS2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p">To construct localized data on this manifold, we use a finite-dimensional localization argument related to the constructions in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib49" title="" class="ltx_ref">49</a>, <a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">46</a>]</cite>. We first replace <math id="S1.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="S1.SS2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi_{R}Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi_{R}Q</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S1.SS2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> is a smooth radial cutoff at a large radius <math id="S1.SS2.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>. We then add a small correction <math id="S1.SS2.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> from a fixed finite-dimensional space of smooth compactly supported radial functions. A further contraction chooses <math id="S1.SS2.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> so that <math id="S1.SS2.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(0)=\chi_{R}Q+g_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(0)=\chi_{R}Q+g_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> belongs to this manifold. This proves Proposition <a href="#S4.Thmthm8" title="Proposition 4.8. ‣ 4.3. Stability and localization ‣ 4. Self-similar blow-up ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.8</span></a> and gives smooth compactly supported initial data for the original equation.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S1.SSx1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Acknowledgements</h3>

<div id="S1.SSx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SSx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">KB, AC and JGS were partially supported by the NSF under grants DMS-2245017, DMS-2554957 and DMS-2434314. JS was partially supported by the Travel Support for Mathematicians program from the Simons Foundation.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S1.SSx2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">AI Disclosure</h3>

<div id="S1.SSx2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SSx2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The authors have used the LLMs GPT-5.6 and GPT-6 during the development of this work. These models have been employed for mathematical exploration, executing proof strategies and assisting with calculations. The main high level ideas of this paper were generated by the authors. The implementation of the code in the supplementary material was also done with the assistance of the same models. All mathematical statements, proofs and code scripts have been checked by the authors, who take full responsibility. All proofs and code scripts influenced by LLMs have been substantially rewritten.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S2" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">2. </span>Self-similar profile equation</h2>

<div id="S2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We seek exact self-similar solutions of (<a href="#S1.E1" title="In 1. Introduction ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) in the complex variable. Denote the nonlinearity by</p>
<table id="S2.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N(q)=|q|^{p-1}q=q^{\frac{p+1}{2}}\overline{q}^{\,\frac{p-1}{2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N(q)=|q|^{p-1}q=q^{\frac{p+1}{2}}\overline{q}^{\,\frac{p-1}{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">For <math id="S2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, use the similarity coordinates</p>
<table id="S2.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(4)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=\log\frac{T}{T-t},\qquad y=\frac{x}{\sqrt{T-t}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>x</mi><msqrt><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=\log\frac{T}{T-t},\qquad y=\frac{x}{\sqrt{T-t}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Thus <math id="S2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\tau/dt=(T-t)^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\tau/dt=(T-t)^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\uparrow T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\uparrow T</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to <math id="S2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="S2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, set</p>
<table id="S2.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(5)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u(t,x)=(T-t)^{-\frac{1}{p-1}}e^{-i\Omega\tau}Q(y),\qquad y=\frac{x}{\sqrt{T-t}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>x</mi><msqrt><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u(t,x)=(T-t)^{-\frac{1}{p-1}}e^{-i\Omega\tau}Q(y),\qquad y=\frac{x}{\sqrt{T-t}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="S2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial_{t}\tau=(T-t)^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{t}\tau=(T-t)^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial_{t}y=y/[2(T-t)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{t}y=y/[2(T-t)]</annotation></semantics></math>, substitution into (<a href="#S1.E1" title="In 1. Introduction ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) gives the profile equation</p>
<table id="S2.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(6)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{y}Q-|Q|^{p-1}Q+\Omega Q+i\left(\frac{1}{p-1}Q+\frac{1}{2}y\cdot\nabla_{y}Q\right)=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>y</mi></msub><mi>Q</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{y}Q-|Q|^{p-1}Q+\Omega Q+i\left(\frac{1}{p-1}Q+\frac{1}{2}y\cdot\nabla_{y}Q\right)=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p1.5" class="ltx_p">If a nonzero bounded smooth profile <math id="S2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> exists globally, (<a href="#S2.E5" title="In 2. Self-similar profile equation ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>) gives an exact solution with</p>
<table id="S2.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|u(t)\|_{L^{\infty}}=(T-t)^{-\frac{1}{p-1}}\|Q\|_{L^{\infty}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|u(t)\|_{L^{\infty}}=(T-t)^{-\frac{1}{p-1}}\|Q\|_{L^{\infty}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p1.6" class="ltx_p">However, these solutions may not have finite energy (<a href="#S1.E3" title="In 1.1. Historical background ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>). For the exact ansatz (<a href="#S2.E5" title="In 2. Self-similar profile equation ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>), scaling gives</p>
<table id="S2.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(7)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E(u(t))=(T-t)^{s_{c}-1}E(Q)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E(u(t))=(T-t)^{s_{c}-1}E(Q).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p1.7" class="ltx_p">If <math id="S2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E(Q)&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E(Q)&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math> and the associated solution lies in a class where energy is conserved, then <math id="S2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{c}&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{c}&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math> forces <math id="S2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E(Q)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E(Q)=0</annotation></semantics></math> and thus <math id="S2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus the nontrivial profiles must be localized to prove Theorem <a href="#S1.Thmthm1" title="Theorem 1.1. ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a>, as in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib52" title="" class="ltx_ref">52</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We now restrict to radial self-similar profiles and study their asymptotic behavior at the origin and at infinity. For a radial profile, write <math id="S2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(y)=Q(r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(y)=Q(r)</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=|y|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=|y|</annotation></semantics></math>. Equation (<a href="#S2.E6" title="In 2. Self-similar profile equation ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>) becomes</p>
<table id="S2.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(8)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\prime\prime}+\frac{d-1}{r}Q^{\prime}-|Q|^{p-1}Q+\Omega Q+i\left(\frac{1}{p-1}Q+\frac{r}{2}Q^{\prime}\right)=0,\qquad r&gt;0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>r</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\prime\prime}+\frac{d-1}{r}Q^{\prime}-|Q|^{p-1}Q+\Omega Q+i\left(\frac{1}{p-1}Q+\frac{r}{2}Q^{\prime}\right)=0,\qquad r&gt;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">After fixing the constant phase, we prescribe</p>
<table id="S2.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(9)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(0)=A&gt;0,\qquad Q^{\prime}(0)=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(0)=A&gt;0,\qquad Q^{\prime}(0)=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Smooth radial profiles extend evenly across <math id="S2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Write <math id="S2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(r)=A+Br^{2}+O(r^{4})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(r)=A+Br^{2}+O(r^{4})</annotation></semantics></math>, so that</p>
<table id="S2.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\prime\prime}(r)+\frac{d-1}{r}Q^{\prime}(r)=2dB+O(r^{2}),\qquad\frac{r}{2}Q^{\prime}(r)=O(r^{2})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>r</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\prime\prime}(r)+\frac{d-1}{r}Q^{\prime}(r)=2dB+O(r^{2}),\qquad\frac{r}{2}Q^{\prime}(r)=O(r^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p2.4" class="ltx_p">The coefficients in (<a href="#S2.E8" title="In 2. Self-similar profile equation ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>) therefore give <math id="S2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2dB-A^{p}+\left(\Omega+\frac{i}{p-1}\right)A=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2dB-A^{p}+\left(\Omega+\frac{i}{p-1}\right)A=0</annotation></semantics></math>, and hence</p>
<table id="S2.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(r)=A+\frac{A}{2d}\left(A^{p-1}-\Omega-\frac{i}{p-1}\right)r^{2}+O(r^{4})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>A</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(r)=A+\frac{A}{2d}\left(A^{p-1}-\Omega-\frac{i}{p-1}\right)r^{2}+O(r^{4}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">At infinity, the two leading behaviors are determined by the linear equation</p>
<table id="S2.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{\prime\prime}+\left(\frac{d-1}{r}+\frac{ir}{2}\right)q^{\prime}+\left(\Omega+\frac{i}{p-1}\right)q=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>r</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{\prime\prime}+\left(\frac{d-1}{r}+\frac{ir}{2}\right)q^{\prime}+\left(\Omega+\frac{i}{p-1}\right)q=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">We first study this asymptotic regime formally. Exact linear solutions with these asymptotics are constructed in Subsection <a href="#S2.SS1" title="2.1. Linear exterior modes ‣ 2. Self-similar profile equation ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>. For an algebraic ansatz <math id="S2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(r)=r^{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>α</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(r)=r^{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>, substitution gives</p>
<table id="S2.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{\prime\prime}+\left(\frac{d-1}{r}+\frac{ir}{2}\right)q^{\prime}+\left(\Omega+\frac{i}{p-1}\right)q=r^{\alpha}\left[\Omega+\frac{i}{p-1}+\frac{i\alpha}{2}+\frac{\alpha(\alpha+d-2)}{r^{2}}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>r</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>α</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{\prime\prime}+\left(\frac{d-1}{r}+\frac{ir}{2}\right)q^{\prime}+\left(\Omega+\frac{i}{p-1}\right)q=r^{\alpha}\left[\Omega+\frac{i}{p-1}+\frac{i\alpha}{2}+\frac{\alpha(\alpha+d-2)}{r^{2}}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Thus the leading coefficient vanishes precisely when <math id="S2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=-\frac{2}{p-1}+2i\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=-\frac{2}{p-1}+2i\Omega</annotation></semantics></math>. This balance is consistent with the nonlinear equation. Thus <math id="S2.p3.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="q(r)=C_{s}r^{-2/(p-1)+2i\Omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(r)=C_{s}r^{-2/(p-1)+2i\Omega}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the nonlinearity becomes</p>
<table id="S2.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|q|^{p-1}q=|C_{s}|^{p-1}r^{-2}q." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|q|^{p-1}q=|C_{s}|^{p-1}r^{-2}q.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p3.4" class="ltx_p">Both the radial Laplacian and the nonlinearity are therefore of order <math id="S2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{-2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{-2}</annotation></semantics></math> relative to <math id="S2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The second behavior includes a quadratic phase oscillatory factor. Substituting <math id="S2.p4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="q(r)=e^{-ir^{2}/4}r^{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi><mi>r</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>β</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(r)=e^{-ir^{2}/4}r^{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>, for which</p>
<table id="S2.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{q^{\prime}}{q}=-\frac{ir}{2}+\frac{\beta}{r},\qquad\frac{q^{\prime\prime}}{q}=-\frac{r^{2}}{4}-i\left(\beta+\frac{1}{2}\right)+\frac{\beta(\beta-1)}{r^{2}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>q</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>β</mi><mi>r</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mi>q</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{q^{\prime}}{q}=-\frac{ir}{2}+\frac{\beta}{r},\qquad\frac{q^{\prime\prime}}{q}=-\frac{r^{2}}{4}-i\left(\beta+\frac{1}{2}\right)+\frac{\beta(\beta-1)}{r^{2}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p4.2" class="ltx_p">gives</p>
<table id="S2.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{\prime\prime}+\left(\frac{d-1}{r}+\frac{ir}{2}\right)q^{\prime}+\left(\Omega+\frac{i}{p-1}\right)q=q\left[\Omega+i\left(\frac{1}{p-1}-\frac{d}{2}-\frac{\beta}{2}\right)+\frac{\beta(\beta+d-2)}{r^{2}}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>r</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{\prime\prime}+\left(\frac{d-1}{r}+\frac{ir}{2}\right)q^{\prime}+\left(\Omega+\frac{i}{p-1}\right)q=q\left[\Omega+i\left(\frac{1}{p-1}-\frac{d}{2}-\frac{\beta}{2}\right)+\frac{\beta(\beta+d-2)}{r^{2}}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p4.3" class="ltx_p">The terms of order <math id="S2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{2}q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{2}q</annotation></semantics></math> cancel, and the remaining leading coefficient vanishes when <math id="S2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=-d+\frac{2}{p-1}-2i\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=-d+\frac{2}{p-1}-2i\Omega</annotation></semantics></math>. For this ansatz, <math id="S2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|q|^{p-1}=r^{(-d+2/(p-1))(p-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|q|^{p-1}=r^{(-d+2/(p-1))(p-1)}</annotation></semantics></math>, so the nonlinearity is again lower order. The formal balances yield the following tail modes, which we refer to as slow and fast modes according to their leading terms,</p>
<table id="S2.Ex16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex16X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex16X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Q_{\mathrm{slow}}(r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>slow</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q_{\mathrm{slow}}(r)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex16X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sim C_{s}r^{-\frac{2}{p-1}+2i\Omega}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sim C_{s}r^{-\frac{2}{p-1}+2i\Omega},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex16Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex16Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Q_{\mathrm{fast}}(r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>fast</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q_{\mathrm{fast}}(r)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex16Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sim C_{f}e^{-\frac{ir^{2}}{4}}r^{-d+\frac{2}{p-1}-2i\Omega}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sim C_{f}e^{-\frac{ir^{2}}{4}}r^{-d+\frac{2}{p-1}-2i\Omega}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The fast oscillation limits derivative integrability. For a nonzero fast mode and an integer <math id="S2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, formally differentiating its asymptotic expansion gives</p>
<table id="S2.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d^{j}}{dr^{j}}Q_{\mathrm{fast}}(r)=C_{f}\left(-\frac{i}{2}\right)^{j}e^{-\frac{ir^{2}}{4}}r^{-d+\frac{2}{p-1}-2i\Omega+j}\left(1+O(r^{-2})\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>d</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>fast</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d^{j}}{dr^{j}}Q_{\mathrm{fast}}(r)=C_{f}\left(-\frac{i}{2}\right)^{j}e^{-\frac{ir^{2}}{4}}r^{-d+\frac{2}{p-1}-2i\Omega+j}\left(1+O(r^{-2})\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p5.2" class="ltx_p">Their squared integrability at infinity is equivalent to convergence of</p>
<table id="S2.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{1}^{\infty}r^{2(-d+\frac{2}{p-1}+j)}r^{d-1}\,dr=\int_{1}^{\infty}r^{2j-d-1+\frac{4}{p-1}}\,dr." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{1}^{\infty}r^{2(-d+\frac{2}{p-1}+j)}r^{d-1}\,dr=\int_{1}^{\infty}r^{2j-d-1+\frac{4}{p-1}}\,dr.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p5.3" class="ltx_p">This integral converges exactly when <math id="S2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j&lt;d/2-2/(p-1)=s_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j&lt;d/2-2/(p-1)=s_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus a nonzero fast mode has derivatives not in <math id="S2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> at every integer order <math id="S2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j&gt;s_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j&gt;s_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>. Derivatives of the slow mode instead decay like <math id="S2.p5.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="r^{-2/(p-1)-j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{-2/(p-1)-j}</annotation></semantics></math> and are square-integrable exactly when <math id="S2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j&gt;s_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j&gt;s_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence the slow mode cannot cancel the failure of integrability of the fast mode. However, the nonzero slow tail is not in <math id="S2.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, nor are its first derivatives in <math id="S2.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Our approach is to remove the fast mode and then localize the slow mode to obtain initial data in every <math id="S2.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>H</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">This section focuses on the construction of a profile satisfying</p>
<table id="S2.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{f}=0,\qquad C_{s}\neq 0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{f}=0,\qquad C_{s}\neq 0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p6.2" class="ltx_p">while the localization of the profile will be studied in Section <a href="#S4" title="4. Self-similar blow-up ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p7.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="S2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{A,\Omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{A,\Omega}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the unique maximal regular solution of (<a href="#S2.E8" title="In 2. Self-similar profile equation ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>)–(<a href="#S2.E9" title="In 2. Self-similar profile equation ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>). Note that equation (<a href="#S2.E8" title="In 2. Self-similar profile equation ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>) is singular at the origin. The following argument shows that this equation defines a unique smooth radial solution starting at the origin, and that this solution cannot vanish while it exists. This will be used later for the construction matching an interior solution to a slow tail at infinity.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmthm1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmthm1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 2.1</span></span><span id="S2.Thmthm1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmthm1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmthm1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.Thmthm1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For each <math id="S2.Thmthm1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.Thmthm1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, the profile problem has a
unique maximal smooth radial solution <math id="S2.Thmthm1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{A,\Omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{A,\Omega}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S2.Thmthm1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,R_{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,R_{*})</annotation></semantics></math>.
It never vanishes, and if <math id="S2.Thmthm1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{*}&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{*}&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, then
<math id="S2.Thmthm1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{r&lt;R_{*}}|Q_{A,\Omega}(r)|=\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>sup</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{r&lt;R_{*}}|Q_{A,\Omega}(r)|=\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.
The solution depends continuously on <math id="S2.Thmthm1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(A,\Omega)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(A,\Omega)</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S2.Thmthm1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> on
compact intervals of existence.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Multiplication of (<a href="#S2.E8" title="In 2. Self-similar profile equation ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>) by an integrating factor <math id="S2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{d-1}e^{ir^{2}/4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{d-1}e^{ir^{2}/4}</annotation></semantics></math> gives</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigl(r^{d-1}e^{\frac{ir^{2}}{4}}Q^{\prime}(r)\bigr)^{\prime}=r^{d-1}e^{\frac{ir^{2}}{4}}\left(N(Q(r))-\left(\Omega+\frac{i}{p-1}\right)Q(r)\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl(r^{d-1}e^{\frac{ir^{2}}{4}}Q^{\prime}(r)\bigr)^{\prime}=r^{d-1}e^{\frac{ir^{2}}{4}}\left(N(Q(r))-\left(\Omega+\frac{i}{p-1}\right)Q(r)\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">For a regular solution, the expression inside the derivative tends to zero at the origin. Integration therefore yields</span></p>
<table id="S2.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(10)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\prime}(r)=r^{1-d}e^{-\frac{ir^{2}}{4}}\int_{0}^{r}\sigma^{d-1}e^{\frac{i\sigma^{2}}{4}}\left(N(Q(\sigma))-\left(\Omega+\frac{i}{p-1}\right)Q(\sigma)\right)\,d\sigma." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\prime}(r)=r^{1-d}e^{-\frac{ir^{2}}{4}}\int_{0}^{r}\sigma^{d-1}e^{\frac{i\sigma^{2}}{4}}\left(N(Q(\sigma))-\left(\Omega+\frac{i}{p-1}\right)Q(\sigma)\right)\,d\sigma.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">We construct a solution by integrating this identity once more and a fixed point argument. For <math id="S2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, consider the closed ball <math id="S2.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{R}=\{q\in C([0,R];\mathbb{C}):\|q-A\|_{\infty}\leq 1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>ℂ</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{R}=\{q\in C([0,R];\mathbb{C}):\|q-A\|_{\infty}\leq 1\}</annotation></semantics></math> and the map</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{T}q)(r)=A+\int_{0}^{r}t^{1-d}e^{-\frac{it^{2}}{4}}\int_{0}^{t}\sigma^{d-1}e^{\frac{i\sigma^{2}}{4}}\left(N(q(\sigma))-\left(\Omega+\frac{i}{p-1}\right)q(\sigma)\right)\,d\sigma\,dt." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{T}q)(r)=A+\int_{0}^{r}t^{1-d}e^{-\frac{it^{2}}{4}}\int_{0}^{t}\sigma^{d-1}e^{\frac{i\sigma^{2}}{4}}\left(N(q(\sigma))-\left(\Omega+\frac{i}{p-1}\right)q(\sigma)\right)\,d\sigma\,dt.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p8.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p8.4.1" class="ltx_text">The integrand in the outer integral extends continuously to zero. Since <math id="S2.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> is polynomial in the real and imaginary parts, there are constants <math id="S2.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M,L&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M,L&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that, whenever <math id="S2.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|z-A|,|w-A|\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|z-A|,|w-A|\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|N(z)-\left(\Omega+\frac{i}{p-1}\right)z\right|\leq M,\qquad\left|N(z)-N(w)-\left(\Omega+\frac{i}{p-1}\right)(z-w)\right|\leq L|z-w|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|N(z)-\left(\Omega+\frac{i}{p-1}\right)z\right|\leq M,\qquad\left|N(z)-N(w)-\left(\Omega+\frac{i}{p-1}\right)(z-w)\right|\leq L|z-w|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p8.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p8.5.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="S2.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\in\mathcal{B}_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\in\mathcal{B}_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq r\leq R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq r\leq R</annotation></semantics></math>, the exponential factors have modulus one, so</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex23X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex23X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|(\mathcal{T}q)(r)-A|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|(\mathcal{T}q)(r)-A|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex23X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\int_{0}^{r}t^{1-d}\int_{0}^{t}\sigma^{d-1}\left|N(q(\sigma))-\left(\Omega+\frac{i}{p-1}\right)q(\sigma)\right|\,d\sigma\,dt" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\int_{0}^{r}t^{1-d}\int_{0}^{t}\sigma^{d-1}\left|N(q(\sigma))-\left(\Omega+\frac{i}{p-1}\right)q(\sigma)\right|\,d\sigma\,dt</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex23Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex23Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq M\int_{0}^{r}t^{1-d}\left(\int_{0}^{t}\sigma^{d-1}\,d\sigma\right)dt=\frac{M}{d}\int_{0}^{r}t\,dt=\frac{Mr^{2}}{2d}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">d</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">d</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>M</mi><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">d</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq M\int_{0}^{r}t^{1-d}\left(\int_{0}^{t}\sigma^{d-1}\,d\sigma\right)dt=\frac{M}{d}\int_{0}^{r}t\,dt=\frac{Mr^{2}}{2d}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p8.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p8.6.1" class="ltx_text">Similarly, for <math id="S2.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q,\widetilde{q}\in\mathcal{B}_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q,\widetilde{q}\in\mathcal{B}_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex24X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex24X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|(\mathcal{T}q)(r)-(\mathcal{T}\widetilde{q})(r)|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|(\mathcal{T}q)(r)-(\mathcal{T}\widetilde{q})(r)|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex24Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex24Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\int_{0}^{r}t^{1-d}\int_{0}^{t}\sigma^{d-1}\bigl|N(q(\sigma))-N(\widetilde{q}(\sigma))-\left(\Omega+\frac{i}{p-1}\right)(q(\sigma)-\widetilde{q}(\sigma))\bigr|\,d\sigma\,dt" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="2.278em">≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\int_{0}^{r}t^{1-d}\int_{0}^{t}\sigma^{d-1}\bigl|N(q(\sigma))-N(\widetilde{q}(\sigma))-\left(\Omega+\frac{i}{p-1}\right)(q(\sigma)-\widetilde{q}(\sigma))\bigr|\,d\sigma\,dt</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex24Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex24Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq L\int_{0}^{r}t^{1-d}\int_{0}^{t}\sigma^{d-1}|q(\sigma)-\widetilde{q}(\sigma)|\,d\sigma\,dt=\frac{Lr^{2}}{2d}\|q-\widetilde{q}\|_{\infty}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="2.278em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><msup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">d</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq L\int_{0}^{r}t^{1-d}\int_{0}^{t}\sigma^{d-1}|q(\sigma)-\widetilde{q}(\sigma)|\,d\sigma\,dt=\frac{Lr^{2}}{2d}\|q-\widetilde{q}\|_{\infty}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p8.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p8.7.1" class="ltx_text">Taking the supremum over <math id="S2.p8.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\in[0,R]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\in[0,R]</annotation></semantics></math> gives</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathcal{T}q-A\|_{\infty}\leq\frac{MR^{2}}{2d},\qquad\|\mathcal{T}q-\mathcal{T}\widetilde{q}\|_{\infty}\leq\frac{LR^{2}}{2d}\|q-\widetilde{q}\|_{\infty}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathcal{T}q-A\|_{\infty}\leq\frac{MR^{2}}{2d},\qquad\|\mathcal{T}q-\mathcal{T}\widetilde{q}\|_{\infty}\leq\frac{LR^{2}}{2d}\|q-\widetilde{q}\|_{\infty}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p8.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p8.8.1" class="ltx_text">Choose <math id="S2.p8.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> so that <math id="S2.p8.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="MR^{2}/(2d)\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">MR^{2}/(2d)\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.p8.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="LR^{2}/(2d)&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">LR^{2}/(2d)&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>. The contraction mapping theorem gives a unique fixed point. It satisfies (<a href="#S2.E10" title="In Proof. ‣ 2. Self-similar profile equation ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>), with <math id="S2.p8.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|Q^{\prime}(r)|\leq Mr/d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|Q^{\prime}(r)|\leq Mr/d</annotation></semantics></math>, and hence is <math id="S2.p8.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> up to zero with <math id="S2.p8.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(0)=A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(0)=A</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.p8.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\prime}(0)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\prime}(0)=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Differentiating the integral formula for <math id="S2.p8.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> shows that it solves the profile equation there. Every regular solution with these initial data lies in <math id="S2.p8.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> on a sufficiently short interval and satisfies the same fixed-point equation. This proves local uniqueness.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">To verify smoothness at the origin, substitute <math id="S2.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma=r\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma=r\theta</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#S2.E10" title="In Proof. ‣ 2. Self-similar profile equation ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>):</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\prime}(r)=r\int_{0}^{1}\theta^{d-1}e^{\frac{ir^{2}(\theta^{2}-1)}{4}}\left(N(Q(r\theta))-\left(\Omega+\frac{i}{p-1}\right)Q(r\theta)\right)\,d\theta." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\prime}(r)=r\int_{0}^{1}\theta^{d-1}e^{\frac{ir^{2}(\theta^{2}-1)}{4}}\left(N(Q(r\theta))-\left(\Omega+\frac{i}{p-1}\right)Q(r\theta)\right)\,d\theta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">The even extension <math id="S2.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(-r)=Q(r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(-r)=Q(r)</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S2.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, since <math id="S2.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\prime}(0)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\prime}(0)=0</annotation></semantics></math>, and satisfies this identity for negative <math id="S2.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> as well. If this extension is <math id="S2.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, differentiation under the integral on the fixed interval <math id="S2.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> shows that the right-hand side is <math id="S2.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{j}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus <math id="S2.p9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S2.p9.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{j+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{j+1}</annotation></semantics></math>, and induction proves smoothness and evenness. A smooth even function of <math id="S2.p9.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> defines a smooth radial function of <math id="S2.p9.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Away from zero the equation is a smooth first-order system for <math id="S2.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Q,Q^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Q,Q^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>, so local uniqueness gives a unique maximal continuation on <math id="S2.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,R_{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,R_{*})</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="S2.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{*}&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{*}&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded there, then <math id="S2.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N(Q)-\left(\Omega+\frac{i}{p-1}\right)Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N(Q)-\left(\Omega+\frac{i}{p-1}\right)Q</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded and (<a href="#S2.E10" title="In Proof. ‣ 2. Self-similar profile equation ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>) bounds <math id="S2.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S2.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,R_{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,R_{*})</annotation></semantics></math>. The differential equation then bounds <math id="S2.p10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\prime\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\prime\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S2.p10.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[R_{*}/2,R_{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[R_{*}/2,R_{*})</annotation></semantics></math>. Consequently <math id="S2.p10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.p10.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> have finite limits at <math id="S2.p10.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, and local existence for the first-order system extends the solution past <math id="S2.p10.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{*}</annotation></semantics></math>. This contradiction proves the continuation criterion. The contraction construction also gives continuous dependence on the parameters.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, set <math id="S2.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=|Q|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=|Q|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J=2\operatorname{Im}(\overline{Q}Q^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J=2\operatorname{Im}(\overline{Q}Q^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>. Taking twice the imaginary part of (<a href="#S2.E8" title="In 2. Self-similar profile equation ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>) multiplied by <math id="S2.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{Q}</annotation></semantics></math> gives, for <math id="S2.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J^{\prime}+\frac{d-1}{r}J+\frac{2}{p-1}\rho+\frac{r}{2}\rho^{\prime}=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>J</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>r</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J^{\prime}+\frac{d-1}{r}J+\frac{2}{p-1}\rho+\frac{r}{2}\rho^{\prime}=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p11.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p11.2.1" class="ltx_text">Here the nonlinear term and <math id="S2.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega|Q|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega|Q|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> are real, and <math id="S2.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho^{\prime}=2\operatorname{Re}(\overline{Q}Q^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho^{\prime}=2\operatorname{Re}(\overline{Q}Q^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>. It follows that</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d}{dr}\left[r^{d-1}\left(J+\frac{r}{2}\rho\right)\right]=s_{c}r^{d-1}\rho." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d}{dr}\left[r^{d-1}\left(J+\frac{r}{2}\rho\right)\right]=s_{c}r^{d-1}\rho.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p11.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p11.3.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="S2.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded and <math id="S2.p11.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\prime}(r)=O(r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\prime}(r)=O(r)</annotation></semantics></math> at zero, the expression in brackets tends to zero there. Integration yields</span></p>
<table id="S2.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(11)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{d-1}\left(2\operatorname{Im}(\overline{Q}Q^{\prime})+\frac{r}{2}|Q|^{2}\right)=s_{c}\int_{0}^{r}\sigma^{d-1}|Q(\sigma)|^{2}\,d\sigma." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{d-1}\left(2\operatorname{Im}(\overline{Q}Q^{\prime})+\frac{r}{2}|Q|^{2}\right)=s_{c}\int_{0}^{r}\sigma^{d-1}|Q(\sigma)|^{2}\,d\sigma.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p11.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p11.4.1" class="ltx_text">Because <math id="S2.p11.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{c}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{c}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.p11.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(0)=A&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(0)=A&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, continuity makes the right-hand side strictly positive for every <math id="S2.p11.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\in(0,R_{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\in(0,R_{*})</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="S2.p11.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(r)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(r)=0</annotation></semantics></math>, the left-hand side would vanish. Hence <math id="S2.p11.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> has no zeros on <math id="S2.p11.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,R_{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,R_{*})</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="S2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.1. </span>Linear exterior modes</h3>

<div id="S2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The linear part of the radial profile equation (<a href="#S2.E8" title="In 2. Self-similar profile equation ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>) is</p>
<table id="S2.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(12)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\Omega}q=q^{\prime\prime}+\left(\frac{d-1}{r}+\frac{ir}{2}\right)q^{\prime}+\left(\Omega+\frac{i}{p-1}\right)q,\qquad r&gt;0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>r</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\Omega}q=q^{\prime\prime}+\left(\frac{d-1}{r}+\frac{ir}{2}\right)q^{\prime}+\left(\Omega+\frac{i}{p-1}\right)q,\qquad r&gt;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Set</p>
<table id="S2.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(13)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu=\frac{1}{p-1}-i\Omega,\quad\kappa=\frac{d}{2}-\mu," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu=\frac{1}{p-1}-i\Omega,\quad\kappa=\frac{d}{2}-\mu,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">so that <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega+\frac{i}{p-1}=i\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega+\frac{i}{p-1}=i\mu</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Re}\mu=\frac{1}{p-1}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Re}\mu=\frac{1}{p-1}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Re}\kappa=\frac{d}{2}-\frac{1}{p-1}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Re}\kappa=\frac{d}{2}-\frac{1}{p-1}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. The following lemma constructs a fundamental system of solutions of the linear equation <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\Omega}q=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\Omega}q=0</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(0,\infty)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(0,\infty)</annotation></semantics></math>, with the previously stated asymptotics at infinity.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmthm2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmthm2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 2.2</span></span><span id="S2.Thmthm2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmthm2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmthm2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.Thmthm2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The equation <math id="S2.Thmthm2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\Omega}q=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\Omega}q=0</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S2.Thmthm2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(0,\infty)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(0,\infty)</annotation></semantics></math> has solutions given by</span></p>
<table id="S2.E14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S2.E14X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_left">(14)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E14X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle S_{\Omega}(r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle S_{\Omega}(r)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E14X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{4^{-\mu}}{\Gamma(\mu)}\int_{0}^{\infty}e^{-\frac{r^{2}t}{4}}t^{\mu-1}(1+it)^{\frac{d}{2}-1-\mu}\,dt," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mn>4</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></msup><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">d</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{4^{-\mu}}{\Gamma(\mu)}\int_{0}^{\infty}e^{-\frac{r^{2}t}{4}}t^{\mu-1}(1+it)^{\frac{d}{2}-1-\mu}\,dt,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.E14Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E14Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle F_{\Omega}(r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle F_{\Omega}(r)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E14Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{4^{-\kappa}e^{-\frac{ir^{2}}{4}}}{\Gamma(\kappa)}\int_{0}^{\infty}e^{-\frac{r^{2}t}{4}}t^{\kappa-1}(1-it)^{\frac{d}{2}-1-\kappa}\,dt." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mn>4</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">d</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{4^{-\kappa}e^{-\frac{ir^{2}}{4}}}{\Gamma(\kappa)}\int_{0}^{\infty}e^{-\frac{r^{2}t}{4}}t^{\kappa-1}(1-it)^{\frac{d}{2}-1-\kappa}\,dt.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.Thmthm2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.Thmthm2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Both integrals converge absolutely for every <math id="S2.Thmthm2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">The change of variables <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=r^{2}/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=r^{2}/4</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(r)=g_{\mu}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(r)=g_{\mu}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>, transforms <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\Omega}q=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\Omega}q=0</annotation></semantics></math> into</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="xg_{\mu}^{\prime\prime}+(d/2+ix)g_{\mu}^{\prime}+i\mu g_{\mu}=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>μ</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>μ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">xg_{\mu}^{\prime\prime}+(d/2+ix)g_{\mu}^{\prime}+i\mu g_{\mu}=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">To exploit the affine dependence of the coefficients on <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>, seek a Laplace integral representation</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\mu}(x)=\int_{0}^{\infty}e^{-xt}h_{\mu}(t)\,dt." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\mu}(x)=\int_{0}^{\infty}e^{-xt}h_{\mu}(t)\,dt.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS1.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting this ansatz and integrating the terms containing <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> by parts formally gives</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="xg_{\mu}^{\prime\prime}+(d/2+ix)g_{\mu}^{\prime}+i\mu g_{\mu}=\int_{0}^{\infty}e^{-xt}\bigl(t(t-i)h_{\mu}^{\prime}+\bigl((2-d/2)t+i(\mu-1)\bigr)h_{\mu}\bigr)\,dt," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>μ</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>μ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>μ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">xg_{\mu}^{\prime\prime}+(d/2+ix)g_{\mu}^{\prime}+i\mu g_{\mu}=\int_{0}^{\infty}e^{-xt}\bigl(t(t-i)h_{\mu}^{\prime}+\bigl((2-d/2)t+i(\mu-1)\bigr)h_{\mu}\bigr)\,dt,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS1.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">provided the boundary term <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[e^{-xt}t(t-i)h_{\mu}(t)]_{0}^{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[e^{-xt}t(t-i)h_{\mu}(t)]_{0}^{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> vanishes. Thus it suffices to solve the first-order equation</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t(t-i)h_{\mu}^{\prime}+\bigl((2-d/2)t+i(\mu-1)\bigr)h_{\mu}=0,\quad\text{equivalently}\quad\frac{h_{\mu}^{\prime}}{h_{\mu}}=\frac{\mu-1}{t}+\frac{i(d/2-1-\mu)}{1+it}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>μ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext>equivalently</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mfrac><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>μ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t(t-i)h_{\mu}^{\prime}+\bigl((2-d/2)t+i(\mu-1)\bigr)h_{\mu}=0,\quad\text{equivalently}\quad\frac{h_{\mu}^{\prime}}{h_{\mu}}=\frac{\mu-1}{t}+\frac{i(d/2-1-\mu)}{1+it}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.p2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS1.p2.5.1" class="ltx_text">Integration yields, up to a multiplicative constant,</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\mu}(t)=t^{\mu-1}(1+it)^{\frac{d}{2}-1-\mu}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\mu}(t)=t^{\mu-1}(1+it)^{\frac{d}{2}-1-\mu}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.p2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS1.p2.6.1" class="ltx_text">This function is <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(t^{1/(p-1)-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(t^{1/(p-1)-1})</annotation></semantics></math> at zero and <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(t^{d/2-2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(t^{d/2-2})</annotation></semantics></math> at infinity. Consequently its Laplace integral converges absolutely for <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, can be differentiated under the integral sign to every order, and has the required vanishing boundary term. The preceding calculation is therefore justified. Multiplication by <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4^{-\mu}/\Gamma(\mu)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mn>4</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4^{-\mu}/\Gamma(\mu)</annotation></semantics></math> gives the stated formula for <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\Omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\Omega}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">To obtain the second solution, extract the quadratic oscillatory factor by seeking <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(r)=e^{-ix}g_{\mu}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(r)=e^{-ix}g_{\mu}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>, again with <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=r^{2}/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=r^{2}/4</annotation></semantics></math>. Direct substitution gives</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\Omega}q=e^{-ix}\bigl(xg_{\mu}^{\prime\prime}+(d/2-ix)g_{\mu}^{\prime}-i\kappa g_{\mu}\bigr)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>μ</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>μ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\Omega}q=e^{-ix}\bigl(xg_{\mu}^{\prime\prime}+(d/2-ix)g_{\mu}^{\prime}-i\kappa g_{\mu}\bigr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">since <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu+\kappa=d/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu+\kappa=d/2</annotation></semantics></math>. The equation in parentheses is the preceding transformed equation with <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> replaced by <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-i</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>. The same Laplace integral construction therefore gives the function <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{\kappa-1}(1-it)^{d/2-1-\kappa}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{\kappa-1}(1-it)^{d/2-1-\kappa}</annotation></semantics></math>. It is integrable at zero because <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Re}\kappa&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Re}\kappa&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and has polynomial growth at infinity, so the same convergence and integration-by-parts arguments apply. Multiplication by <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4^{-\kappa}/\Gamma(\kappa)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mn>4</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4^{-\kappa}/\Gamma(\kappa)</annotation></semantics></math> and restoration of the factor <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{-ix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{-ix}</annotation></semantics></math> yield <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{\Omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{\Omega}</annotation></semantics></math>. These representations are consistent with the standard confluent hypergeometric integral formulas; see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib57" title="" class="ltx_ref">57</a>, Sections 13.2 and 13.4]</cite>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Changing variables <math id="S2.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\mapsto 4t/r^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\mapsto 4t/r^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> gives</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex35" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex35X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex35X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle S_{\Omega}(r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle S_{\Omega}(r)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex35X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=r^{-2\mu}\left(1+\frac{4i\mu(d/2-1-\mu)}{r^{2}}+O_{\Omega}(r^{-4})\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=r^{-2\mu}\left(1+\frac{4i\mu(d/2-1-\mu)}{r^{2}}+O_{\Omega}(r^{-4})\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex35Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex35Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle F_{\Omega}(r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle F_{\Omega}(r)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex35Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=e^{-\frac{ir^{2}}{4}}r^{-2\kappa}\left(1+O_{\Omega}(r^{-2})\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=e^{-\frac{ir^{2}}{4}}r^{-2\kappa}\left(1+O_{\Omega}(r^{-2})\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">The same rescaling applied to the differentiated integrals justifies differentiation of these asymptotic expansions. Abel’s identity and the leading asymptotics then give</span></p>
<table id="S2.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(15)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{\Omega}=S_{\Omega}F_{\Omega}^{\prime}-S_{\Omega}^{\prime}F_{\Omega}=-\frac{i}{2}r^{1-d}e^{-\frac{ir^{2}}{4}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{\Omega}=S_{\Omega}F_{\Omega}^{\prime}-S_{\Omega}^{\prime}F_{\Omega}=-\frac{i}{2}r^{1-d}e^{-\frac{ir^{2}}{4}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS1.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">Thus <math id="S2.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{\Omega}(r)\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{\Omega}(r)\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math> for every <math id="S2.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, proving that <math id="S2.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\Omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\Omega}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{\Omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{\Omega}</annotation></semantics></math> form a fundamental system.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">For a nonlinear profile with a nonzero slow tail, <math id="S2.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the leading slow coefficient. We define the fast coefficient <math id="S2.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{f}</annotation></semantics></math> by requiring that there exist constants <math id="S2.SS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{1},c_{2}\in\mathbb{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℂ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{1},c_{2}\in\mathbb{C}</annotation></semantics></math> with</p>
<table id="S2.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(16)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(r)=C_{s}r^{\beta}\bigl(1+c_{1}r^{-2}+c_{2}r^{-4}\bigr)+C_{f}F_{\Omega}(r)+o(r^{-d+\frac{2}{p-1}}),\qquad\beta=-\frac{2}{p-1}+2i\Omega." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(r)=C_{s}r^{\beta}\bigl(1+c_{1}r^{-2}+c_{2}r^{-4}\bigr)+C_{f}F_{\Omega}(r)+o(r^{-d+\frac{2}{p-1}}),\qquad\beta=-\frac{2}{p-1}+2i\Omega.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.p5.2" class="ltx_p">Note that here <math id="S2.SS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{\Omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{\Omega}</annotation></semantics></math> carries the factor <math id="S2.SS1.p5.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="e^{-ir^{2}/4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi><mi>r</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{-ir^{2}/4}</annotation></semantics></math>. Comparing the distinct decay rates in (<a href="#S2.E16" title="In 2.1. Linear exterior modes ‣ 2. Self-similar profile equation ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>) determines <math id="S2.SS1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS1.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{f}</annotation></semantics></math> uniquely. For our parameter pairs, <math id="S2.SS1.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4/(p-1)&lt;d&lt;6+4/(p-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4/(p-1)&lt;d&lt;6+4/(p-1)</annotation></semantics></math>, so the fast mode decays faster than the leading slow mode, while <math id="S2.SS1.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{\operatorname{Re}\beta-6}=o(r^{-d+2/(p-1)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{\operatorname{Re}\beta-6}=o(r^{-d+2/(p-1)})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">The exterior construction below proves this expansion with <math id="S2.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{f}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{f}=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Considering subsequent nonlinear slow terms is necessary in this definition since, in the case of <math id="S2.SS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(d,p)=(5,7)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(d,p)=(5,7)</annotation></semantics></math>, the first term of <math id="S2.SS1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{\Omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{\Omega}</annotation></semantics></math> is of order <math id="S2.SS1.p6.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="O(r^{-14/3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>14</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(r^{-14/3})</annotation></semantics></math>, while the first two nonlinear slow terms are of orders <math id="S2.SS1.p6.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="O(r^{\beta-2})=O(r^{-7/3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(r^{\beta-2})=O(r^{-7/3})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS1.p6.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="O(r^{\beta-4})=O(r^{-13/3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>13</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(r^{\beta-4})=O(r^{-13/3})</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">3. </span>Construction of the self-similar profile</h2>

<div id="S3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To construct a profile with <math id="S3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{f}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{f}=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{s}\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{s}\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, we first construct the slow exterior solution and obtain rigorous bounds on its value and derivative at a finite radius. We then match it to the regular-origin solution by Brouwer’s fixed-point theorem. All statements established by computation are collected in Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmthm10" title="Lemma 3.10 (Computer-assisted bounds). ‣ 3.4. Computer-assisted proof of the matching conditions ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.10</span></a>. The code is available in the supplementary material and at <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>]</cite>. The estimates that justify the computation are proved below.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The computer-assisted shooting and matching strategy used in this subsection is inspired by the work in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">26</a>]</cite>. As in their construction, we build solutions satisfying the prescribed conditions at the origin and at infinity and certify that they match at an intermediate radius. Related computer-assisted constructions have appeared in many works, for example, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib72" title="" class="ltx_ref">72</a>, <a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">44</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Use the parameters</p>
<table id="S3.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vartheta=(A,\Omega,K),\qquad A&gt;0,\quad K&gt;0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ϑ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vartheta=(A,\Omega,K),\qquad A&gt;0,\quad K&gt;0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> is the value of the profile at the origin, <math id="S3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega</annotation></semantics></math> is the self-similar frequency, and <math id="S3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=|C_{s}|^{p-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=|C_{s}|^{p-1}</annotation></semantics></math> relates to the leading coefficient of the slow tail at infinity. We introduce the variable <math id="S3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> because it naturally enters the nonlinear expansion at infinity. Let <math id="S3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vartheta_{0}=(A_{0},\Omega_{0},K_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϑ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vartheta_{0}=(A_{0},\Omega_{0},K_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> be the parameters supplied by the computer-assisted code. These parameters were found using a shooting and continuation method to discover approximate solutions of the profile equation. They can be found in the accompanying code. Their approximate values are</p>
<table id="S3.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{array}[]{c|rrr}(d,p)&amp;A_{0}&amp;\Omega_{0}&amp;K_{0}\\
\hline\cr(3,27)&amp;0.0501485544258024&amp;-1.3966245573341954&amp;70.8930132091120\\
(4,9)&amp;0.0014126481622802&amp;-2.9442997039706108&amp;230.5787044287510\\
(5,7)&amp;0.0409508188010580&amp;-1.7226834479870780&amp;120.4293553317432\end{array}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_border_r"><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_border_t"></mtd><mtd class="ltx_border_t"></mtd><mtd class="ltx_border_t"></mtd><mtd class="ltx_border_t"></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_border_r"><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>27</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mn>0.0501485544258024</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1.3966245573341954</mn></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mn>70.8930132091120</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_border_r"><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>9</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mn>0.0014126481622802</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2.9442997039706108</mn></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mn>230.5787044287510</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_border_r"><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mn>0.0409508188010580</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1.7226834479870780</mn></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mn>120.4293553317432</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{array}[]{c|rrr}(d,p)&amp;A_{0}&amp;\Omega_{0}&amp;K_{0}\\
\hline\cr(3,27)&amp;0.0501485544258024&amp;-1.3966245573341954&amp;70.8930132091120\\
(4,9)&amp;0.0014126481622802&amp;-2.9442997039706108&amp;230.5787044287510\\
(5,7)&amp;0.0409508188010580&amp;-1.7226834479870780&amp;120.4293553317432\end{array}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Define the parameter cube</p>
<table id="S3.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(17)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=\{\vartheta\in\mathbb{R}^{3}:\|\vartheta-\vartheta_{0}\|_{\infty}\leq\rho\},\qquad\rho=\begin{cases}2^{-240},&amp;(d,p)=(3,27),\\
2^{-320},&amp;(d,p)=(4,9),\\
2^{-220},&amp;(d,p)=(5,7).\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>ϑ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>ϑ</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ϑ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>240</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>27</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>320</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>9</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>220</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=\{\vartheta\in\mathbb{R}^{3}:\|\vartheta-\vartheta_{0}\|_{\infty}\leq\rho\},\qquad\rho=\begin{cases}2^{-240},&amp;(d,p)=(3,27),\\
2^{-320},&amp;(d,p)=(4,9),\\
2^{-220},&amp;(d,p)=(5,7).\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p3.4" class="ltx_p">This small parameter cube is needed in the computer-assisted proof to control the propagation of the error bound. Our shooting method is extremely sensitive to the parameters, and the smallness of <math id="S3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>, together with the use of multiple-precision arithmetic, is necessary to obtain a rigorous enclosure of the solution. The next theorem shows that the parameters <math id="S3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(A_{0},\Omega_{0},K_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(A_{0},\Omega_{0},K_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> can be perturbed inside the parameter cube <math id="S3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> to yield a global regular profile with a slow tail at infinity.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmthm1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_thm">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmthm1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 3.1</span></span><span id="S3.Thmthm1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmthm1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmthm1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmthm1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There is a <math id="S3.Thmthm1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vartheta_{*}=(A_{*},\Omega_{*},K_{*})\in D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϑ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vartheta_{*}=(A_{*},\Omega_{*},K_{*})\in D</annotation></semantics></math> such that
the regular profile <math id="S3.Thmthm1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{A_{*},\Omega_{*}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{A_{*},\Omega_{*}}</annotation></semantics></math> is global and has</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{f}=0,\qquad|C_{s}|=K_{*}^{\frac{1}{p-1}}&gt;0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mo>∗</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{f}=0,\qquad|C_{s}|=K_{*}^{\frac{1}{p-1}}&gt;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.Thmthm1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmthm1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In particular, the profile is smooth, regular at the origin, and nonvanishing at every finite radius. At infinity it has a slow expansion to every algebraic order, as specified in Corollary <a href="#S3.Thmthm5" title="Corollary 3.5. ‣ 3.1. Exterior solution at infinity ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.5</span></a>, up to a constant unit phase.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">To construct this profile, we first build a finite slow-tail expansion and bound its residual. Next, using the two linear modes at infinity, we construct a right inverse whose corrections have zero limiting modal coefficients, and use it to obtain an exact exterior solution with <math id="S3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{s}=K^{1/(p-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{s}=K^{1/(p-1)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{f}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{f}=0</annotation></semantics></math>. The exterior construction is then shown to have a full slow expansion and to depend continuously on the parameters.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">We then construct a finite Taylor approximation at the origin and use a contraction argument for the integral equation to enclose the exact regular solution starting from the origin and its initial data. We then define the exact and finite three-component matching maps; a zero of the exact map joins the inner and outer solutions up to a constant unit phase. Finally, flow estimates propagate the finite inner and outer enclosures, the computer-assisted verification checks the resulting boundary, propagation, nonvanishing, and matching bounds, and the Brouwer fixed point theorem yields the required matching zero.</p>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.1. </span>Exterior solution at infinity</h3>

<div id="S3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We now start by constructing a finite approximation to the slow exterior solution for the whole nonlinear equation. The leading slow asymptotic mode of the linear exterior equation <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\Omega}q=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\Omega}q=0</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{1/(p-1)}r^{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>β</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{1/(p-1)}r^{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\beta=-2/(p-1)+2i\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=-2/(p-1)+2i\Omega</annotation></semantics></math>. We correct this mode by a finite expansion in inverse even powers of <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>, chosen so that the first <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math> orders of the nonlinear profile equation cancel. For <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, define</p>
<table id="S3.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(18)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)}(r)=K^{\frac{1}{p-1}}r^{\beta}e^{\Phi_{J}(r^{-2})},\quad\Phi_{J}(t)=\sum_{n=1}^{J}\ell_{n}t^{n}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>J</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)}(r)=K^{\frac{1}{p-1}}r^{\beta}e^{\Phi_{J}(r^{-2})},\quad\Phi_{J}(t)=\sum_{n=1}^{J}\ell_{n}t^{n}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To derive a recursive relation for the coefficients, write <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=r^{-2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=r^{-2}</annotation></semantics></math> and temporarily regard <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi(t)=\sum_{n\geq 1}\ell_{n}t^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi(t)=\sum_{n\geq 1}\ell_{n}t^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> as a formal power series. The logarithmic derivative of the corresponding formal ansatz with respect to <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log r</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="S3.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta-2t\Phi^{\prime}(t)=:F(t)=\sum_{n\geq 0}f_{n}t^{n}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta-2t\Phi^{\prime}(t)=:F(t)=\sum_{n\geq 0}f_{n}t^{n},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">and hence</p>
<table id="S3.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{0}=\beta,\qquad f_{n}=-2n\ell_{n},\qquad n\geq 1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{0}=\beta,\qquad f_{n}=-2n\ell_{n},\qquad n\geq 1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">We now define the two remaining series that enter after substitution:</p>
<table id="S3.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(19)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle e^{(p-1)\operatorname{Re}\Phi(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle e^{(p-1)\operatorname{Re}\Phi(t)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{n\geq 0}E_{n}t^{n}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{n\geq 0}E_{n}t^{n},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.E20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(20)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle F(t)^{2}+(d-2)F(t)-2tF^{\prime}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle F(t)^{2}+(d-2)F(t)-2tF^{\prime}(t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{n\geq 0}H_{n}t^{n}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{n\geq 0}H_{n}t^{n}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p2.4" class="ltx_p">Differentiating (<a href="#S3.E19" title="In 3.1. Exterior solution at infinity ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>) and comparing coefficients gives</p>
<table id="S3.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(21)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{0}=1,\qquad E_{n}=\frac{p-1}{n}\sum_{j=1}^{n}j\operatorname{Re}\ell_{j}\,E_{n-j},\qquad n\geq 1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{0}=1,\qquad E_{n}=\frac{p-1}{n}\sum_{j=1}^{n}j\operatorname{Re}\ell_{j}\,E_{n-j},\qquad n\geq 1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p2.5" class="ltx_p">Expanding (<a href="#S3.E20" title="In 3.1. Exterior solution at infinity ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>) gives directly</p>
<table id="S3.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{n}=\sum_{j=0}^{n}f_{j}f_{n-j}+(d-2-2n)f_{n},\qquad n\geq 0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{n}=\sum_{j=0}^{n}f_{j}f_{n-j}+(d-2-2n)f_{n},\qquad n\geq 0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p2.6" class="ltx_p">Finally, after division by the corresponding formal ansatz, equation (<a href="#S2.E8" title="In 2. Self-similar profile equation ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>) formally reads</p>
<table id="S3.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\left(\sum_{n\geq 0}(H_{n}-KE_{n})t^{n}-i\Phi^{\prime}(t)\right)=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\left(\sum_{n\geq 0}(H_{n}-KE_{n})t^{n}-i\Phi^{\prime}(t)\right)=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p2.7" class="ltx_p">Thus the coefficient of <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{n+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{n+1}</annotation></semantics></math> vanishes precisely when</p>
<table id="S3.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(22)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{n+1}=\frac{i}{n+1}(KE_{n}-H_{n}),\qquad n\geq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{n+1}=\frac{i}{n+1}(KE_{n}-H_{n}),\qquad n\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p2.8" class="ltx_p">In particular, the case <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=0</annotation></semantics></math> yields <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{1}=i\{K-\beta(\beta+d-2)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{1}=i\{K-\beta(\beta+d-2)\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thereafter, the coefficients are determined successively: once <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{1},\ldots,\ell_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{1},\ldots,\ell_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> are known, so are <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the last formula determines <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{n+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{n+1}</annotation></semantics></math>. The approximation (<a href="#S3.E18" title="In 3.1. Exterior solution at infinity ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>) retains the first <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math> coefficients of this formal expansion. The next part of the construction concerns the analysis of the residual of this finite approximation.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We next estimate the residual of <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[r_{\mathrm{out}},\infty)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[r_{\mathrm{out}},\infty)</annotation></semantics></math>. In the definitions above, we now take <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi=\Phi_{J}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi=\Phi_{J}</annotation></semantics></math> and hence regard <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> as polynomials. We set the rescaled variables</p>
<table id="S3.Ex43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="u=(r_{\mathrm{out}}/r)^{2},\qquad L_{n}=\ell_{n}r_{\mathrm{out}}^{-2n}\quad(1\leq n\leq J)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u=(r_{\mathrm{out}}/r)^{2},\qquad L_{n}=\ell_{n}r_{\mathrm{out}}^{-2n}\quad(1\leq n\leq J),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">and introduce the rescaled polynomials</p>
<table id="S3.Ex44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi_{r_{\mathrm{out}}}(u):=\Phi_{J}(r_{\mathrm{out}}^{-2}u)=\sum_{n=1}^{J}L_{n}u^{n},\qquad G(u):=H(r_{\mathrm{out}}^{-2}u)=\sum_{n=0}^{2J}G_{n}u^{n}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>J</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi_{r_{\mathrm{out}}}(u):=\Phi_{J}(r_{\mathrm{out}}^{-2}u)=\sum_{n=1}^{J}L_{n}u^{n},\qquad G(u):=H(r_{\mathrm{out}}^{-2}u)=\sum_{n=0}^{2J}G_{n}u^{n}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Thus the new variable satisfies <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq u\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq u\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi_{J}(r^{-2})=\Phi_{r_{\mathrm{out}}}(u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi_{J}(r^{-2})=\Phi_{r_{\mathrm{out}}}(u)</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{\nu,r_{\mathrm{out}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{\nu,r_{\mathrm{out}}}</annotation></semantics></math> be the space of continuous complex functions on <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[r_{\mathrm{out}},\infty)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[r_{\mathrm{out}},\infty)</annotation></semantics></math> with weighted norm</p>
<table id="S3.Ex45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|f\|_{\nu,r_{\mathrm{out}}}:=\sup_{r\geq r_{\mathrm{out}}}r^{\nu}|f(r)|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>ν</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|f\|_{\nu,r_{\mathrm{out}}}:=\sup_{r\geq r_{\mathrm{out}}}r^{\nu}|f(r)|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p3.4" class="ltx_p">The preceding coefficient recursions yield the following estimates. We need to have explicit constants in the bounds to use them in the computer-assisted proof.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmthm2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmthm2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3.2</span></span><span id="S3.Thmthm2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmthm2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmthm2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmthm2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Recall that <math id="S3.Thmthm2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N(q)=|q|^{p-1}q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N(q)=|q|^{p-1}q</annotation></semantics></math>. For any <math id="S3.Thmthm2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, define</span></p>
<table id="S3.E23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(23)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}=\sum_{n=J}^{2J}|G_{n}|+K\chi^{-J}\exp\left((p-1)\sum_{n=1}^{J}|\operatorname{Re}L_{n}|\chi^{n}\right),\qquad M=K^{\frac{1}{p-1}}\exp\left(\sum_{n=1}^{J}|\operatorname{Re}L_{n}|\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></munderover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>χ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>J</mi></munderover><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>χ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>J</mi></munderover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}=\sum_{n=J}^{2J}|G_{n}|+K\chi^{-J}\exp\left((p-1)\sum_{n=1}^{J}|\operatorname{Re}L_{n}|\chi^{n}\right),\qquad M=K^{\frac{1}{p-1}}\exp\left(\sum_{n=1}^{J}|\operatorname{Re}L_{n}|\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.Thmthm2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmthm2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then the residual of <math id="S3.Thmthm2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)}</annotation></semantics></math> is</span></p>
<table id="S3.E24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(24)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\Omega}P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)}-N(P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)})=P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)}(r)\left\{\frac{u}{r_{\mathrm{out}}^{2}}\left(G(u)-Ke^{(p-1)\operatorname{Re}\Phi_{r_{\mathrm{out}}}(u)}\right)-iu\Phi_{r_{\mathrm{out}}}^{\prime}(u)\right\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>u</mi><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\Omega}P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)}-N(P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)})=P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)}(r)\left\{\frac{u}{r_{\mathrm{out}}^{2}}\left(G(u)-Ke^{(p-1)\operatorname{Re}\Phi_{r_{\mathrm{out}}}(u)}\right)-iu\Phi_{r_{\mathrm{out}}}^{\prime}(u)\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.Thmthm2.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmthm2.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Moreover, for <math id="S3.Thmthm2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq u\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq u\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, we have the estimates</span></p>
<table id="S3.E25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S3.E25X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_left">(25)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E25X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left|\frac{u}{r_{\mathrm{out}}^{2}}\left(G(u)-Ke^{(p-1)\operatorname{Re}\Phi_{r_{\mathrm{out}}}(u)}\right)-iu\Phi_{r_{\mathrm{out}}}^{\prime}(u)\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>u</mi><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left|\frac{u}{r_{\mathrm{out}}^{2}}\left(G(u)-Ke^{(p-1)\operatorname{Re}\Phi_{r_{\mathrm{out}}}(u)}\right)-iu\Phi_{r_{\mathrm{out}}}^{\prime}(u)\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E25X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq r_{\mathrm{out}}^{-2}\mathcal{B}\,u^{J+1}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq r_{\mathrm{out}}^{-2}\mathcal{B}\,u^{J+1},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E25Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E25Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|L_{\Omega}P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)}-N(P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)})\|_{\nu,r_{\mathrm{out}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|L_{\Omega}P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)}-N(P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)})\|_{\nu,r_{\mathrm{out}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E25Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq Mr_{\mathrm{out}}^{2J}\mathcal{B},\qquad\nu=\frac{2}{p-1}+2J+2." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>M</mi><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>out</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>J</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq Mr_{\mathrm{out}}^{2J}\mathcal{B},\qquad\nu=\frac{2}{p-1}+2J+2.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Direct substitution of <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)}</annotation></semantics></math> into the profile equation, using the definitions of <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>, gives (<a href="#S3.E24" title="In Lemma 3.2. ‣ 3.1. Exterior solution at infinity ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a>). The coefficient recursions from above make every coefficient through degree <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math> of the expression in braces vanish.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Write</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{(p-1)\operatorname{Re}\Phi_{r_{\mathrm{out}}}(u)}=\sum_{m=0}^{\infty}e_{m}u^{m},\qquad\exp\left((p-1)\sum_{n=1}^{J}|\operatorname{Re}L_{n}|u^{n}\right)=\sum_{m=0}^{\infty}b_{m}u^{m}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>J</mi></munderover><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{(p-1)\operatorname{Re}\Phi_{r_{\mathrm{out}}}(u)}=\sum_{m=0}^{\infty}e_{m}u^{m},\qquad\exp\left((p-1)\sum_{n=1}^{J}|\operatorname{Re}L_{n}|u^{n}\right)=\sum_{m=0}^{\infty}b_{m}u^{m}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">The Cauchy product formula gives <math id="S3.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|e_{m}|\leq b_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|e_{m}|\leq b_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> for every <math id="S3.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S3.SS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{m}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{m}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. After factoring out <math id="S3.SS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u/r_{\mathrm{out}}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u/r_{\mathrm{out}}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, the term involving <math id="S3.SS1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi_{r_{\mathrm{out}}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi_{r_{\mathrm{out}}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> has degree at most <math id="S3.SS1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J-1</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence the cancellations through degree <math id="S3.SS1.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math> in the expression in braces are equivalent to cancellation of the coefficients of degrees <math id="S3.SS1.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0,\ldots,J-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0,\ldots,J-1</annotation></semantics></math> in the bracket, and thus</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G(u)-Ke^{(p-1)\operatorname{Re}\Phi_{r_{\mathrm{out}}}(u)}-ir_{\mathrm{out}}^{2}\Phi_{r_{\mathrm{out}}}^{\prime}(u)=\sum_{m=J}^{2J}G_{m}u^{m}-K\sum_{m=J}^{\infty}e_{m}u^{m}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G(u)-Ke^{(p-1)\operatorname{Re}\Phi_{r_{\mathrm{out}}}(u)}-ir_{\mathrm{out}}^{2}\Phi_{r_{\mathrm{out}}}^{\prime}(u)=\sum_{m=J}^{2J}G_{m}u^{m}-K\sum_{m=J}^{\infty}e_{m}u^{m}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="S3.SS1.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq u\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq u\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, it follows that</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left|G(u)-Ke^{(p-1)\operatorname{Re}\Phi_{r_{\mathrm{out}}}(u)}-ir_{\mathrm{out}}^{2}\Phi_{r_{\mathrm{out}}}^{\prime}(u)\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left|G(u)-Ke^{(p-1)\operatorname{Re}\Phi_{r_{\mathrm{out}}}(u)}-ir_{\mathrm{out}}^{2}\Phi_{r_{\mathrm{out}}}^{\prime}(u)\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex48.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq u^{J}\left(\sum_{m=J}^{2J}|G_{m}|+K\sum_{m=J}^{\infty}|e_{m}|\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mi>J</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq u^{J}\left(\sum_{m=J}^{2J}|G_{m}|+K\sum_{m=J}^{\infty}|e_{m}|\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq u^{J}\left(\sum_{m=J}^{2J}|G_{m}|+K\chi^{-J}\sum_{m=J}^{\infty}b_{m}\chi^{m}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mi>J</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>χ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>χ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq u^{J}\left(\sum_{m=J}^{2J}|G_{m}|+K\chi^{-J}\sum_{m=J}^{\infty}b_{m}\chi^{m}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mathcal{B}u^{J}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mi>J</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mathcal{B}u^{J},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text">because <math id="S3.SS1.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{m=0}^{\infty}b_{m}\chi^{m}=\exp((p-1)\sum_{n=1}^{J}|\operatorname{Re}L_{n}|\chi^{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>χ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>J</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>χ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{m=0}^{\infty}b_{m}\chi^{m}=\exp((p-1)\sum_{n=1}^{J}|\operatorname{Re}L_{n}|\chi^{n})</annotation></semantics></math>. Multiplication by <math id="S3.SS1.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u/r_{\mathrm{out}}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u/r_{\mathrm{out}}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> proves the first bound in (<a href="#S3.E25" title="In Lemma 3.2. ‣ 3.1. Exterior solution at infinity ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">25</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, for <math id="S3.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq u\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq u\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\operatorname{Re}\Phi_{r_{\mathrm{out}}}(u)|\leq\sum_{n=1}^{J}|\operatorname{Re}L_{n}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>J</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\operatorname{Re}\Phi_{r_{\mathrm{out}}}(u)|\leq\sum_{n=1}^{J}|\operatorname{Re}L_{n}|</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence <math id="S3.SS1.p6.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="|P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)}(r)|\leq Mr^{-2/(p-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≤</mo><mi>M</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)}(r)|\leq Mr^{-2/(p-1)}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S3.SS1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\geq r_{\mathrm{out}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\geq r_{\mathrm{out}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Combining this amplitude bound with <math id="S3.SS1.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u=(r_{\mathrm{out}}/r)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u=(r_{\mathrm{out}}/r)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> gives the second estimate in (<a href="#S3.E25" title="In Lemma 3.2. ‣ 3.1. Exterior solution at infinity ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">25</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">To correct <math id="S3.SS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)}</annotation></semantics></math> to an exact exterior solution, write <math id="S3.SS1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\mathrm{out}}=P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)}+h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>out</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\mathrm{out}}=P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)}+h</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</p>
<table id="S3.Ex51" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\Omega}h=N(P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)}+h)-N(P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)})-\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{out}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>out</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\Omega}h=N(P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)}+h)-N(P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)})-\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{out}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p7.2" class="ltx_p">where the exterior residual is <math id="S3.SS1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{out}}(r):=(L_{\Omega}P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)})(r)-N(P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)}(r))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{out}}(r):=(L_{\Omega}P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)})(r)-N(P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)}(r))</annotation></semantics></math>. Here <math id="S3.SS1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\Omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\Omega}</annotation></semantics></math> is the linear exterior operator from (<a href="#S2.E12" title="In 2.1. Linear exterior modes ‣ 2. Self-similar profile equation ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>). We therefore need an inverse for <math id="S3.SS1.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\Omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\Omega}</annotation></semantics></math> whose output has zero limiting slow and fast modal coefficients, so that the prescribed values of <math id="S3.SS1.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{f}</annotation></semantics></math> are unchanged.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p">Recall the weighted space <math id="S3.SS1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{\nu,r_{\mathrm{out}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{\nu,r_{\mathrm{out}}}</annotation></semantics></math> defined above. For <math id="S3.SS1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\in X_{\nu,r_{\mathrm{out}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in X_{\nu,r_{\mathrm{out}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, use the variation of parameters formula to define</p>
<table id="S3.Ex52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{L}_{\Omega,\infty}^{-1}f)(r):={}S_{\Omega}(r)\int_{r}^{\infty}\frac{F_{\Omega}(\sigma)f(\sigma)}{W_{\Omega}(\sigma)}\,d\sigma\\
-F_{\Omega}(r)\int_{r}^{\infty}\frac{S_{\Omega}(\sigma)f(\sigma)}{W_{\Omega}(\sigma)}\,d\sigma." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>r</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>r</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{L}_{\Omega,\infty}^{-1}f)(r):={}S_{\Omega}(r)\int_{r}^{\infty}\frac{F_{\Omega}(\sigma)f(\sigma)}{W_{\Omega}(\sigma)}\,d\sigma\\
-F_{\Omega}(r)\int_{r}^{\infty}\frac{S_{\Omega}(\sigma)f(\sigma)}{W_{\Omega}(\sigma)}\,d\sigma.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p8.2" class="ltx_p">The following lemma shows that this gives a right inverse to <math id="S3.SS1.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\Omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\Omega}</annotation></semantics></math> on the weighted space <math id="S3.SS1.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{\nu,r_{\mathrm{out}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{\nu,r_{\mathrm{out}}}</annotation></semantics></math> and provides explicit bounds for the inverse. These bounds must be compatible with the computer-assisted verification, so the constants are tracked explicitly.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmthm3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmthm3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3.3</span></span><span id="S3.Thmthm3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmthm3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmthm3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmthm3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose <math id="S3.Thmthm3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\mathrm{out}}\geq 32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\mathrm{out}}\geq 32</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="S3.Thmthm3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu&gt;d-\frac{2}{p-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu&gt;d-\frac{2}{p-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S3.Thmthm3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\Omega|\leq\Omega_{\mathrm{bd}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>bd</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\Omega|\leq\Omega_{\mathrm{bd}}</annotation></semantics></math>, where</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega_{\mathrm{bd}}:=\begin{cases}7/5,&amp;(d,p)=(3,27),\\
59/20,&amp;(d,p)=(4,9),\\
7/4,&amp;(d,p)=(5,7).\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>bd</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>27</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mn>59</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>9</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega_{\mathrm{bd}}:=\begin{cases}7/5,&amp;(d,p)=(3,27),\\
59/20,&amp;(d,p)=(4,9),\\
7/4,&amp;(d,p)=(5,7).\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.Thmthm3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmthm3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then, for every <math id="S3.Thmthm3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\in X_{\nu,r_{\mathrm{out}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in X_{\nu,r_{\mathrm{out}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the function <math id="S3.Thmthm3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\Omega,\infty}^{-1}f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\Omega,\infty}^{-1}f</annotation></semantics></math> belongs to <math id="S3.Thmthm3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{2}([r_{\mathrm{out}},\infty))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{2}([r_{\mathrm{out}},\infty))</annotation></semantics></math> and satisfies the equality <math id="S3.Thmthm3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\Omega}\mathcal{L}_{\Omega,\infty}^{-1}f=f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\Omega}\mathcal{L}_{\Omega,\infty}^{-1}f=f</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, there is an explicit constant <math id="S3.Thmthm3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{C}_{\nu,r_{\mathrm{out}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℭ</mi><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{C}_{\nu,r_{\mathrm{out}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, independent of <math id="S3.Thmthm3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.Thmthm3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>, such that</span></p>
<table id="S3.E26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(26)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathcal{L}_{\Omega,\infty}^{-1}f\|_{\nu,r_{\mathrm{out}}}\leq\mathfrak{C}_{\nu,r_{\mathrm{out}}}\|f\|_{\nu,r_{\mathrm{out}}},\qquad\|(\mathcal{L}_{\Omega,\infty}^{-1}f)^{\prime}\|_{\nu-1,r_{\mathrm{out}}}\leq\mathfrak{C}_{\nu,r_{\mathrm{out}}}\|f\|_{\nu,r_{\mathrm{out}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ℭ</mi><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ℭ</mi><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathcal{L}_{\Omega,\infty}^{-1}f\|_{\nu,r_{\mathrm{out}}}\leq\mathfrak{C}_{\nu,r_{\mathrm{out}}}\|f\|_{\nu,r_{\mathrm{out}}},\qquad\|(\mathcal{L}_{\Omega,\infty}^{-1}f)^{\prime}\|_{\nu-1,r_{\mathrm{out}}}\leq\mathfrak{C}_{\nu,r_{\mathrm{out}}}\|f\|_{\nu,r_{\mathrm{out}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Recall <math id="S3.SS1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> defined by (<a href="#S2.E13" title="In 2.1. Linear exterior modes ‣ 2. Self-similar profile equation ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>). We first normalize <math id="S3.SS1.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\Omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\Omega}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{\Omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{\Omega}</annotation></semantics></math> using these parameters and derive estimates on the rescaled functions. Let</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex54" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{S}_{\Omega}(r):=r^{2\mu}S_{\Omega}(r),\qquad\widehat{F}_{\Omega}(r):=e^{\frac{ir^{2}}{4}}r^{2\kappa}F_{\Omega}(r)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{S}_{\Omega}(r):=r^{2\mu}S_{\Omega}(r),\qquad\widehat{F}_{\Omega}(r):=e^{\frac{ir^{2}}{4}}r^{2\kappa}F_{\Omega}(r).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">Rescaling (<a href="#S2.E14" title="In Lemma 2.2. ‣ 2.1. Linear exterior modes ‣ 2. Self-similar profile equation ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>), we obtain <math id="S3.SS1.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{S}_{\Omega}=H_{\mu}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>μ</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{S}_{\Omega}=H_{\mu}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{F}_{\Omega}=H_{\kappa}^{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>κ</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{F}_{\Omega}=H_{\kappa}^{-}</annotation></semantics></math>, where</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex55" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{z}^{\pm}(r):=\frac{1}{\Gamma(z)}\int_{0}^{\infty}e^{-t}t^{z-1}\left(1\pm\frac{4it}{r^{2}}\right)^{\frac{d}{2}-1-z}\,dt." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>±</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>±</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{z}^{\pm}(r):=\frac{1}{\Gamma(z)}\int_{0}^{\infty}e^{-t}t^{z-1}\left(1\pm\frac{4it}{r^{2}}\right)^{\frac{d}{2}-1-z}\,dt.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p9.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p9.3.1" class="ltx_text">We estimate both integrals at once. Write <math id="S3.SS1.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z=x+i\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z=x+i\omega</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="S3.SS1.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.p9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\omega|\leq\Omega_{\mathrm{bd}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>bd</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\omega|\leq\Omega_{\mathrm{bd}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and set</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex56" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha:=\frac{d}{2}-1-z,\qquad c(x):=\Omega_{\mathrm{bd}}+\max\left\{0,\frac{d}{2}-2-x\right\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>bd</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha:=\frac{d}{2}-1-z,\qquad c(x):=\Omega_{\mathrm{bd}}+\max\left\{0,\frac{d}{2}-2-x\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p9.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p9.4.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="S3.SS1.p9.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\arg(1\pm iv)|\leq v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>±</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\arg(1\pm iv)|\leq v</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.p9.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log|1\pm iv|\leq v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>±</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log|1\pm iv|\leq v</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S3.SS1.p9.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, the principal powers satisfy</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex57" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|(1\pm iv)^{\alpha-1}|=\exp\left[\left(\frac{d}{2}-2-x\right)\log|1\pm iv|+\omega\arg(1\pm iv)\right]\leq e^{c(x)v}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>±</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>±</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>±</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|(1\pm iv)^{\alpha-1}|=\exp\left[\left(\frac{d}{2}-2-x\right)\log|1\pm iv|+\omega\arg(1\pm iv)\right]\leq e^{c(x)v}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p9.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p9.5.1" class="ltx_text">Integrating the derivative in <math id="S3.SS1.p9.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> therefore gives</span></p>
<table id="S3.E27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(27)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|(1\pm iv)^{\alpha}-1|\leq|\alpha|\int_{0}^{v}e^{c(x)w}\,dw\leq|\alpha|ve^{c(x)v}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>±</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>α</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>v</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|(1\pm iv)^{\alpha}-1|\leq|\alpha|\int_{0}^{v}e^{c(x)w}\,dw\leq|\alpha|ve^{c(x)v}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p9.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p9.6.1" class="ltx_text">For the stated parameter pairs, <math id="S3.SS1.p9.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c(x)\leq 59/20+1/2&lt;32^{2}/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>59</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msup><mn>32</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(x)\leq 59/20+1/2&lt;32^{2}/4</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus <math id="S3.SS1.p9.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{x}:=1-4c(x)/32^{2}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mn>32</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{x}:=1-4c(x)/32^{2}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Subtracting the Gamma integral <math id="S3.SS1.p9.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma(z)^{-1}\int_{0}^{\infty}e^{-t}t^{z-1}\,dt=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma(z)^{-1}\int_{0}^{\infty}e^{-t}t^{z-1}\,dt=1</annotation></semantics></math>, we infer, for <math id="S3.SS1.p9.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\geq 32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\geq 32</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex58" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex58X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex58X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|H_{z}^{\pm}(r)-1|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>±</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|H_{z}^{\pm}(r)-1|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex58X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{4|\alpha|}{r^{2}|\Gamma(z)|}\int_{0}^{\infty}e^{-(1-4c(x)/r^{2})t}t^{x}\,dt" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>x</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{4|\alpha|}{r^{2}|\Gamma(z)|}\int_{0}^{\infty}e^{-(1-4c(x)/r^{2})t}t^{x}\,dt</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex58Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex58Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{4|\alpha|\Gamma(x+1)}{r^{2}|\Gamma(z)|}\left(1-\frac{4c(x)}{r^{2}}\right)^{-x-1}\leq\frac{4|\alpha|\Gamma(x+1)}{r^{2}|\Gamma(z)|}\delta_{x}^{-x-1}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{4|\alpha|\Gamma(x+1)}{r^{2}|\Gamma(z)|}\left(1-\frac{4c(x)}{r^{2}}\right)^{-x-1}\leq\frac{4|\alpha|\Gamma(x+1)}{r^{2}|\Gamma(z)|}\delta_{x}^{-x-1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p9.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p9.7.1" class="ltx_text">To estimate the derivative, we compute</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex59" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\frac{d}{dr}\left(1\pm\frac{4it}{r^{2}}\right)^{\alpha}=\mp\frac{8i\alpha t}{r^{2}}\left(1\pm\frac{4it}{r^{2}}\right)^{\alpha-1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>±</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>α</mi></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>∓</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>±</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\frac{d}{dr}\left(1\pm\frac{4it}{r^{2}}\right)^{\alpha}=\mp\frac{8i\alpha t}{r^{2}}\left(1\pm\frac{4it}{r^{2}}\right)^{\alpha-1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p9.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p9.8.1" class="ltx_text">The derivative integrand is bounded by a constant times <math id="S3.SS1.p9.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{x}e^{-\delta_{x}t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>x</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{x}e^{-\delta_{x}t}</annotation></semantics></math>, uniformly for <math id="S3.SS1.p9.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\geq 32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\geq 32</annotation></semantics></math>; the original integrand is bounded by a constant times <math id="S3.SS1.p9.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{-t}t^{x-1}+t^{x}e^{-\delta_{x}t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>x</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{-t}t^{x-1}+t^{x}e^{-\delta_{x}t}</annotation></semantics></math>, by (<a href="#S3.E27" title="In Proof. ‣ 3.1. Exterior solution at infinity ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">27</span></a>). These integrable bounds justify differentiation under the integral and yield</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex60" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|r(H_{z}^{\pm})^{\prime}(r)|\leq\frac{8|\alpha|}{r^{2}|\Gamma(z)|}\int_{0}^{\infty}t^{x}e^{-\delta_{x}t}\,dt\\
=\frac{8|\alpha|\Gamma(x+1)}{r^{2}|\Gamma(z)|}\delta_{x}^{-x-1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>±</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>x</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|r(H_{z}^{\pm})^{\prime}(r)|\leq\frac{8|\alpha|}{r^{2}|\Gamma(z)|}\int_{0}^{\infty}t^{x}e^{-\delta_{x}t}\,dt\\
=\frac{8|\alpha|\Gamma(x+1)}{r^{2}|\Gamma(z)|}\delta_{x}^{-x-1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">It remains to bound the Gamma quotient uniformly in <math id="S3.SS1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega</annotation></semantics></math>. Euler’s product formula gives</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex61" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\Gamma(x)}{|\Gamma(x+i\omega)|}=\prod_{n=0}^{\infty}\left(1+\frac{\omega^{2}}{(x+n)^{2}}\right)^{1/2}\leq R(x)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\Gamma(x)}{|\Gamma(x+i\omega)|}=\prod_{n=0}^{\infty}\left(1+\frac{\omega^{2}}{(x+n)^{2}}\right)^{1/2}\leq R(x),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p10.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p10.3.1" class="ltx_text">where</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex62" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(x):=\prod_{n=0}^{15}\left(1+\frac{\Omega_{\mathrm{bd}}^{2}}{(x+n)^{2}}\right)^{1/2}\exp\left[\frac{\Omega_{\mathrm{bd}}^{2}}{2}\left((x+16)^{-2}+(x+16)^{-1}\right)\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mn>15</mn></munderover><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>bd</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mfrac><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>bd</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(x):=\prod_{n=0}^{15}\left(1+\frac{\Omega_{\mathrm{bd}}^{2}}{(x+n)^{2}}\right)^{1/2}\exp\left[\frac{\Omega_{\mathrm{bd}}^{2}}{2}\left((x+16)^{-2}+(x+16)^{-1}\right)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p10.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p10.4.1" class="ltx_text">Indeed, <math id="S3.SS1.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(1+t)\leq t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(1+t)\leq t</annotation></semantics></math> bounds the logarithm of the product tail, and the integral comparison gives</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex63" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{n=16}^{\infty}(x+n)^{-2}\leq(x+16)^{-2}+\int_{16}^{\infty}(x+t)^{-2}\,dt=(x+16)^{-2}+(x+16)^{-1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mn>16</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{n=16}^{\infty}(x+n)^{-2}\leq(x+16)^{-2}+\int_{16}^{\infty}(x+t)^{-2}\,dt=(x+16)^{-2}+(x+16)^{-1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p10.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p10.5.1" class="ltx_text">Define the explicit constants</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex64" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex64X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex64X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle D(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex64X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=4x\sqrt{\left(\frac{d}{2}-1-x\right)^{2}+\Omega_{\mathrm{bd}}^{2}}\,R(x)\delta_{x}^{-x-1}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>bd</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=4x\sqrt{\left(\frac{d}{2}-1-x\right)^{2}+\Omega_{\mathrm{bd}}^{2}}\,R(x)\delta_{x}^{-x-1},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex64Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex64Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle D_{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{S}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex64Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=D\left(\frac{1}{p-1}\right),\qquad D_{F}:=D\left(\frac{d}{2}-\frac{1}{p-1}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo lspace="0em">=</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>D</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=D\left(\frac{1}{p-1}\right),\qquad D_{F}:=D\left(\frac{d}{2}-\frac{1}{p-1}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p10.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p10.6.1" class="ltx_text">Using <math id="S3.SS1.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma(x+1)=x\Gamma(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma(x+1)=x\Gamma(x)</annotation></semantics></math> and applying the preceding bounds with <math id="S3.SS1.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z=\mu,\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z=\mu,\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain</span></p>
<table id="S3.E28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S3.E28X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_left">(28)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E28X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|\widehat{S}_{\Omega}(r)-1|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|\widehat{S}_{\Omega}(r)-1|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E28X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq D_{S}r^{-2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq D_{S}r^{-2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E28X.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|r\widehat{S}_{\Omega}^{\prime}(r)|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|r\widehat{S}_{\Omega}^{\prime}(r)|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E28X.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 2D_{S}r^{-2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 2D_{S}r^{-2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E28Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E28Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|\widehat{F}_{\Omega}(r)-1|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|\widehat{F}_{\Omega}(r)-1|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E28Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq D_{F}r^{-2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq D_{F}r^{-2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E28Xa.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|r\widehat{F}_{\Omega}^{\prime}(r)|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|r\widehat{F}_{\Omega}^{\prime}(r)|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E28Xa.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 2D_{F}r^{-2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 2D_{F}r^{-2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p11.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p11.2.1" class="ltx_text">Returning to the original modes, we compute</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex65" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\Omega}^{\prime}(r)=r^{-2\mu-1}\left(-2\mu\widehat{S}_{\Omega}+r\widehat{S}_{\Omega}^{\prime}\right),\qquad F_{\Omega}^{\prime}(r)=e^{-\frac{ir^{2}}{4}}r^{-2\kappa}\left[\widehat{F}_{\Omega}^{\prime}-\left(\frac{ir}{2}+\frac{2\kappa}{r}\right)\widehat{F}_{\Omega}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mi>r</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\Omega}^{\prime}(r)=r^{-2\mu-1}\left(-2\mu\widehat{S}_{\Omega}+r\widehat{S}_{\Omega}^{\prime}\right),\qquad F_{\Omega}^{\prime}(r)=e^{-\frac{ir^{2}}{4}}r^{-2\kappa}\left[\widehat{F}_{\Omega}^{\prime}-\left(\frac{ir}{2}+\frac{2\kappa}{r}\right)\widehat{F}_{\Omega}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p11.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p11.3.1" class="ltx_text">Hence (<a href="#S3.E28" title="In Proof. ‣ 3.1. Exterior solution at infinity ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a>), together with <math id="S3.SS1.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mu|\leq\sqrt{\frac{1}{(p-1)^{2}}+\Omega_{\mathrm{bd}}^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msqrt><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>bd</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mu|\leq\sqrt{\frac{1}{(p-1)^{2}}+\Omega_{\mathrm{bd}}^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\kappa|\leq\sqrt{\left(\frac{d}{2}-\frac{1}{p-1}\right)^{2}+\Omega_{\mathrm{bd}}^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>bd</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\kappa|\leq\sqrt{\left(\frac{d}{2}-\frac{1}{p-1}\right)^{2}+\Omega_{\mathrm{bd}}^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>, yields</span></p>
<table id="S3.E29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S3.E29X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_left">(29)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E29X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r^{\frac{2}{p-1}}|S_{\Omega}(r)|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r^{\frac{2}{p-1}}|S_{\Omega}(r)|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E29X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq A_{r_{\mathrm{out}}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq A_{r_{\mathrm{out}}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E29X.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r^{\frac{2}{p-1}+1}|S_{\Omega}^{\prime}(r)|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r^{\frac{2}{p-1}+1}|S_{\Omega}^{\prime}(r)|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E29X.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq A_{r_{\mathrm{out}}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq A_{r_{\mathrm{out}}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E29Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E29Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r^{d-\frac{2}{p-1}}|F_{\Omega}(r)|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r^{d-\frac{2}{p-1}}|F_{\Omega}(r)|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E29Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq A_{r_{\mathrm{out}}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq A_{r_{\mathrm{out}}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E29Xa.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r^{d-\frac{2}{p-1}-1}|F_{\Omega}^{\prime}(r)|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r^{d-\frac{2}{p-1}-1}|F_{\Omega}^{\prime}(r)|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E29Xa.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq A_{r_{\mathrm{out}}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq A_{r_{\mathrm{out}}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p11.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p11.4.1" class="ltx_text">for <math id="S3.SS1.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\geq r_{\mathrm{out}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\geq r_{\mathrm{out}}</annotation></semantics></math>, where we choose</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex66" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex66X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex66X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A_{r_{\mathrm{out}}}:=\max\Biggl\{" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub></msub><mo>:=</mo><mi>max</mi><mo stretchy="false">{</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A_{r_{\mathrm{out}}}:=\max\Biggl\{</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex66X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 1+\frac{D_{S}}{r_{\mathrm{out}}^{2}},\quad 1+\frac{D_{F}}{r_{\mathrm{out}}^{2}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 1+\frac{D_{S}}{r_{\mathrm{out}}^{2}},\quad 1+\frac{D_{F}}{r_{\mathrm{out}}^{2}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex66Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex66Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 2\sqrt{\frac{1}{(p-1)^{2}}+\Omega_{\mathrm{bd}}^{2}}\left(1+\frac{D_{S}}{r_{\mathrm{out}}^{2}}\right)+\frac{2D_{S}}{r_{\mathrm{out}}^{2}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>bd</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 2\sqrt{\frac{1}{(p-1)^{2}}+\Omega_{\mathrm{bd}}^{2}}\left(1+\frac{D_{S}}{r_{\mathrm{out}}^{2}}\right)+\frac{2D_{S}}{r_{\mathrm{out}}^{2}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex66Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex66Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left(\frac{1}{2}+\frac{2\sqrt{\left(\frac{d}{2}-\frac{1}{p-1}\right)^{2}+\Omega_{\mathrm{bd}}^{2}}}{r_{\mathrm{out}}^{2}}\right)\left(1+\frac{D_{F}}{r_{\mathrm{out}}^{2}}\right)+\frac{2D_{F}}{r_{\mathrm{out}}^{4}}\Biggr\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>bd</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></msqrt></mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi><mn>4</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left(\frac{1}{2}+\frac{2\sqrt{\left(\frac{d}{2}-\frac{1}{p-1}\right)^{2}+\Omega_{\mathrm{bd}}^{2}}}{r_{\mathrm{out}}^{2}}\right)\left(1+\frac{D_{F}}{r_{\mathrm{out}}^{2}}\right)+\frac{2D_{F}}{r_{\mathrm{out}}^{4}}\Biggr\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p11.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p11.5.1" class="ltx_text">Here we used <math id="S3.SS1.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{-j}\leq r_{\mathrm{out}}^{-j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msup><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{-j}\leq r_{\mathrm{out}}^{-j}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S3.SS1.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=2,4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=2,4</annotation></semantics></math> to make the bounds uniform on the exterior interval.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p12.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p12.2.1" class="ltx_text">Now we will show that the inverse is well-defined and use the bounds on the unscaled modes to derive bounds on this inverse. Let <math id="S3.SS1.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\in X_{\nu,r_{\mathrm{out}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in X_{\nu,r_{\mathrm{out}}}</annotation></semantics></math> and write</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex67" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{F}(r):=\int_{r}^{\infty}\frac{F_{\Omega}(\sigma)f(\sigma)}{W_{\Omega}(\sigma)}\,d\sigma,\qquad I_{S}(r):=\int_{r}^{\infty}\frac{S_{\Omega}(\sigma)f(\sigma)}{W_{\Omega}(\sigma)}\,d\sigma." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>r</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>r</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{F}(r):=\int_{r}^{\infty}\frac{F_{\Omega}(\sigma)f(\sigma)}{W_{\Omega}(\sigma)}\,d\sigma,\qquad I_{S}(r):=\int_{r}^{\infty}\frac{S_{\Omega}(\sigma)f(\sigma)}{W_{\Omega}(\sigma)}\,d\sigma.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p12.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p12.3.1" class="ltx_text">For each of the three parameter pairs, <math id="S3.SS1.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d-\frac{2}{p-1}&gt;\frac{2}{p-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d-\frac{2}{p-1}&gt;\frac{2}{p-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, so the assumption on <math id="S3.SS1.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ν</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu</annotation></semantics></math> implies both <math id="S3.SS1.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu&gt;d-\frac{2}{p-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu&gt;d-\frac{2}{p-1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.p12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu&gt;\frac{2}{p-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu&gt;\frac{2}{p-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Using <math id="S3.SS1.p12.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|W_{\Omega}(r)|=r^{1-d}/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|W_{\Omega}(r)|=r^{1-d}/2</annotation></semantics></math> from (<a href="#S2.E15" title="In Proof. ‣ 2.1. Linear exterior modes ‣ 2. Self-similar profile equation ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>) and (<a href="#S3.E29" title="In Proof. ‣ 3.1. Exterior solution at infinity ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">29</span></a>), we obtain the absolutely convergent tail estimates</span></p>
<table id="S3.E30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S3.E30X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_left">(30)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E30X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|I_{F}(r)|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|I_{F}(r)|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E30X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 2A_{r_{\mathrm{out}}}\|f\|_{\nu,r_{\mathrm{out}}}\int_{r}^{\infty}\sigma^{\frac{2}{p-1}-\nu-1}\,d\sigma=\frac{2A_{r_{\mathrm{out}}}}{\nu-\frac{2}{p-1}}\|f\|_{\nu,r_{\mathrm{out}}}r^{\frac{2}{p-1}-\nu}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>r</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">d</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 2A_{r_{\mathrm{out}}}\|f\|_{\nu,r_{\mathrm{out}}}\int_{r}^{\infty}\sigma^{\frac{2}{p-1}-\nu-1}\,d\sigma=\frac{2A_{r_{\mathrm{out}}}}{\nu-\frac{2}{p-1}}\|f\|_{\nu,r_{\mathrm{out}}}r^{\frac{2}{p-1}-\nu},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E30Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E30Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|I_{S}(r)|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|I_{S}(r)|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E30Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 2A_{r_{\mathrm{out}}}\|f\|_{\nu,r_{\mathrm{out}}}\int_{r}^{\infty}\sigma^{d-\frac{2}{p-1}-\nu-1}\,d\sigma=\frac{2A_{r_{\mathrm{out}}}}{\nu+\frac{2}{p-1}-d}\|f\|_{\nu,r_{\mathrm{out}}}r^{d-\frac{2}{p-1}-\nu}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>r</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">d</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 2A_{r_{\mathrm{out}}}\|f\|_{\nu,r_{\mathrm{out}}}\int_{r}^{\infty}\sigma^{d-\frac{2}{p-1}-\nu-1}\,d\sigma=\frac{2A_{r_{\mathrm{out}}}}{\nu+\frac{2}{p-1}-d}\|f\|_{\nu,r_{\mathrm{out}}}r^{d-\frac{2}{p-1}-\nu}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p12.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p12.4.1" class="ltx_text">Thus <math id="S3.SS1.p12.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u:=\mathcal{L}_{\Omega,\infty}^{-1}f=S_{\Omega}I_{F}-F_{\Omega}I_{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u:=\mathcal{L}_{\Omega,\infty}^{-1}f=S_{\Omega}I_{F}-F_{\Omega}I_{S}</annotation></semantics></math> is well-defined. Since <math id="S3.SS1.p12.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is continuous, variation of parameters gives <math id="S3.SS1.p12.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in C^{2}([r_{\mathrm{out}},\infty))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in C^{2}([r_{\mathrm{out}},\infty))</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.p12.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\Omega}u=f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\Omega}u=f</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular, the endpoint terms cancel in the first derivative:</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex68" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u^{\prime}=S_{\Omega}^{\prime}I_{F}-F_{\Omega}^{\prime}I_{S}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u^{\prime}=S_{\Omega}^{\prime}I_{F}-F_{\Omega}^{\prime}I_{S}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p12.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p12.5.1" class="ltx_text">Combining (<a href="#S3.E29" title="In Proof. ‣ 3.1. Exterior solution at infinity ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">29</span></a>) and (<a href="#S3.E30" title="In Proof. ‣ 3.1. Exterior solution at infinity ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">30</span></a>) with these formulas yields</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex69" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex69X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex69X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r^{\nu}|u(r)|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>ν</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r^{\nu}|u(r)|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex69X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 2A_{r_{\mathrm{out}}}^{2}\left(\frac{1}{\nu-\frac{2}{p-1}}+\frac{1}{\nu+\frac{2}{p-1}-d}\right)\|f\|_{\nu,r_{\mathrm{out}}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 2A_{r_{\mathrm{out}}}^{2}\left(\frac{1}{\nu-\frac{2}{p-1}}+\frac{1}{\nu+\frac{2}{p-1}-d}\right)\|f\|_{\nu,r_{\mathrm{out}}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex69Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex69Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r^{\nu-1}|u^{\prime}(r)|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r^{\nu-1}|u^{\prime}(r)|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex69Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 2A_{r_{\mathrm{out}}}^{2}\left(\frac{r^{-2}}{\nu-\frac{2}{p-1}}+\frac{1}{\nu+\frac{2}{p-1}-d}\right)\|f\|_{\nu,r_{\mathrm{out}}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 2A_{r_{\mathrm{out}}}^{2}\left(\frac{r^{-2}}{\nu-\frac{2}{p-1}}+\frac{1}{\nu+\frac{2}{p-1}-d}\right)\|f\|_{\nu,r_{\mathrm{out}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p12.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p12.6.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="S3.SS1.p12.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\geq 32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\geq 32</annotation></semantics></math>, taking suprema proves (<a href="#S3.E26" title="In Lemma 3.3. ‣ 3.1. Exterior solution at infinity ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26</span></a>) with</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex70" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{C}_{\nu,r_{\mathrm{out}}}:=2A_{r_{\mathrm{out}}}^{2}\left(\frac{1}{\nu-\frac{2}{p-1}}+\frac{1}{\nu+\frac{2}{p-1}-d}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ℭ</mi><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{C}_{\nu,r_{\mathrm{out}}}:=2A_{r_{\mathrm{out}}}^{2}\left(\frac{1}{\nu-\frac{2}{p-1}}+\frac{1}{\nu+\frac{2}{p-1}-d}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p12.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p12.7.1" class="ltx_text">All constants depend only on <math id="S3.SS1.p12.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS1.p12.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS1.p12.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega_{\mathrm{bd}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>bd</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega_{\mathrm{bd}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS1.p12.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\mathrm{out}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\mathrm{out}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S3.SS1.p12.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ν</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu</annotation></semantics></math>, and are therefore independent of <math id="S3.SS1.p12.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.p12.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p13.1" class="ltx_p">We now use this right inverse to correct the finite approximation in the weighted exterior space <math id="S3.SS1.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{\nu,r_{\mathrm{out}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{\nu,r_{\mathrm{out}}}</annotation></semantics></math>. More precisely, we seek an additive correction <math id="S3.SS1.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S3.SS1.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\mathrm{out}}=P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)}+h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>out</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\mathrm{out}}=P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)}+h</annotation></semantics></math> solves the full nonlinear profile equation. We solve for this correction using a fixed point argument. Its weighted decay will preserve <math id="S3.SS1.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{s}=K^{1/(p-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{s}=K^{1/(p-1)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{f}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{f}=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmthm4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_prop">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmthm4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 3.4</span></span><span id="S3.Thmthm4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmthm4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\mathrm{out}}\geq 32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\mathrm{out}}\geq 32</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the
frequency bound in Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmthm3" title="Lemma 3.3. ‣ 3.1. Exterior solution at infinity ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>. Set
<math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu=2/(p-1)+2J+2&gt;d-2/(p-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu=2/(p-1)+2J+2&gt;d-2/(p-1)</annotation></semantics></math>.
If there is a <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{\mathrm{ext}}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>ext</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{\mathrm{ext}}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="S3.E31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S3.E31X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_left">(31)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E31X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p\mathfrak{C}_{\nu,r_{\mathrm{out}}}r_{\mathrm{out}}^{-2}(M+\delta_{\mathrm{ext}})^{p-1}&lt;1," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ℭ</mi><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>ext</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p\mathfrak{C}_{\nu,r_{\mathrm{out}}}r_{\mathrm{out}}^{-2}(M+\delta_{\mathrm{ext}})^{p-1}&lt;1,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E31Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E31Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\mathfrak{C}_{\nu,r_{\mathrm{out}}}M\mathcal{B}}{r_{\mathrm{out}}^{2}}\leq\left[1-p\mathfrak{C}_{\nu,r_{\mathrm{out}}}r_{\mathrm{out}}^{-2}(M+\delta_{\mathrm{ext}})^{p-1}\right]\delta_{\mathrm{ext}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>ℭ</mi><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ℭ</mi><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>ext</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>ext</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\mathfrak{C}_{\nu,r_{\mathrm{out}}}M\mathcal{B}}{r_{\mathrm{out}}^{2}}\leq\left[1-p\mathfrak{C}_{\nu,r_{\mathrm{out}}}r_{\mathrm{out}}^{-2}(M+\delta_{\mathrm{ext}})^{p-1}\right]\delta_{\mathrm{ext}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E31Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E31Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\delta_{\mathrm{ext}}&lt;\frac{K^{\frac{2}{p-1}}}{M}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>ext</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>K</mi><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup><mi>M</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\delta_{\mathrm{ext}}&lt;\frac{K^{\frac{2}{p-1}}}{M},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">then there is a smooth nonvanishing exterior solution <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\mathrm{out}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>out</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\mathrm{out}}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{s}=K^{1/(p-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{s}=K^{1/(p-1)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{f}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{f}=0</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\geq r_{\mathrm{out}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\geq r_{\mathrm{out}}</annotation></semantics></math> it satisfies</span></p>
<table id="S3.E32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(32)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|Q^{\mathrm{out}}-P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)}|\leq\delta_{\mathrm{ext}}r_{\mathrm{out}}^{2J+2}r^{-\frac{2}{p-1}-2J-2},\qquad|(Q^{\mathrm{out}})^{\prime}-(P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)})^{\prime}|\leq\delta_{\mathrm{ext}}r_{\mathrm{out}}^{2J+2}r^{-\frac{2}{p-1}-2J-1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>out</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>ext</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>out</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>ext</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|Q^{\mathrm{out}}-P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)}|\leq\delta_{\mathrm{ext}}r_{\mathrm{out}}^{2J+2}r^{-\frac{2}{p-1}-2J-2},\qquad|(Q^{\mathrm{out}})^{\prime}-(P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)})^{\prime}|\leq\delta_{\mathrm{ext}}r_{\mathrm{out}}^{2J+2}r^{-\frac{2}{p-1}-2J-1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS1.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">We apply the inverse from Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmthm3" title="Lemma 3.3. ‣ 3.1. Exterior solution at infinity ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a> to the correction equation. The three conditions in (<a href="#S3.E31" title="In Proposition 3.4. ‣ 3.1. Exterior solution at infinity ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">31</span></a>) ensure, respectively, contraction, invariance of the correction ball, and nonvanishing of the resulting profile.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="S3.SS1.p15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\operatorname{Re}\beta=-2/(p-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mi>β</mi><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Re}\beta=-2/(p-1)</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex71" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)}(r)|=K^{\frac{1}{p-1}}r^{-\frac{2}{p-1}}e^{\operatorname{Re}\Phi_{r_{\mathrm{out}}}(u)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)}(r)|=K^{\frac{1}{p-1}}r^{-\frac{2}{p-1}}e^{\operatorname{Re}\Phi_{r_{\mathrm{out}}}(u)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p15.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p15.2.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="S3.SS1.p15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq u\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq u\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex72" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex72.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\operatorname{Re}\Phi_{r_{\mathrm{out}}}(u)|\leq\sum_{n=1}^{J}|\operatorname{Re}L_{n}|u^{n}\leq\sum_{n=1}^{J}|\operatorname{Re}L_{n}|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>J</mi></munderover><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>J</mi></munderover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\operatorname{Re}\Phi_{r_{\mathrm{out}}}(u)|\leq\sum_{n=1}^{J}|\operatorname{Re}L_{n}|u^{n}\leq\sum_{n=1}^{J}|\operatorname{Re}L_{n}|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p15.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p15.3.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex73" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex73.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)}(r)|\geq\frac{K^{\frac{2}{p-1}}}{M}r^{-\frac{2}{p-1}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>K</mi><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup><mi>M</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)}(r)|\geq\frac{K^{\frac{2}{p-1}}}{M}r^{-\frac{2}{p-1}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p15.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p15.4.1" class="ltx_text">This lower bound will prevent the correction from producing a zero.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p16" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text">Consider the closed ball <math id="S3.SS1.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{h\in X_{\nu,r_{\mathrm{out}}}:\|h\|_{\nu,r_{\mathrm{out}}}\leq\delta_{\mathrm{ext}}r_{\mathrm{out}}^{2J+2}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>ext</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{h\in X_{\nu,r_{\mathrm{out}}}:\|h\|_{\nu,r_{\mathrm{out}}}\leq\delta_{\mathrm{ext}}r_{\mathrm{out}}^{2J+2}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="S3.SS1.p16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> in this ball and <math id="S3.SS1.p16.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\geq r_{\mathrm{out}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\geq r_{\mathrm{out}}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex74" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|h(r)|\leq\delta_{\mathrm{ext}}r_{\mathrm{out}}^{2J+2}r^{-\nu}=\delta_{\mathrm{ext}}r_{\mathrm{out}}^{2J+2}r^{-\frac{2}{p-1}-2J-2}\leq\delta_{\mathrm{ext}}r^{-\frac{2}{p-1}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>ext</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>ext</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>ext</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|h(r)|\leq\delta_{\mathrm{ext}}r_{\mathrm{out}}^{2J+2}r^{-\nu}=\delta_{\mathrm{ext}}r_{\mathrm{out}}^{2J+2}r^{-\frac{2}{p-1}-2J-2}\leq\delta_{\mathrm{ext}}r^{-\frac{2}{p-1}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p16.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p16.2.1" class="ltx_text">Consequently, <math id="S3.SS1.p16.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="|P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)}+h|\leq(M+\delta_{\mathrm{ext}})r^{-2/(p-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>ext</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)}+h|\leq(M+\delta_{\mathrm{ext}})r^{-2/(p-1)}</annotation></semantics></math>. We consider the map</span></p>
<table id="S3.E33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(33)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\longmapsto\mathcal{L}_{\Omega,\infty}^{-1}\{N(P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)}+h)-N(P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)})-\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{out}}\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟼</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>out</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\longmapsto\mathcal{L}_{\Omega,\infty}^{-1}\{N(P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)}+h)-N(P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)})-\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{out}}\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p16.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p16.3.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="S3.SS1.p16.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|DN(q)\|\leq p|q|^{p-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|DN(q)\|\leq p|q|^{p-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, the first condition in (<a href="#S3.E31" title="In Proposition 3.4. ‣ 3.1. Exterior solution at infinity ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">31</span></a>) makes (<a href="#S3.E33" title="In Proof. ‣ 3.1. Exterior solution at infinity ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">33</span></a>) a contraction. At zero, the inverse estimate and (<a href="#S3.E25" title="In Lemma 3.2. ‣ 3.1. Exterior solution at infinity ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">25</span></a>) give the norm bound <math id="S3.SS1.p16.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{C}_{\nu,r_{\mathrm{out}}}Mr_{\mathrm{out}}^{2J}\mathcal{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ℭ</mi><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{C}_{\nu,r_{\mathrm{out}}}Mr_{\mathrm{out}}^{2J}\mathcal{B}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus the second condition in (<a href="#S3.E31" title="In Proposition 3.4. ‣ 3.1. Exterior solution at infinity ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">31</span></a>) makes this ball invariant. Banach’s fixed-point theorem gives <math id="S3.SS1.p16.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>, and the derivative estimate in Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmthm3" title="Lemma 3.3. ‣ 3.1. Exterior solution at infinity ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a> yields (<a href="#S3.E32" title="In Proposition 3.4. ‣ 3.1. Exterior solution at infinity ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">32</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p17" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p17.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p17.1.1" class="ltx_text">The inverse identity gives the profile equation. Since</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex75" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex75.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|h(r)|\leq\delta_{\mathrm{ext}}r^{-\frac{2}{p-1}}&lt;K^{\frac{2}{p-1}}M^{-1}r^{-\frac{2}{p-1}}\leq|P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)}(r)|," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>ext</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|h(r)|\leq\delta_{\mathrm{ext}}r^{-\frac{2}{p-1}}&lt;K^{\frac{2}{p-1}}M^{-1}r^{-\frac{2}{p-1}}\leq|P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)}(r)|,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p17.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p17.2.1" class="ltx_text">the profile is nonvanishing. Smoothness follows from the equation. Also, <math id="S3.SS1.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{2\mu}Q^{\mathrm{out}}\to K^{1/(p-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>out</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{2\mu}Q^{\mathrm{out}}\to K^{1/(p-1)}</annotation></semantics></math> by the enclosure. Moreover, for <math id="S3.SS1.p17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math> the approximation <math id="S3.SS1.p17.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)}</annotation></semantics></math> agrees with <math id="S3.SS1.p17.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|C_{s}|r^{\beta}(1+c_{1}r^{-2}+c_{2}r^{-4})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|C_{s}|r^{\beta}(1+c_{1}r^{-2}+c_{2}r^{-4})</annotation></semantics></math>, the slow part in (<a href="#S2.E16" title="In 2.1. Linear exterior modes ‣ 2. Self-similar profile equation ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>), up to <math id="S3.SS1.p17.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="O(r^{-2/(p-1)-6})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(r^{-2/(p-1)-6})</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S3.SS1.p17.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{1}=\ell_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{1}=\ell_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.p17.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{2}=\ell_{2}+\ell_{1}^{2}/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{2}=\ell_{2}+\ell_{1}^{2}/2</annotation></semantics></math>. Both this difference and <math id="S3.SS1.p17.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> are <math id="S3.SS1.p17.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o(r^{-d+2/(p-1)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o(r^{-d+2/(p-1)})</annotation></semantics></math>. The definition of the nonlinear fast coefficient therefore gives <math id="S3.SS1.p17.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{f}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{f}=0</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p18" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p18.1" class="ltx_p">In this proposition the parameter <math id="S3.SS1.p18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{\mathrm{ext}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>ext</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{\mathrm{ext}}</annotation></semantics></math> measures the size of the correction. In the following argument, we will use two different choices of this parameter. The first one will be used to show uniqueness of the exterior solution, and the second choice will be used inside the computer-assisted argument.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p19" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p19.1" class="ltx_p">The exterior construction above is initially carried out at one finite order. To use the resulting profile in the later global estimates, we need a single exterior solution with an expansion to every algebraic order, rather than a different solution at each truncation order.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmthm5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_cor">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmthm5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 3.5</span></span><span id="S3.Thmthm5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmthm5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmthm5.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmthm5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The exterior solution constructed in
Proposition <a href="#S3.Thmthm4" title="Proposition 3.4. ‣ 3.1. Exterior solution at infinity ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a> satisfies,
for every integer <math id="S3.Thmthm5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S3.E34" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S3.E34X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_left">(34)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E34X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Q^{\mathrm{out}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>out</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q^{\mathrm{out}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E34X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)}+O(r^{-\frac{2}{p-1}-2J-2})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)}+O(r^{-\frac{2}{p-1}-2J-2}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E34Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E34Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(Q^{\mathrm{out}})^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>out</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(Q^{\mathrm{out}})^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E34Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)})^{\prime}+O(r^{-\frac{2}{p-1}-2J-3})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)})^{\prime}+O(r^{-\frac{2}{p-1}-2J-3}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.Thmthm5.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmthm5.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In particular, its algebraic asymptotic expansion contains only the slow mode.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS1.p20" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p20.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p20.1.1" class="ltx_text">Fix an order <math id="S3.SS1.p20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>. With <math id="S3.SS1.p20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi=2</annotation></semantics></math>, the residual constant in (<a href="#S3.E23" title="In Lemma 3.2. ‣ 3.1. Exterior solution at infinity ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a>) remains bounded as <math id="S3.SS1.p20.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\mathrm{out}}\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\mathrm{out}}\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, while <math id="S3.SS1.p20.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M,K^{2/(p-1)}/M\to K^{1/(p-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M,K^{2/(p-1)}/M\to K^{1/(p-1)}</annotation></semantics></math>. Set <math id="S3.SS1.p20.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{\mathrm{ext}}=2\mathfrak{C}_{\nu,r_{\mathrm{out}}}M\mathcal{B}/r_{\mathrm{out}}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>ext</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ℭ</mi><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{\mathrm{ext}}=2\mathfrak{C}_{\nu,r_{\mathrm{out}}}M\mathcal{B}/r_{\mathrm{out}}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. For sufficiently large <math id="S3.SS1.p20.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\mathrm{out}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\mathrm{out}}</annotation></semantics></math>, both <math id="S3.SS1.p20.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{\mathrm{ext}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>ext</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{\mathrm{ext}}</annotation></semantics></math> and the contraction constant tend to zero. Hence the three conditions in (<a href="#S3.E31" title="In Proposition 3.4. ‣ 3.1. Exterior solution at infinity ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">31</span></a>) hold. Thus, for each fixed <math id="S3.SS1.p20.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math>, Proposition <a href="#S3.Thmthm4" title="Proposition 3.4. ‣ 3.1. Exterior solution at infinity ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a> applies and gives an exact exterior solution</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex76" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex76.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)}=P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)}+O(r^{-\frac{2}{p-1}-2J-2}),\qquad r\geq R_{J}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>J</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)}=P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)}+O(r^{-\frac{2}{p-1}-2J-2}),\qquad r\geq R_{J}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p20.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p20.2.1" class="ltx_text">We now show that these constructions, that depend on <math id="S3.SS1.p20.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math>, define one solution. Let <math id="S3.SS1.p20.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J_{1})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J_{1})}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.p20.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J_{2})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J_{2})}</annotation></semantics></math> be two of them, and work on the common region <math id="S3.SS1.p20.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\geq R_{*}:=\max\{R_{J_{1}},R_{J_{2}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><msub><mi>J</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><msub><mi>J</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\geq R_{*}:=\max\{R_{J_{1}},R_{J_{2}}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S3.SS1.p20.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{1},J_{2}\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{1},J_{2}\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>, their difference <math id="S3.SS1.p20.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex77" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\Omega}w=N(Q_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J_{1})})-N(Q_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J_{2})})=:f,\qquad w=O(r^{-\frac{2}{p-1}-6}),\qquad f=O(r^{-\frac{2}{p-1}-8})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\Omega}w=N(Q_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J_{1})})-N(Q_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J_{2})})=:f,\qquad w=O(r^{-\frac{2}{p-1}-6}),\qquad f=O(r^{-\frac{2}{p-1}-8}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p20.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p20.3.1" class="ltx_text">Since both terms in <math id="S3.SS1.p20.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w-\mathcal{L}_{\Omega,\infty}^{-1}f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w-\mathcal{L}_{\Omega,\infty}^{-1}f</annotation></semantics></math> decay faster than the slow and fast modes, its coefficients in the fundamental system <math id="S3.SS1.p20.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{S_{\Omega},F_{\Omega}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{S_{\Omega},F_{\Omega}\}</annotation></semantics></math> vanish. Then this homogeneous solution is zero, and hence <math id="S3.SS1.p20.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w=\mathcal{L}_{\Omega,\infty}^{-1}f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w=\mathcal{L}_{\Omega,\infty}^{-1}f</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="S3.SS1.p20.m18" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="|Q_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J_{1})}|,|Q_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J_{2})}|\leq M_{*}r^{-2/(p-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>out</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo>,</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>out</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≤</mo><mi>M</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub><mi>r</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|Q_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J_{1})}|,|Q_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J_{2})}|\leq M_{*}r^{-2/(p-1)}</annotation></semantics></math>, then</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex78" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex78.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|f|\leq pM_{*}^{p-1}r^{-2}|w|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mo>∗</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|f|\leq pM_{*}^{p-1}r^{-2}|w|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p20.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p20.4.1" class="ltx_text">Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmthm3" title="Lemma 3.3. ‣ 3.1. Exterior solution at infinity ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a> consequently gives</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex79" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex79.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|w\|_{2/(p-1)+6,r_{\mathrm{out}}}\leq p\mathfrak{C}_{2/(p-1)+6,r_{\mathrm{out}}}M_{*}^{p-1}r_{\mathrm{out}}^{-2}\|w\|_{2/(p-1)+6,r_{\mathrm{out}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ℭ</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mo>∗</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|w\|_{2/(p-1)+6,r_{\mathrm{out}}}\leq p\mathfrak{C}_{2/(p-1)+6,r_{\mathrm{out}}}M_{*}^{p-1}r_{\mathrm{out}}^{-2}\|w\|_{2/(p-1)+6,r_{\mathrm{out}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p20.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p20.5.1" class="ltx_text">For sufficiently large <math id="S3.SS1.p20.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{*}</annotation></semantics></math> the coefficient is less than one, so <math id="S3.SS1.p20.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w=0</annotation></semantics></math> on the common exterior region. ODE uniqueness then extends this equality throughout the common interval of regularity. We denote the resulting common solution simply by <math id="S3.SS1.p20.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\mathrm{out}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>out</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\mathrm{out}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The solution certified at the computational <math id="S3.SS1.p20.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\mathrm{out}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\mathrm{out}}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the same tail bounds by (<a href="#S3.E32" title="In Proposition 3.4. ‣ 3.1. Exterior solution at infinity ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">32</span></a>), so this uniqueness argument identifies it with <math id="S3.SS1.p20.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\mathrm{out}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>out</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\mathrm{out}}</annotation></semantics></math>, first on a tail and then on <math id="S3.SS1.p20.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[r_{\mathrm{out}},\infty)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[r_{\mathrm{out}},\infty)</annotation></semantics></math> by ODE uniqueness.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p21" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p21.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p21.1.1" class="ltx_text">The estimate for <math id="S3.SS1.p21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)}</annotation></semantics></math> now applies to this common <math id="S3.SS1.p21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\mathrm{out}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>out</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\mathrm{out}}</annotation></semantics></math>, proving the first line of (<a href="#S3.E34" title="In Corollary 3.5. ‣ 3.1. Exterior solution at infinity ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">34</span></a>). Applying the derivative estimate in (<a href="#S3.E32" title="In Proposition 3.4. ‣ 3.1. Exterior solution at infinity ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">32</span></a>) at order <math id="S3.SS1.p21.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J+1</annotation></semantics></math>, and using <math id="S3.SS1.p21.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J+1)})^{\prime}-(P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)})^{\prime}=O(r^{-2/(p-1)-2J-3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>J</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J+1)})^{\prime}-(P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)})^{\prime}=O(r^{-2/(p-1)-2J-3})</annotation></semantics></math>, proves the second line. The case <math id="S3.SS1.p21.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J=1</annotation></semantics></math> follows by truncating the expansion at order two, for both the value and the derivative.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p22" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p22.1" class="ltx_p">The matching argument that will be used varies <math id="S3.SS1.p22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Omega,K)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Omega,K)</annotation></semantics></math> over the parameter cube <math id="S3.SS1.p22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>. It therefore requires <math id="S3.SS1.p22.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigl(Q^{\mathrm{out}}(r_{\mathrm{out}}),(Q^{\mathrm{out}})^{\prime}(r_{\mathrm{out}})\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>out</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>out</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl(Q^{\mathrm{out}}(r_{\mathrm{out}}),(Q^{\mathrm{out}})^{\prime}(r_{\mathrm{out}})\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math> to depend continuously on <math id="S3.SS1.p22.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Omega,K)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Omega,K)</annotation></semantics></math>. The three inequalities in the following corollary are the same as those in (<a href="#S3.E31" title="In Proposition 3.4. ‣ 3.1. Exterior solution at infinity ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">31</span></a>), except that they are now required to hold uniformly.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmthm6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_cor">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmthm6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 3.6</span></span><span id="S3.Thmthm6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmthm6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmthm6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmthm6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose there is a single <math id="S3.Thmthm6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{\mathrm{ext}}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>ext</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{\mathrm{ext}}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>
such that all three conditions (<a href="#S3.E31" title="In Proposition 3.4. ‣ 3.1. Exterior solution at infinity ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">31</span></a>)
hold with this same <math id="S3.Thmthm6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{\mathrm{ext}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>ext</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{\mathrm{ext}}</annotation></semantics></math> for every <math id="S3.Thmthm6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Omega,K)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Omega,K)</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying
<math id="S3.Thmthm6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\Omega-\Omega_{0}|\leq\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\Omega-\Omega_{0}|\leq\rho</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.Thmthm6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|K-K_{0}|\leq\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|K-K_{0}|\leq\rho</annotation></semantics></math>,
with <math id="S3.Thmthm6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> as in (<a href="#S3.E17" title="In 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmthm6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmthm6.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmthm6.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then the map</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex80" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex80.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Omega,K)\longmapsto\bigl(Q^{\mathrm{out}}(r_{\mathrm{out}}),(Q^{\mathrm{out}})^{\prime}(r_{\mathrm{out}})\bigr)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟼</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>out</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>out</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Omega,K)\longmapsto\bigl(Q^{\mathrm{out}}(r_{\mathrm{out}}),(Q^{\mathrm{out}})^{\prime}(r_{\mathrm{out}})\bigr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.Thmthm6.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmthm6.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">is continuous.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.6" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS1.p23" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p23.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p23.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S3.SS1.p23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Omega_{n},K_{n})\to(\Omega,K)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Omega_{n},K_{n})\to(\Omega,K)</annotation></semantics></math> in the parameter rectangle above, and denote the corresponding exterior solutions by <math id="S3.SS1.p23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{n}^{\mathrm{out}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>out</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{n}^{\mathrm{out}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The coefficients of <math id="S3.SS1.p23.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)}</annotation></semantics></math> depend continuously on <math id="S3.SS1.p23.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Omega,K)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Omega,K)</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus (<a href="#S3.E32" title="In Proposition 3.4. ‣ 3.1. Exterior solution at infinity ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">32</span></a>) bounds <math id="S3.SS1.p23.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{n}^{\mathrm{out}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>out</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{n}^{\mathrm{out}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.p23.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Q_{n}^{\mathrm{out}})^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>out</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Q_{n}^{\mathrm{out}})^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> uniformly on every compact interval of <math id="S3.SS1.p23.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[r_{\mathrm{out}},\infty)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[r_{\mathrm{out}},\infty)</annotation></semantics></math>, and the profile equation also bounds <math id="S3.SS1.p23.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Q_{n}^{\mathrm{out}})^{\prime\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>out</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>′′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Q_{n}^{\mathrm{out}})^{\prime\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. By Arzelà–Ascoli and a diagonal extraction, every subsequence has a further subsequence converging in <math id="S3.SS1.p23.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{1}_{\mathrm{loc}}([r_{\mathrm{out}},\infty))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>loc</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{1}_{\mathrm{loc}}([r_{\mathrm{out}},\infty))</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p24" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p24.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p24.1.1" class="ltx_text">Any such limit solves the profile equation at <math id="S3.SS1.p24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Omega,K)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Omega,K)</annotation></semantics></math> and inherits the enclosure (<a href="#S3.E32" title="In Proposition 3.4. ‣ 3.1. Exterior solution at infinity ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">32</span></a>), by passing to the limit at each <math id="S3.SS1.p24.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\geq r_{\mathrm{out}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\geq r_{\mathrm{out}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Its difference from <math id="S3.SS1.p24.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\mathrm{out}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>out</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\mathrm{out}}</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="S3.SS1.p24.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Omega,K)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Omega,K)</annotation></semantics></math> is therefore <math id="S3.SS1.p24.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="O(r^{-2/(p-1)-2J-2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>J</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(r^{-2/(p-1)-2J-2})</annotation></semantics></math>, hence <math id="S3.SS1.p24.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="O(r^{-2/(p-1)-6})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(r^{-2/(p-1)-6})</annotation></semantics></math> because <math id="S3.SS1.p24.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>. The uniqueness argument in Corollary <a href="#S3.Thmthm5" title="Corollary 3.5. ‣ 3.1. Exterior solution at infinity ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.5</span></a> identifies the two solutions on a sufficiently distant tail, and ODE uniqueness extends their equality to <math id="S3.SS1.p24.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[r_{\mathrm{out}},\infty)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[r_{\mathrm{out}},\infty)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p25" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p25.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p25.1.1" class="ltx_text">Consequently the entire sequence converges to <math id="S3.SS1.p25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\mathrm{out}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>out</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\mathrm{out}}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S3.SS1.p25.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{1}_{\mathrm{loc}}([r_{\mathrm{out}},\infty))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>loc</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{1}_{\mathrm{loc}}([r_{\mathrm{out}},\infty))</annotation></semantics></math>. Evaluation at <math id="S3.SS1.p25.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\mathrm{out}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\mathrm{out}}</annotation></semantics></math> proves the claimed continuity.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.2. </span>Interior solution at the origin</h3>

<div id="S3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We next construct and enclose the profile starting from its data at the origin. First, an even Taylor polynomial is chosen so that the low orders of the profile equation vanish, leaving an explicitly computable finite residual. We then use the integral formula with zero initial data to correct this polynomial to the exact solution <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\mathrm{in}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>in</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\mathrm{in}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The resulting value and derivative bounds at <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=r_{\mathrm{in}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>in</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=r_{\mathrm{in}}</annotation></semantics></math> provide the initial data needed to propagate the inner solution to the matching radius.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Fix <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\mathrm{in}}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>in</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\mathrm{in}}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and an integer <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>. Define the inner Taylor polynomial, truncated at order <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I</annotation></semantics></math>, by</p>
<table id="S3.Ex81" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex81.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\mathrm{in}}^{(I)}(r)=\sum_{n=0}^{I}c_{n}r^{2n},\qquad c_{0}=A," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>in</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>I</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\mathrm{in}}^{(I)}(r)=\sum_{n=0}^{I}c_{n}r^{2n},\qquad c_{0}=A,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">where the coefficients are determined by the recurrence</p>
<table id="S3.E35" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S3.E35X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_left">(35)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E35X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 2(n+1)(2n+d)c_{n+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 2(n+1)(2n+d)c_{n+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E35X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=[z^{n}]\bigl(C_{n}(z)^{\frac{p+1}{2}}\overline{C}_{n}(z)^{\,\frac{p-1}{2}}\bigr)-\left(\Omega+i\left(\frac{1}{p-1}+n\right)\right)c_{n}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=[z^{n}]\bigl(C_{n}(z)^{\frac{p+1}{2}}\overline{C}_{n}(z)^{\,\frac{p-1}{2}}\bigr)-\left(\Omega+i\left(\frac{1}{p-1}+n\right)\right)c_{n},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E35Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E35Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle C_{n}(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle C_{n}(z)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E35Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{j=0}^{n}c_{j}z^{j}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{j=0}^{n}c_{j}z^{j}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.4" class="ltx_p">The recurrence is used for <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq n&lt;I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq n&lt;I</annotation></semantics></math>. Here <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[z^{n}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[z^{n}]</annotation></semantics></math> denotes coefficient extraction, and the bar conjugates coefficients. The residual <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{in}}=L_{\Omega}P_{\mathrm{in}}^{(I)}-N(P_{\mathrm{in}}^{(I)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>in</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>in</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>in</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{in}}=L_{\Omega}P_{\mathrm{in}}^{(I)}-N(P_{\mathrm{in}}^{(I)})</annotation></semantics></math> is a polynomial in <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Its coefficients below degree <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I</annotation></semantics></math> vanish identically. We denote its coefficients by <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, so that</p>
<table id="S3.E36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(36)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{in}}(r)=\sum_{n=I}^{pI}d_{n}r^{2n}\quad\text{and}\quad\|\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{in}}\|_{L^{\infty}(0,r_{\mathrm{in}})}\leq H_{0}:=\sum_{n=I}^{pI}|d_{n}|r_{\mathrm{in}}^{2n}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>in</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>in</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>in</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></munderover><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>in</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{in}}(r)=\sum_{n=I}^{pI}d_{n}r^{2n}\quad\text{and}\quad\|\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{in}}\|_{L^{\infty}(0,r_{\mathrm{in}})}\leq H_{0}:=\sum_{n=I}^{pI}|d_{n}|r_{\mathrm{in}}^{2n}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">A direct contraction converts this finite residual bound into a bound for the actual origin solution. Explicit constants are needed in our computer-assisted argument. In the following lemma we set <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{0}=\left|\Omega+\frac{i}{p-1}\right|+p(1/2)^{p-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{0}=\left|\Omega+\frac{i}{p-1}\right|+p(1/2)^{p-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, which will be used as a Lipschitz bound for the full right-hand side in a neighborhood of the origin. We will close a fixed point argument in the ball of radius</p>
<table id="S3.Ex82" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex82.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{\mathrm{in}}=\frac{2r_{\mathrm{in}}^{2}H_{0}}{2d-r_{\mathrm{in}}^{2}L_{0}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>in</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>in</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>in</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{\mathrm{in}}=\frac{2r_{\mathrm{in}}^{2}H_{0}}{2d-r_{\mathrm{in}}^{2}L_{0}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmthm7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmthm7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3.7</span></span><span id="S3.Thmthm7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmthm7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmthm7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmthm7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that <math id="S3.Thmthm7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|A|\leq 1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|A|\leq 1/2</annotation></semantics></math> and set <math id="S3.Thmthm7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\mathrm{in}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>in</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\mathrm{in}}</annotation></semantics></math> small enough so that</span></p>
<table id="S3.E37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(37)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{r_{\mathrm{in}}^{2}L_{0}}{2d}&lt;1,\qquad\sup_{[0,r_{\mathrm{in}}]}|P_{\mathrm{in}}^{(I)}|+\delta_{\mathrm{in}}&lt;\frac{1}{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>in</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="1.889em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>in</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>in</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>in</mi></msub></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{r_{\mathrm{in}}^{2}L_{0}}{2d}&lt;1,\qquad\sup_{[0,r_{\mathrm{in}}]}|P_{\mathrm{in}}^{(I)}|+\delta_{\mathrm{in}}&lt;\frac{1}{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.Thmthm7.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmthm7.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">then there is an exact solution <math id="S3.Thmthm7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\mathrm{in}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>in</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\mathrm{in}}</annotation></semantics></math> of (<a href="#S2.E8" title="In 2. Self-similar profile equation ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>) with <math id="S3.Thmthm7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\mathrm{in}}(0)=A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>in</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\mathrm{in}}(0)=A</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.Thmthm7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Q^{\mathrm{in}})^{\prime}(0)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>in</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Q^{\mathrm{in}})^{\prime}(0)=0</annotation></semantics></math>, and</span></p>
<table id="S3.E38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(38)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|Q^{\mathrm{in}}(r_{\mathrm{in}})-P_{\mathrm{in}}^{(I)}(r_{\mathrm{in}})|\leq\delta_{\mathrm{in}},\qquad|(Q^{\mathrm{in}})^{\prime}(r_{\mathrm{in}})-(P_{\mathrm{in}}^{(I)})^{\prime}(r_{\mathrm{in}})|\leq\frac{r_{\mathrm{in}}}{d}(H_{0}+L_{0}\delta_{\mathrm{in}})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>in</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>in</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>in</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>in</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>in</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>in</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>in</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>in</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>in</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>in</mi></msub><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>in</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|Q^{\mathrm{in}}(r_{\mathrm{in}})-P_{\mathrm{in}}^{(I)}(r_{\mathrm{in}})|\leq\delta_{\mathrm{in}},\qquad|(Q^{\mathrm{in}})^{\prime}(r_{\mathrm{in}})-(P_{\mathrm{in}}^{(I)})^{\prime}(r_{\mathrm{in}})|\leq\frac{r_{\mathrm{in}}}{d}(H_{0}+L_{0}\delta_{\mathrm{in}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">The inverse with zero data <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(0)=h^{\prime}(0)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(0)=h^{\prime}(0)=0</annotation></semantics></math> of the ODE <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{\prime\prime}+((d-1)/r+ir/2)h^{\prime}=f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{\prime\prime}+((d-1)/r+ir/2)h^{\prime}=f</annotation></semantics></math> is</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex83" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex83.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(T_{0}f)(r)=\int_{0}^{r}t^{1-d}e^{-\frac{it^{2}}{4}}\int_{0}^{t}\sigma^{d-1}e^{\frac{i\sigma^{2}}{4}}f(\sigma)\,d\sigma\,dt." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(T_{0}f)(r)=\int_{0}^{r}t^{1-d}e^{-\frac{it^{2}}{4}}\int_{0}^{t}\sigma^{d-1}e^{\frac{i\sigma^{2}}{4}}f(\sigma)\,d\sigma\,dt.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">It satisfies</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex84" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex84.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|(T_{0}f)^{\prime}(r_{\mathrm{in}})|\leq\frac{r_{\mathrm{in}}}{d}\|f\|_{\infty}\qquad\text{ so }\qquad\|T_{0}f\|_{\infty}\leq\frac{r_{\mathrm{in}}^{2}}{2d}\|f\|_{\infty}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>in</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>in</mi></msub><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mtext> so </mtext><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>in</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|(T_{0}f)^{\prime}(r_{\mathrm{in}})|\leq\frac{r_{\mathrm{in}}}{d}\|f\|_{\infty}\qquad\text{ so }\qquad\|T_{0}f\|_{\infty}\leq\frac{r_{\mathrm{in}}^{2}}{2d}\|f\|_{\infty}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">The definition of <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{\mathrm{in}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>in</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{\mathrm{in}}</annotation></semantics></math> and the first inequality in (<a href="#S3.E37" title="In Lemma 3.7. ‣ 3.2. Interior solution at the origin ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">37</span></a>) give</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex85" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex85.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{r_{\mathrm{in}}^{2}H_{0}}{2d}+\frac{r_{\mathrm{in}}^{2}L_{0}}{2d}\delta_{\mathrm{in}}\leq\delta_{\mathrm{in}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>in</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>in</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>in</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>in</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{r_{\mathrm{in}}^{2}H_{0}}{2d}+\frac{r_{\mathrm{in}}^{2}L_{0}}{2d}\delta_{\mathrm{in}}\leq\delta_{\mathrm{in}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">Hence the map</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex86" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex86.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\longmapsto T_{0}\{N(P_{\mathrm{in}}^{(I)}+h)-N(P_{\mathrm{in}}^{(I)})-\left(\Omega+\frac{i}{p-1}\right)h-\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{in}}\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>in</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>in</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>in</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\longmapsto T_{0}\{N(P_{\mathrm{in}}^{(I)}+h)-N(P_{\mathrm{in}}^{(I)})-\left(\Omega+\frac{i}{p-1}\right)h-\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{in}}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p4.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p4.5.1" class="ltx_text">contracts on <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|h\|_{\infty}\leq\delta_{\mathrm{in}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>in</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|h\|_{\infty}\leq\delta_{\mathrm{in}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Its fixed point gives the regular-origin solution from (<a href="#S2.E10" title="In Proof. ‣ 2. Self-similar profile equation ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>), by uniqueness, and the bounds for <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> give (<a href="#S3.E38" title="In Lemma 3.7. ‣ 3.2. Interior solution at the origin ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">38</span></a>). The same uniqueness identifies the constructed function with the smooth profile.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.3. </span>Matching the inner and outer solutions</h3>

<div id="S3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This subsection sets up the computer-assisted matching argument by comparing the exact inner and outer solutions selected at the origin and at infinity. We define the corresponding matching maps and state the criterion that will transfer rigorous finite computations to the exact problem.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For the computer-assisted argument, we set the parameters <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\mathrm{in}},r_{\mathrm{m}},r_{\mathrm{out}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>in</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\mathrm{in}},r_{\mathrm{m}},r_{\mathrm{out}}</annotation></semantics></math>, which represent an inner, matching and outer radius respectively. We use <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I,J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I,J</annotation></semantics></math> for truncation orders of Taylor polynomials and exterior expansions respectively. These parameters are fixed in the code. Recall the parameter cube is defined by (<a href="#S3.E17" title="In 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For each <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vartheta=(A,\Omega,K)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϑ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vartheta=(A,\Omega,K)</annotation></semantics></math>, we compare two solutions on each shooting interval. The solutions <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\mathrm{in}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>in</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\mathrm{in}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\mathrm{out}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>out</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\mathrm{out}}</annotation></semantics></math> are selected by the desired exact boundary conditions <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\mathrm{in}}(0)=A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>in</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\mathrm{in}}(0)=A</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Q^{\mathrm{in}})^{\prime}(0)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>in</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Q^{\mathrm{in}})^{\prime}(0)=0</annotation></semantics></math>, while <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\mathrm{out}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>out</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\mathrm{out}}</annotation></semantics></math> has <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{f}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{f}=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{s}=K^{1/(p-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{s}=K^{1/(p-1)}</annotation></semantics></math>. Meanwhile <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{Q}^{\mathrm{in}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>in</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{Q}^{\mathrm{in}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{Q}^{\mathrm{out}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>out</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{Q}^{\mathrm{out}}</annotation></semantics></math> instead start from computable data. Specifically,</p>
<table id="S3.Ex87" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex87.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\widetilde{Q}^{\mathrm{in}},(\widetilde{Q}^{\mathrm{in}})^{\prime})(r_{\mathrm{in}})=(P_{\mathrm{in}}^{(I)},(P_{\mathrm{in}}^{(I)})^{\prime})(r_{\mathrm{in}}),\qquad(\widetilde{Q}^{\mathrm{out}},(\widetilde{Q}^{\mathrm{out}})^{\prime})(r_{\mathrm{out}})=(P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)},(P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)})^{\prime})(r_{\mathrm{out}})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>in</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>in</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>in</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>in</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>in</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>in</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>out</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>out</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\widetilde{Q}^{\mathrm{in}},(\widetilde{Q}^{\mathrm{in}})^{\prime})(r_{\mathrm{in}})=(P_{\mathrm{in}}^{(I)},(P_{\mathrm{in}}^{(I)})^{\prime})(r_{\mathrm{in}}),\qquad(\widetilde{Q}^{\mathrm{out}},(\widetilde{Q}^{\mathrm{out}})^{\prime})(r_{\mathrm{out}})=(P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)},(P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)})^{\prime})(r_{\mathrm{out}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">All four functions solve the same profile ODE. The computable solutions <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{Q}^{\mathrm{in}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>in</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{Q}^{\mathrm{in}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{Q}^{\mathrm{out}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>out</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{Q}^{\mathrm{out}}</annotation></semantics></math> are the ones that we consider in the computer-assisted argument while the true solutions <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\mathrm{in}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>in</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\mathrm{in}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\mathrm{out}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>out</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\mathrm{out}}</annotation></semantics></math> are not explicit, as they exist only by the fixed point arguments above. We bound their difference using estimates from the contraction arguments.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma\in\{\mathrm{in},\mathrm{out}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>in</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>out</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma\in\{\mathrm{in},\mathrm{out}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, define the exact and finite-data profile state vectors</p>
<table id="S3.Ex88" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex88.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Q}_{\vartheta}^{\sigma}(r):=\begin{pmatrix}Q_{\vartheta}^{\sigma}(r)\\
(Q_{\vartheta}^{\sigma})^{\prime}(r)\end{pmatrix},\qquad\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta}^{\sigma}(r):=\begin{pmatrix}\widetilde{Q}_{\vartheta}^{\sigma}(r)\\
(\widetilde{Q}_{\vartheta}^{\sigma})^{\prime}(r)\end{pmatrix}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐐</mi><mi>ϑ</mi><mi>σ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>ϑ</mi><mi>σ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>ϑ</mi><mi>σ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>ϑ</mi><mi>σ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>ϑ</mi><mi>σ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>ϑ</mi><mi>σ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Q}_{\vartheta}^{\sigma}(r):=\begin{pmatrix}Q_{\vartheta}^{\sigma}(r)\\
(Q_{\vartheta}^{\sigma})^{\prime}(r)\end{pmatrix},\qquad\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta}^{\sigma}(r):=\begin{pmatrix}\widetilde{Q}_{\vartheta}^{\sigma}(r)\\
(\widetilde{Q}_{\vartheta}^{\sigma})^{\prime}(r)\end{pmatrix}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Where these solutions exist and are nonzero, set</p>
<table id="S3.Ex89" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex89.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}\begin{pmatrix}q\\
v\end{pmatrix}:=\begin{pmatrix}\log|q|\\
r_{\mathrm{m}}\operatorname{Re}(v/q)\\
r_{\mathrm{m}}\operatorname{Im}(v/q)\end{pmatrix}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mi>q</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>v</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}\begin{pmatrix}q\\
v\end{pmatrix}:=\begin{pmatrix}\log|q|\\
r_{\mathrm{m}}\operatorname{Re}(v/q)\\
r_{\mathrm{m}}\operatorname{Im}(v/q)\end{pmatrix},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p4.3" class="ltx_p">and define for <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vartheta=(A,\Omega,K)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϑ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vartheta=(A,\Omega,K)</annotation></semantics></math> the matching maps</p>
<table id="S3.E39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(39)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{aligned} \mathcal{M}(\vartheta)&amp;:=\mathcal{H}(\mathbf{Q}_{\vartheta}^{\mathrm{in}})-\mathcal{H}(\mathbf{Q}_{\vartheta}^{\mathrm{out}}),\\
\widetilde{\mathcal{M}}(\vartheta)&amp;:=\mathcal{H}(\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta}^{\mathrm{in}})-\mathcal{H}(\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta}^{\mathrm{out}}),\end{aligned}\qquad\text{at }r=r_{\mathrm{m}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϑ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐐</mi><mi>ϑ</mi><mi>in</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐐</mi><mi>ϑ</mi><mi>out</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϑ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>ϑ</mi><mi>in</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>ϑ</mi><mi>out</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mtext>at </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{aligned} \mathcal{M}(\vartheta)&amp;:=\mathcal{H}(\mathbf{Q}_{\vartheta}^{\mathrm{in}})-\mathcal{H}(\mathbf{Q}_{\vartheta}^{\mathrm{out}}),\\
\widetilde{\mathcal{M}}(\vartheta)&amp;:=\mathcal{H}(\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta}^{\mathrm{in}})-\mathcal{H}(\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta}^{\mathrm{out}}),\end{aligned}\qquad\text{at }r=r_{\mathrm{m}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p4.4" class="ltx_p">These maps measure the mismatch between the inner and outer solutions at the matching radius <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\mathrm{m}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\mathrm{m}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Logarithmic coordinates are chosen so that the difference is a ratio as opposed to an absolute difference. The factor <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\mathrm{m}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\mathrm{m}}</annotation></semantics></math> makes <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\mathrm{m}}v/q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\mathrm{m}}v/q</annotation></semantics></math> the derivative of <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log q</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log r</annotation></semantics></math>, whose real and imaginary parts are on a dimensionless scale. A zero of the exact map <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math> is precisely the condition needed to join the two solutions, while the finite map <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the computable object whose value and derivative are used in the computer-assisted existence argument.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The map <math id="S3.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math> is continuous by Lemma <a href="#S2.Thmthm1" title="Lemma 2.1. ‣ 2. Self-similar profile equation ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a> and Corollary <a href="#S3.Thmthm6" title="Corollary 3.6. ‣ 3.1. Exterior solution at infinity ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.6</span></a>, together with existence and nonvanishing on both shooting intervals from Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmthm10" title="Lemma 3.10 (Computer-assisted bounds). ‣ 3.4. Computer-assisted proof of the matching conditions ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.10</span></a>. The initial data <math id="S3.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\mathrm{in}}^{(I)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>in</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\mathrm{in}}^{(I)}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)}</annotation></semantics></math> depend real analytically on the parameters. By <math id="S3.SS3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> dependence of the ODE flow on initial data and parameters, and smoothness of <math id="S3.SS3.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S3.SS3.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, the map <math id="S3.SS3.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S3.SS3.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> on its domain of regularity. Its derivative is computed using</p>
<table id="S3.E40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(40)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D\mathcal{H}\begin{pmatrix}q\\
v\end{pmatrix}\begin{pmatrix}u\\
w\end{pmatrix}=\begin{pmatrix}\operatorname{Re}(u/q)\\
r_{\mathrm{m}}\operatorname{Re}(w/q-vu/q^{2})\\
r_{\mathrm{m}}\operatorname{Im}(w/q-vu/q^{2})\end{pmatrix}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mi>q</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>v</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mi>u</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>w</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D\mathcal{H}\begin{pmatrix}q\\
v\end{pmatrix}\begin{pmatrix}u\\
w\end{pmatrix}=\begin{pmatrix}\operatorname{Re}(u/q)\\
r_{\mathrm{m}}\operatorname{Re}(w/q-vu/q^{2})\\
r_{\mathrm{m}}\operatorname{Im}(w/q-vu/q^{2})\end{pmatrix}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="S3.SS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}(\vartheta)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϑ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}(\vartheta)=0</annotation></semantics></math>, a constant unit phase makes the inner and outer Cauchy data agree at <math id="S3.SS3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\mathrm{m}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\mathrm{m}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then ODE uniqueness joins them into the desired global profile without changing <math id="S3.SS3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{f}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{f}=0</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="S3.SS3.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|C_{s}|=K^{1/(p-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|C_{s}|=K^{1/(p-1)}</annotation></semantics></math>. The next proposition establishes a criterion for the existence of such a zero.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmthm8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_prop">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmthm8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 3.8</span></span><span id="S3.Thmthm8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmthm8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmthm8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmthm8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose <math id="S3.Thmthm8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.Thmthm8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math> are defined on <math id="S3.Thmthm8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>,
with the regularity stated above and radius <math id="S3.Thmthm8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> as in
(<a href="#S3.E17" title="In 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>). Let <math id="S3.Thmthm8.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> be an invertible real
<math id="S3.Thmthm8.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3\times 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3\times 3</annotation></semantics></math> matrix. If</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex90" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex90X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex90X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|B\widetilde{\mathcal{M}}(\vartheta_{0})\|_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϑ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|B\widetilde{\mathcal{M}}(\vartheta_{0})\|_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex90X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq Y," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq Y,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex90Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex90Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sup_{D}\|B(\mathcal{M}-\widetilde{\mathcal{M}})\|_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mi>D</mi></munder><msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sup_{D}\|B(\mathcal{M}-\widetilde{\mathcal{M}})\|_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex90Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq E," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq E,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex90Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex90Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sup_{D}\|I-BD\widetilde{\mathcal{M}}\|_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mi>D</mi></munder><msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sup_{D}\|I-BD\widetilde{\mathcal{M}}\|_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex90Xb.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq Z,\qquad Y+E+Z\rho&lt;\rho," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>Z</mi><mi>ρ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq Z,\qquad Y+E+Z\rho&lt;\rho,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.Thmthm8.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmthm8.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">then <math id="S3.Thmthm8.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math> has a zero in <math id="S3.Thmthm8.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>. The matrix norm is the operator norm induced by the vector infinity norm.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">The continuous map <math id="S3.SS3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T(\vartheta)=\vartheta-B\mathcal{M}(\vartheta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϑ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ϑ</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϑ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(\vartheta)=\vartheta-B\mathcal{M}(\vartheta)</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex91" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex91X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex91X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|T(\vartheta)-\vartheta_{0}\|_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϑ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ϑ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|T(\vartheta)-\vartheta_{0}\|_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex91X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\|B\widetilde{\mathcal{M}}(\vartheta_{0})\|_{\infty}+Z\|\vartheta-\vartheta_{0}\|_{\infty}+\|B(\mathcal{M}-\widetilde{\mathcal{M}})(\vartheta)\|_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϑ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>ϑ</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ϑ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϑ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\|B\widetilde{\mathcal{M}}(\vartheta_{0})\|_{\infty}+Z\|\vartheta-\vartheta_{0}\|_{\infty}+\|B(\mathcal{M}-\widetilde{\mathcal{M}})(\vartheta)\|_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex91Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex91Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq Y+Z\rho+E&lt;\rho." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq Y+Z\rho+E&lt;\rho.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">The middle term follows from convexity of <math id="S3.SS3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> and</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex92" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex92X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex92X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bigl\|\vartheta-\vartheta_{0}-B\bigl(\widetilde{\mathcal{M}}(\vartheta)-\widetilde{\mathcal{M}}(\vartheta_{0})\bigr)\bigr\|_{\infty}=\left\|\int_{0}^{1}\bigl[I-BD\widetilde{\mathcal{M}}(\vartheta_{0}+t(\vartheta-\vartheta_{0}))\bigr](\vartheta-\vartheta_{0})\,dt\right\|_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mi>ϑ</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ϑ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϑ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϑ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϑ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϑ</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ϑ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϑ</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ϑ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0em">d</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bigl\|\vartheta-\vartheta_{0}-B\bigl(\widetilde{\mathcal{M}}(\vartheta)-\widetilde{\mathcal{M}}(\vartheta_{0})\bigr)\bigr\|_{\infty}=\left\|\int_{0}^{1}\bigl[I-BD\widetilde{\mathcal{M}}(\vartheta_{0}+t(\vartheta-\vartheta_{0}))\bigr](\vartheta-\vartheta_{0})\,dt\right\|_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex92Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex92Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq Z\|\vartheta-\vartheta_{0}\|_{\infty}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="1.278em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>ϑ</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ϑ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq Z\|\vartheta-\vartheta_{0}\|_{\infty}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">Thus <math id="S3.SS3.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> maps the compact convex cube <math id="S3.SS3.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> into itself. Brouwer’s fixed-point theorem gives a fixed point, and invertibility of <math id="S3.SS3.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> makes it a zero of <math id="S3.SS3.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.4. </span>Computer-assisted proof of the matching conditions</h3>

<div id="S3.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We check the inner shooting from <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\mathrm{in}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>in</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\mathrm{in}}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\mathrm{m}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\mathrm{m}}</annotation></semantics></math> and the outer shooting from <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\mathrm{out}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\mathrm{out}}</annotation></semantics></math> back to <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\mathrm{m}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\mathrm{m}}</annotation></semantics></math> by the same stepwise estimates. On each mesh step, we have four polynomials that approximate the solution and its three derivatives with respect to <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A,\Omega,K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A,\Omega,K</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Because <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined by the finite shooting solutions at <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\mathrm{m}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\mathrm{m}}</annotation></semantics></math>, its value and derivative are bounded by propagating the Cauchy data through the profile equation. The profile ODE can be written as a first-order system for <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(q,v)=(Q,Q^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(q,v)=(Q,Q^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> using the vector field</p>
<table id="S3.E41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(41)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\Omega}\left(r,\begin{pmatrix}q\\
v\end{pmatrix}\right)=\begin{pmatrix}v\\
N(q)-\left(\Omega+\frac{i}{p-1}\right)q-\left(\frac{d-1}{r}+\frac{ir}{2}\right)v\end{pmatrix}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mi>q</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>v</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mi>v</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>r</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\Omega}\left(r,\begin{pmatrix}q\\
v\end{pmatrix}\right)=\begin{pmatrix}v\\
N(q)-\left(\Omega+\frac{i}{p-1}\right)q-\left(\frac{d-1}{r}+\frac{ir}{2}\right)v\end{pmatrix}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">We write <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Df_{\Omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Df_{\Omega}</annotation></semantics></math> for the derivative with respect to <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(q,v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(q,v)</annotation></semantics></math>. On either mesh, we suppress the label <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma\in\left\{\mathrm{in},\mathrm{out}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi>in</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>out</mi></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma\in\left\{\mathrm{in},\mathrm{out}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Q}_{\vartheta}^{\sigma}=(Q_{\vartheta}^{\sigma},(Q_{\vartheta}^{\sigma})^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐐</mi><mi>ϑ</mi><mi>σ</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>ϑ</mi><mi>σ</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>ϑ</mi><mi>σ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Q}_{\vartheta}^{\sigma}=(Q_{\vartheta}^{\sigma},(Q_{\vartheta}^{\sigma})^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta}^{\sigma}=(\widetilde{Q}_{\vartheta}^{\sigma},(\widetilde{Q}_{\vartheta}^{\sigma})^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>ϑ</mi><mi>σ</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>ϑ</mi><mi>σ</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>ϑ</mi><mi>σ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta}^{\sigma}=(\widetilde{Q}_{\vartheta}^{\sigma},(\widetilde{Q}_{\vartheta}^{\sigma})^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>. The exact and finite-data solutions satisfy</p>
<table id="S3.Ex93" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex93.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbf{Q}_{\vartheta})^{\prime}=f_{\Omega}(r,\mathbf{Q}_{\vartheta}),\qquad(\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta})^{\prime}=f_{\Omega}(r,\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mi>ϑ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mi>ϑ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>ϑ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>ϑ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbf{Q}_{\vartheta})^{\prime}=f_{\Omega}(r,\mathbf{Q}_{\vartheta}),\qquad(\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta})^{\prime}=f_{\Omega}(r,\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">To bound <math id="S3.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D\widetilde{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D\widetilde{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math>, differentiate <math id="S3.SS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>ϑ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta}</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to its three real parameters. This gives the three variational equations</p>
<table id="S3.Ex94" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex94X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex94X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(\partial_{A}\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta})^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>A</mi></msub><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>ϑ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(\partial_{A}\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta})^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex94X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=Df_{\Omega}(r,\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta})\partial_{A}\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>ϑ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>A</mi></msub><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>ϑ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=Df_{\Omega}(r,\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta})\partial_{A}\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex94Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex94Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(\partial_{\Omega}\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta})^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>ϑ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(\partial_{\Omega}\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta})^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex94Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=Df_{\Omega}(r,\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta})\partial_{\Omega}\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta}-\begin{pmatrix}0\\
(\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta})_{1}\end{pmatrix}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>ϑ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>ϑ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>ϑ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=Df_{\Omega}(r,\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta})\partial_{\Omega}\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta}-\begin{pmatrix}0\\
(\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta})_{1}\end{pmatrix},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex94Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex94Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(\partial_{K}\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta})^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>K</mi></msub><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>ϑ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(\partial_{K}\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta})^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex94Xb.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=Df_{\Omega}(r,\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta})\partial_{K}\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>ϑ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>K</mi></msub><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>ϑ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=Df_{\Omega}(r,\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta})\partial_{K}\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Finally, the propagation estimates require bounds on the Jacobian and its variation. We use the Euclidean norms on <math id="S3.SS4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℂ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{C}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{C}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{C}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, viewed as real vector spaces, and their induced operator norms for derivatives. Direct differentiation of <math id="S3.SS4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{(p+1)/2}\overline{q}^{\,(p-1)/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{(p+1)/2}\overline{q}^{\,(p-1)/2}</annotation></semantics></math> gives</p>
<table id="S3.Ex95" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex95.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{gathered}DN(q)u=\frac{p+1}{2}|q|^{p-1}u+\frac{p-1}{2}q^{2}|q|^{p-3}\overline{u},\\
\|DN(q)\|\leq p|q|^{p-1},\qquad\|D^{2}N(q)\|\leq p(p-1)|q|^{p-2}.\end{gathered}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>D</mi><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0.0835em">≤</mo><mi>p</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>q</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo rspace="3.889em">,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>D</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0.0835em">≤</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>q</mi><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{gathered}DN(q)u=\frac{p+1}{2}|q|^{p-1}u+\frac{p-1}{2}q^{2}|q|^{p-3}\overline{u},\\
\|DN(q)\|\leq p|q|^{p-1},\qquad\|D^{2}N(q)\|\leq p(p-1)|q|^{p-2}.\end{gathered}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p4.2" class="ltx_p">We now explain how to propagate solutions and bound the error along a mesh step. Consider a mesh step <math id="S3.SS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(u)=r_{*}+hu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(u)=r_{*}+hu</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq u\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq u\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S3.SS4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math> may have either sign, and set <math id="S3.SS4.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\min}=\min\{r_{*},r_{*}+h\}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\min}=\min\{r_{*},r_{*}+h\}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S3.SS4.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(u)</annotation></semantics></math> approximate <math id="S3.SS4.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta_{0}}(r(u))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mi>ϑ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta_{0}}(r(u))</annotation></semantics></math>, and write <math id="S3.SS4.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{q}</annotation></semantics></math> for its first component. For each parameter label <math id="S3.SS4.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi\in\{A,\Omega,K\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi\in\{A,\Omega,K\}</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S3.SS4.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\xi}(u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\xi}(u)</annotation></semantics></math> approximate <math id="S3.SS4.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left.\partial_{\xi}\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta}(r(u))\right|_{\vartheta=\vartheta_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>ξ</mi></msub><msub><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>ϑ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>ϑ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ϑ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left.\partial_{\xi}\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta}(r(u))\right|_{\vartheta=\vartheta_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Primes on these polynomials denote differentiation with respect to <math id="S3.SS4.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math>. Their integrated residuals satisfy</p>
<table id="S3.E42" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S3.E42X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="4" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_left">(42)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E42X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\int_{0}^{1}\bigl\|P^{\prime}-hf_{\Omega_{0}}(r(u),P)\bigr\|\,du" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int_{0}^{1}\bigl\|P^{\prime}-hf_{\Omega_{0}}(r(u),P)\bigr\|\,du</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E42X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\delta_{0}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\delta_{0},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E42Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E42Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\int_{0}^{1}\bigl\|P_{A}^{\prime}-hDf_{\Omega_{0}}(r(u),P)P_{A}\bigr\|\,du" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int_{0}^{1}\bigl\|P_{A}^{\prime}-hDf_{\Omega_{0}}(r(u),P)P_{A}\bigr\|\,du</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E42Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\delta_{A}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\delta_{A},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E42Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E42Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\int_{0}^{1}\bigl\|P_{\Omega}^{\prime}-h\{Df_{\Omega_{0}}(r(u),P)P_{\Omega}-(0,p_{q})\}\bigr\|\,du" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int_{0}^{1}\bigl\|P_{\Omega}^{\prime}-h\{Df_{\Omega_{0}}(r(u),P)P_{\Omega}-(0,p_{q})\}\bigr\|\,du</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E42Xb.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\delta_{\Omega}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\delta_{\Omega},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E42Xc" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E42Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\int_{0}^{1}\bigl\|P_{K}^{\prime}-hDf_{\Omega_{0}}(r(u),P)P_{K}\bigr\|\,du" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int_{0}^{1}\bigl\|P_{K}^{\prime}-hDf_{\Omega_{0}}(r(u),P)P_{K}\bigr\|\,du</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E42Xc.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\delta_{K}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\delta_{K}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p4.3" class="ltx_p">These bounds can be computed through finite polynomial calculations.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p">At the starting point <math id="S3.SS4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{*}</annotation></semantics></math> of a step, suppose we have error bounds</p>
<table id="S3.E43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(43)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{gathered}\|\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta_{0}}(r_{*})-P(0)\|\leq\varepsilon_{\mathrm{poly}},\\
\sup_{\vartheta\in D}\|\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta}(r_{*})-\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta_{0}}(r_{*})\|\leq r_{Q},\\
\sup_{\vartheta\in D}\|\mathbf{Q}_{\vartheta}(r_{*})-\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta}(r_{*})\|\leq\delta_{\mathrm{bd}}.\end{gathered}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mi>ϑ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>poly</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mi>ϑ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>ϑ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mi>ϑ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mi>ϑ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mi>ϑ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>ϑ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>bd</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{gathered}\|\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta_{0}}(r_{*})-P(0)\|\leq\varepsilon_{\mathrm{poly}},\\
\sup_{\vartheta\in D}\|\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta}(r_{*})-\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta_{0}}(r_{*})\|\leq r_{Q},\\
\sup_{\vartheta\in D}\|\mathbf{Q}_{\vartheta}(r_{*})-\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta}(r_{*})\|\leq\delta_{\mathrm{bd}}.\end{gathered}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p5.2" class="ltx_p">These bound, respectively, the polynomial error, the variation across the parameter set <math id="S3.SS4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>, and the discrepancy between the exact and finite-data flows. For the parameter derivatives, also suppose</p>
<table id="S3.E44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(44)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigl\|\partial_{\xi}\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta}(r_{*})\bigr|_{\vartheta=\vartheta_{0}}-P_{\xi}(0)\bigr\|\leq\varepsilon_{\mathrm{poly},\xi},\qquad\sup_{\vartheta\in D}\bigl\|\partial_{\xi}\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta}(r_{*})-\partial_{\xi}\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta}(r_{*})\bigr|_{\vartheta=\vartheta_{0}}\bigr\|\leq r_{\xi}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>ξ</mi></msub><msub><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>ϑ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>ϑ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ϑ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>poly</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="1.889em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>ϑ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>ϑ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>ξ</mi></msub><msub><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>ϑ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>ϑ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ϑ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl\|\partial_{\xi}\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta}(r_{*})\bigr|_{\vartheta=\vartheta_{0}}-P_{\xi}(0)\bigr\|\leq\varepsilon_{\mathrm{poly},\xi},\qquad\sup_{\vartheta\in D}\bigl\|\partial_{\xi}\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta}(r_{*})-\partial_{\xi}\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta}(r_{*})\bigr|_{\vartheta=\vartheta_{0}}\bigr\|\leq r_{\xi}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p5.3" class="ltx_p">The derivative bounds are needed to control <math id="S3.SS4.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D\widetilde{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D\widetilde{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math> uniformly on <math id="S3.SS4.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>. The bounds in (<a href="#S3.E43" title="In 3.4. Computer-assisted proof of the matching conditions ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">43</span></a>)– (<a href="#S3.E44" title="In 3.4. Computer-assisted proof of the matching conditions ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">44</span></a>) are checked at the first mesh point by interval arithmetic, with <math id="S3.SS4.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{\mathrm{bd}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>bd</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{\mathrm{bd}}</annotation></semantics></math> supplied by the origin or exterior boundary contraction argument. On later steps, they follow from the preceding bounds after new error is included.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p6.2" class="ltx_p">We denote components of <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(u)=(p_{q}(u),p_{v}(u))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(u)=(p_{q}(u),p_{v}(u))</annotation></semantics></math>. Choose an enclosure radius <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and bounds</p>
<table id="S3.E45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(45)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{\mathrm{step}}\geq\sup_{u\in[0,1]}|p_{q}(u)|+\varepsilon,\qquad V_{\xi}\geq\sup_{u\in[0,1]}\|P_{\xi}(u)\|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>step</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">≥</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">≥</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\mathrm{step}}\geq\sup_{u\in[0,1]}|p_{q}(u)|+\varepsilon,\qquad V_{\xi}\geq\sup_{u\in[0,1]}\|P_{\xi}(u)\|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p6.3" class="ltx_p">Thus <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{\mathrm{step}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>step</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\mathrm{step}}</annotation></semantics></math> bounds <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|q|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|q|</annotation></semantics></math> for states within <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>, while <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\xi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\xi}</annotation></semantics></math> bounds the polynomial parameter derivative. Define the growth factor <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> for perturbations within this enclosure by</p>
<table id="S3.Ex96" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex96.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=\frac{1+\sup_{D}|\Omega|+\frac{1}{p-1}+pM_{\mathrm{step}}^{p-1}}{2}+\begin{cases}0,&amp;h&gt;0,\\
(d-1)/r_{\min},&amp;h&lt;0,\end{cases}\qquad g=\exp(|h|L)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mi>D</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>step</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=\frac{1+\sup_{D}|\Omega|+\frac{1}{p-1}+pM_{\mathrm{step}}^{p-1}}{2}+\begin{cases}0,&amp;h&gt;0,\\
(d-1)/r_{\min},&amp;h&lt;0,\end{cases}\qquad g=\exp(|h|L).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p6.4" class="ltx_p">We denote by a subscript <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>+</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+</annotation></semantics></math> a candidate bound valid throughout the current step, including its endpoint. Define</p>
<table id="S3.E46" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S3.E46X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_left">(46)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E46X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(\varepsilon_{\mathrm{poly}})_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>poly</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(\varepsilon_{\mathrm{poly}})_{+}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E46X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=g\bigl(\varepsilon_{\mathrm{poly}}+\delta_{0}\bigr)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>poly</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=g\bigl(\varepsilon_{\mathrm{poly}}+\delta_{0}\bigr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E46Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E46Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(r_{Q})_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(r_{Q})_{+}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E46Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=g\bigl(r_{Q}+|h|\rho M_{\mathrm{step}}\bigr)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>step</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=g\bigl(r_{Q}+|h|\rho M_{\mathrm{step}}\bigr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E46Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E46Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(\delta_{\mathrm{bd}})_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>bd</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(\delta_{\mathrm{bd}})_{+}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E46Xb.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=g\delta_{\mathrm{bd}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>bd</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=g\delta_{\mathrm{bd}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p6.5" class="ltx_p">These will be used as bounds in Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmthm9" title="Lemma 3.9. ‣ 3.4. Computer-assisted proof of the matching conditions ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.9</span></a>. These errors obey</p>
<table id="S3.Ex97" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex97X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex97X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(\varepsilon_{\mathrm{poly},\xi})_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>poly</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(\varepsilon_{\mathrm{poly},\xi})_{+}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex97X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=g\Bigl\{\varepsilon_{\mathrm{poly},\xi}+\delta_{\xi}+p(p-1)|h|M_{\mathrm{step}}^{p-2}V_{\xi}(\varepsilon_{\mathrm{poly}})_{+}\Bigr\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>poly</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>step</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>poly</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=g\Bigl\{\varepsilon_{\mathrm{poly},\xi}+\delta_{\xi}+p(p-1)|h|M_{\mathrm{step}}^{p-2}V_{\xi}(\varepsilon_{\mathrm{poly}})_{+}\Bigr\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex97X.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\xi=A,K," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\xi=A,K,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex97Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex97Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(\varepsilon_{\mathrm{poly},\Omega})_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>poly</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(\varepsilon_{\mathrm{poly},\Omega})_{+}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex97Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=g\Bigl\{\varepsilon_{\mathrm{poly},\Omega}+\delta_{\Omega}+|h|\bigl(p(p-1)M_{\mathrm{step}}^{p-2}V_{\Omega}+1\bigr)(\varepsilon_{\mathrm{poly}})_{+}\Bigr\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>poly</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>step</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>poly</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=g\Bigl\{\varepsilon_{\mathrm{poly},\Omega}+\delta_{\Omega}+|h|\bigl(p(p-1)M_{\mathrm{step}}^{p-2}V_{\Omega}+1\bigr)(\varepsilon_{\mathrm{poly}})_{+}\Bigr\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="3"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p6.6" class="ltx_p">Again, this is proven in Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmthm9" title="Lemma 3.9. ‣ 3.4. Computer-assisted proof of the matching conditions ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.9</span></a>. For their variation across the parameter cube, set</p>
<table id="S3.Ex98" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex98X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex98X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(r_{\xi})_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(r_{\xi})_{+}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex98X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=g\Bigl\{r_{\xi}+|h|(p(p-1)M_{\mathrm{step}}^{p-2}(r_{Q})_{+}+\rho)\bigl(V_{\xi}+(\varepsilon_{\mathrm{poly},\xi})_{+}\bigr)\Bigr\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>step</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>poly</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=g\Bigl\{r_{\xi}+|h|(p(p-1)M_{\mathrm{step}}^{p-2}(r_{Q})_{+}+\rho)\bigl(V_{\xi}+(\varepsilon_{\mathrm{poly},\xi})_{+}\bigr)\Bigr\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex98X.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\xi=A,K," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\xi=A,K,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex98Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex98Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(r_{\Omega})_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(r_{\Omega})_{+}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex98Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=g\Bigl\{r_{\Omega}+|h|(p(p-1)M_{\mathrm{step}}^{p-2}(r_{Q})_{+}+\rho)\bigl(V_{\Omega}+(\varepsilon_{\mathrm{poly},\Omega})_{+}\bigr)+|h|(r_{Q})_{+}\Bigr\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>step</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>poly</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=g\Bigl\{r_{\Omega}+|h|(p(p-1)M_{\mathrm{step}}^{p-2}(r_{Q})_{+}+\rho)\bigl(V_{\Omega}+(\varepsilon_{\mathrm{poly},\Omega})_{+}\bigr)+|h|(r_{Q})_{+}\Bigr\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="3"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p6.7" class="ltx_p">The nonvanishing test for the step is</p>
<table id="S3.E47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(47)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|p_{q}(0)|-\sum_{n\geq 1}|[u^{n}]p_{q}|&gt;\varepsilon." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|p_{q}(0)|-\sum_{n\geq 1}|[u^{n}]p_{q}|&gt;\varepsilon.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p6.8" class="ltx_p">Here <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[u^{n}]p_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[u^{n}]p_{q}</annotation></semantics></math> is the coefficient of <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>u</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{q}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq u\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq u\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, the left-hand side bounds <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|p_{q}(u)|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|p_{q}(u)|</annotation></semantics></math> from below throughout the step. Once the enclosure condition in the next lemma holds, every exact and finite profile lies within <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> and therefore has <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|q|&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|q|&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. This also ensures that the logarithm and ratios in the matching map are defined at <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\mathrm{m}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\mathrm{m}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p7.1" class="ltx_p">The next lemma turns the residual and starting bounds into enclosures valid throughout one step. Its strict inequality ensures that the solutions stay inside the enclosure used to compute <math id="S3.SS4.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmthm9" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmthm9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3.9</span></span><span id="S3.Thmthm9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmthm9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmthm9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmthm9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assume the residual bounds (<a href="#S3.E42" title="In 3.4. Computer-assisted proof of the matching conditions ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">42</span></a>),
the starting bounds
(<a href="#S3.E43" title="In 3.4. Computer-assisted proof of the matching conditions ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">43</span></a>)–
(<a href="#S3.E44" title="In 3.4. Computer-assisted proof of the matching conditions ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">44</span></a>),
and the enclosure bounds (<a href="#S3.E45" title="In 3.4. Computer-assisted proof of the matching conditions ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">45</span></a>) defining
<math id="S3.Thmthm9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{\mathrm{step}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>step</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\mathrm{step}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.Thmthm9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\xi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\xi}</annotation></semantics></math>.
If</span></p>
<table id="S3.E48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(48)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\varepsilon_{\mathrm{poly}})_{+}+(r_{Q})_{+}+(\delta_{\mathrm{bd}})_{+}&lt;\varepsilon," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>poly</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>bd</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\varepsilon_{\mathrm{poly}})_{+}+(r_{Q})_{+}+(\delta_{\mathrm{bd}})_{+}&lt;\varepsilon,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.Thmthm9.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmthm9.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">then the following bounds hold for every <math id="S3.Thmthm9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex99" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex99.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{gathered}\|\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta_{0}}-P\|\leq(\varepsilon_{\mathrm{poly}})_{+},\qquad\sup_{\vartheta\in D}\|\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta}-\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta_{0}}\|\leq(r_{Q})_{+},\qquad\sup_{\vartheta\in D}\|\mathbf{Q}_{\vartheta}-\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta}\|\leq(\delta_{\mathrm{bd}})_{+},\\
\|\left.\partial_{\xi}\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta}\right|_{\vartheta=\vartheta_{0}}-P_{\xi}\|\leq(\varepsilon_{\mathrm{poly},\xi})_{+},\\
\sup_{\vartheta\in D}\|\partial_{\xi}\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta}-\left.\partial_{\xi}\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta}\right|_{\vartheta=\vartheta_{0}}\|\leq(r_{\xi})_{+},\quad\xi\in\{A,\Omega,K\}.\end{gathered}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>ϑ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0.0835em">≤</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>poly</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo rspace="3.889em">,</mo><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>ϑ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ϑ</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>ϑ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0.0835em">≤</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo rspace="3.889em">,</mo><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>ϑ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝐐</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ϑ</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ϑ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0.0835em">≤</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>bd</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>ξ</mi></msub><msub><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>ϑ</mi></msub><mo>|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>ϑ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ϑ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>poly</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>ϑ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ϑ</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ϑ</mi></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>ϑ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ϑ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0.0835em">≤</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{gathered}\|\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta_{0}}-P\|\leq(\varepsilon_{\mathrm{poly}})_{+},\qquad\sup_{\vartheta\in D}\|\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta}-\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta_{0}}\|\leq(r_{Q})_{+},\qquad\sup_{\vartheta\in D}\|\mathbf{Q}_{\vartheta}-\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta}\|\leq(\delta_{\mathrm{bd}})_{+},\\
\|\left.\partial_{\xi}\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta}\right|_{\vartheta=\vartheta_{0}}-P_{\xi}\|\leq(\varepsilon_{\mathrm{poly},\xi})_{+},\\
\sup_{\vartheta\in D}\|\partial_{\xi}\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta}-\left.\partial_{\xi}\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta}\right|_{\vartheta=\vartheta_{0}}\|\leq(r_{\xi})_{+},\quad\xi\in\{A,\Omega,K\}.\end{gathered}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.Thmthm9.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmthm9.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">All exact and finite profile solutions involved continue to the endpoint. If, in addition, (<a href="#S3.E47" title="In 3.4. Computer-assisted proof of the matching conditions ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">47</span></a>) holds, they are nonvanishing throughout the step.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS4.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">We first bound the growth of perturbations to the profile flow. For every <math id="S3.SS4.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\eta,\zeta)\in\mathbb{C}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\eta,\zeta)\in\mathbb{C}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, direct differentiation of (<a href="#S3.E41" title="In 3.4. Computer-assisted proof of the matching conditions ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">41</span></a>) gives</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex100" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex100.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Df_{\Omega}(r,(q,v))(\eta,\zeta)=\left(\zeta,DN(q)\eta-\left(\Omega+\frac{i}{p-1}\right)\eta-\left(\frac{d-1}{r}+\frac{ir}{2}\right)\zeta\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>r</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ζ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Df_{\Omega}(r,(q,v))(\eta,\zeta)=\left(\zeta,DN(q)\eta-\left(\Omega+\frac{i}{p-1}\right)\eta-\left(\frac{d-1}{r}+\frac{ir}{2}\right)\zeta\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">If <math id="S3.SS4.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|q|\leq M_{\mathrm{step}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>step</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|q|\leq M_{\mathrm{step}}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S3.SS4.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|DN(q)\|\leq pM_{\mathrm{step}}^{p-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>step</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|DN(q)\|\leq pM_{\mathrm{step}}^{p-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, the term <math id="S3.SS4.p8.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="-ir\zeta/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>ζ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-ir\zeta/2</annotation></semantics></math> has zero real inner product with <math id="S3.SS4.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ζ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta</annotation></semantics></math>. The radial damping decreases the norm when <math id="S3.SS4.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, whereas for <math id="S3.SS4.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math> its contribution is at most <math id="S3.SS4.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(d-1)/r_{\min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(d-1)/r_{\min}</annotation></semantics></math>. Consequently,</span></p>
<table id="S3.E49" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S3.E49X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_left">(49)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E49X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\operatorname{Re}\left\langle(\eta,\zeta),\frac{h}{|h|}Df_{\Omega}(r,(q,v))(\eta,\zeta)\right\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\operatorname{Re}\left\langle(\eta,\zeta),\frac{h}{|h|}Df_{\Omega}(r,(q,v))(\eta,\zeta)\right\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E49X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\left(1+|\Omega|+\frac{1}{p-1}+pM_{\mathrm{step}}^{p-1}\right)|\eta||\zeta|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>step</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\left(1+|\Omega|+\frac{1}{p-1}+pM_{\mathrm{step}}^{p-1}\right)|\eta||\zeta|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E49Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E49Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{d-1}{r_{\min}}\mathbf{1}_{\{h&lt;0\}}|\zeta|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{d-1}{r_{\min}}\mathbf{1}_{\{h&lt;0\}}|\zeta|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E49Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E49Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq L\bigl(|\eta|^{2}+|\zeta|^{2}\bigr)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq L\bigl(|\eta|^{2}+|\zeta|^{2}\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">We give the details for the polynomial error. Set</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex101" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex101.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}(u)=\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta_{0}}(r(u))-P(u),\qquad\mathcal{R}(u)=P^{\prime}(u)-hf_{\Omega_{0}}(r(u),P(u))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mi>ϑ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}(u)=\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta_{0}}(r(u))-P(u),\qquad\mathcal{R}(u)=P^{\prime}(u)-hf_{\Omega_{0}}(r(u),P(u)).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">The fundamental theorem of calculus applied to the vector field yields</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex102" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex102.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}^{\prime}(u)=h\int_{0}^{1}Df_{\Omega_{0}}\bigl(r(u),P(u)+\tau\mathcal{E}(u)\bigr)\mathcal{E}(u)\,d\tau-\mathcal{R}(u)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}^{\prime}(u)=h\int_{0}^{1}Df_{\Omega_{0}}\bigl(r(u),P(u)+\tau\mathcal{E}(u)\bigr)\mathcal{E}(u)\,d\tau-\mathcal{R}(u).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p9.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p9.3.1" class="ltx_text">Thus (<a href="#S3.E49" title="In Proof. ‣ 3.4. Computer-assisted proof of the matching conditions ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">49</span></a>) implies, wherever <math id="S3.SS4.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}(u)\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}(u)\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex103" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex103.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d}{du}\|\mathcal{E}(u)\|=\frac{\operatorname{Re}\langle\mathcal{E}(u),\mathcal{E}^{\prime}(u)\rangle}{\|\mathcal{E}(u)\|}\leq|h|L\|\mathcal{E}(u)\|+\|\mathcal{R}(u)\|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d}{du}\|\mathcal{E}(u)\|=\frac{\operatorname{Re}\langle\mathcal{E}(u),\mathcal{E}^{\prime}(u)\rangle}{\|\mathcal{E}(u)\|}\leq|h|L\|\mathcal{E}(u)\|+\|\mathcal{R}(u)\|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p9.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p9.4.1" class="ltx_text">Multiplying by <math id="S3.SS4.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{-|h|Lu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{-|h|Lu}</annotation></semantics></math> and using (<a href="#S3.E42" title="In 3.4. Computer-assisted proof of the matching conditions ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">42</span></a>), for <math id="S3.SS4.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq u\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq u\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> we obtain</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex104" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex104X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex104X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\mathcal{E}(u)\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\mathcal{E}(u)\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex104X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq e^{|h|Lu}\|\mathcal{E}(0)\|+\int_{0}^{u}e^{|h|L(u-t)}\|\mathcal{R}(t)\|\,dt" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>u</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq e^{|h|Lu}\|\mathcal{E}(0)\|+\int_{0}^{u}e^{|h|L(u-t)}\|\mathcal{R}(t)\|\,dt</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex104Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex104Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq e^{|h|Lu}\left(\varepsilon_{\mathrm{poly}}+\int_{0}^{u}\|\mathcal{R}(t)\|\,dt\right)\leq g\bigl(\varepsilon_{\mathrm{poly}}+\delta_{0}\bigr)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>poly</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>u</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">d</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>poly</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq e^{|h|Lu}\left(\varepsilon_{\mathrm{poly}}+\int_{0}^{u}\|\mathcal{R}(t)\|\,dt\right)\leq g\bigl(\varepsilon_{\mathrm{poly}}+\delta_{0}\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p9.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p9.5.1" class="ltx_text">This proves the first line of (<a href="#S3.E46" title="In 3.4. Computer-assisted proof of the matching conditions ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">46</span></a>). For <math id="S3.SS4.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta}-\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>ϑ</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mi>ϑ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta}-\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the additional source <math id="S3.SS4.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigl(0,-(\Omega-\Omega_{0})(\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta_{0}})_{1}\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mi>ϑ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl(0,-(\Omega-\Omega_{0})(\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta_{0}})_{1}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math> has norm at most <math id="S3.SS4.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho M_{\mathrm{step}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>step</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho M_{\mathrm{step}}</annotation></semantics></math>, giving the second line. The exact and finite solutions at fixed parameter solve the same ODE, giving the third line.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Subtracting the center variational equation from its polynomial approximation gives an additional source bounded by <math id="S3.SS4.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(p-1)M_{\mathrm{step}}^{p-2}V_{\xi}(\varepsilon_{\mathrm{poly}})_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>step</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>poly</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(p-1)M_{\mathrm{step}}^{p-2}V_{\xi}(\varepsilon_{\mathrm{poly}})_{+}</annotation></semantics></math>, together with <math id="S3.SS4.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\varepsilon_{\mathrm{poly}})_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>poly</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\varepsilon_{\mathrm{poly}})_{+}</annotation></semantics></math> for the frequency derivative, proving the bound for <math id="S3.SS4.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\varepsilon_{\mathrm{poly},\xi})_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>poly</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\varepsilon_{\mathrm{poly},\xi})_{+}</annotation></semantics></math>. For the variation across the parameter cube,</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex105" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex105.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|Df_{\Omega}(r,\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta})-Df_{\Omega_{0}}(r,\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta_{0}})\|\leq p(p-1)M_{\mathrm{step}}^{p-2}(r_{Q})_{+}+\rho." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>ϑ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mi>ϑ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>step</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|Df_{\Omega}(r,\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta})-Df_{\Omega_{0}}(r,\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta_{0}})\|\leq p(p-1)M_{\mathrm{step}}^{p-2}(r_{Q})_{+}+\rho.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">Also <math id="S3.SS4.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\left.\partial_{\xi}\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta}\right|_{\vartheta=\vartheta_{0}}\|\leq V_{\xi}+(\varepsilon_{\mathrm{poly},\xi})_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>ξ</mi></msub><msub><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>ϑ</mi></msub><mo>|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>ϑ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ϑ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>poly</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\left.\partial_{\xi}\widetilde{\mathbf{Q}}_{\vartheta}\right|_{\vartheta=\vartheta_{0}}\|\leq V_{\xi}+(\varepsilon_{\mathrm{poly},\xi})_{+}</annotation></semantics></math> throughout the step. The difference of the frequency sources is bounded by <math id="S3.SS4.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(r_{Q})_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(r_{Q})_{+}</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="S3.SS4.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi=\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi=\Omega</annotation></semantics></math> and vanishes when <math id="S3.SS4.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi=A,K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi=A,K</annotation></semantics></math>. Subtracting the variational equations and applying Gronwall, including the additional source bounded by <math id="S3.SS4.p10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|h|(r_{Q})_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|h|(r_{Q})_{+}</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="S3.SS4.p10.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi=\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi=\Omega</annotation></semantics></math>, proves the last estimate.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">These estimates are initially valid up to a possible first exit from the enclosure. Their strict sum bound excludes such an exit. The vector field is smooth for <math id="S3.SS4.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, and bounded solutions continue, proving existence through the step. Finally, (<a href="#S3.E47" title="In 3.4. Computer-assisted proof of the matching conditions ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">47</span></a>) and the enclosure bound give a positive lower bound for the modulus.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p12.1" class="ltx_p">Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmthm9" title="Lemma 3.9. ‣ 3.4. Computer-assisted proof of the matching conditions ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.9</span></a> is applied successively on the mesh covering the inner and outer finite intervals. At each step the polynomial coefficients are exact numbers. Errors are added to the propagated bounds before the next step, and the enclosure condition is rechecked. The initial bounds and parameter variations are obtained by interval evaluation and differentiation of the finite formulas (<a href="#S3.E35" title="In 3.2. Interior solution at the origin ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">35</span></a>) and (<a href="#S3.E21" title="In 3.1. Exterior solution at infinity ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a>)–(<a href="#S3.E22" title="In 3.1. Exterior solution at infinity ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p13.1" class="ltx_p">It remains to convert the endpoint enclosure into an error bound for the matching map. Suppose a finite endpoint satisfies <math id="S3.SS4.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|q|\geq q_{\min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|q|\geq q_{\min}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS4.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|v|\leq v_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|v|\leq v_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math>, while the exact endpoint is within Euclidean distance <math id="S3.SS4.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{\mathrm{bd}}&lt;q_{\min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>bd</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{\mathrm{bd}}&lt;q_{\min}</annotation></semantics></math>. For the inner endpoints, the amplitude and slope bounds are</p>
<table id="S3.Ex106" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex106.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{aligned} \left|\log|Q^{\mathrm{in}}|-\log|\widetilde{Q}^{\mathrm{in}}|\right|&amp;\leq\frac{\delta_{\mathrm{bd}}}{q_{\min}-\delta_{\mathrm{bd}}},\\
r_{\mathrm{m}}\left|\operatorname{Re}\left(\frac{(Q^{\mathrm{in}})^{\prime}}{Q^{\mathrm{in}}}-\frac{(\widetilde{Q}^{\mathrm{in}})^{\prime}}{\widetilde{Q}^{\mathrm{in}}}\right)\right|&amp;\leq\frac{r_{\mathrm{m}}\delta_{\mathrm{bd}}(1+v_{\max}/q_{\min})}{q_{\min}-\delta_{\mathrm{bd}}},\\
r_{\mathrm{m}}\left|\operatorname{Im}\left(\frac{(Q^{\mathrm{in}})^{\prime}}{Q^{\mathrm{in}}}-\frac{(\widetilde{Q}^{\mathrm{in}})^{\prime}}{\widetilde{Q}^{\mathrm{in}}}\right)\right|&amp;\leq\frac{r_{\mathrm{m}}\delta_{\mathrm{bd}}(1+v_{\max}/q_{\min})}{q_{\min}-\delta_{\mathrm{bd}}},\end{aligned}\qquad\text{at }r=r_{\mathrm{m}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>in</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>in</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>bd</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>bd</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>in</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>in</mi></msup></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>in</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>in</mi></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>bd</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>bd</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>in</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>in</mi></msup></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>in</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>in</mi></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>bd</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>bd</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mtext>at </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{aligned} \left|\log|Q^{\mathrm{in}}|-\log|\widetilde{Q}^{\mathrm{in}}|\right|&amp;\leq\frac{\delta_{\mathrm{bd}}}{q_{\min}-\delta_{\mathrm{bd}}},\\
r_{\mathrm{m}}\left|\operatorname{Re}\left(\frac{(Q^{\mathrm{in}})^{\prime}}{Q^{\mathrm{in}}}-\frac{(\widetilde{Q}^{\mathrm{in}})^{\prime}}{\widetilde{Q}^{\mathrm{in}}}\right)\right|&amp;\leq\frac{r_{\mathrm{m}}\delta_{\mathrm{bd}}(1+v_{\max}/q_{\min})}{q_{\min}-\delta_{\mathrm{bd}}},\\
r_{\mathrm{m}}\left|\operatorname{Im}\left(\frac{(Q^{\mathrm{in}})^{\prime}}{Q^{\mathrm{in}}}-\frac{(\widetilde{Q}^{\mathrm{in}})^{\prime}}{\widetilde{Q}^{\mathrm{in}}}\right)\right|&amp;\leq\frac{r_{\mathrm{m}}\delta_{\mathrm{bd}}(1+v_{\max}/q_{\min})}{q_{\min}-\delta_{\mathrm{bd}}},\end{aligned}\qquad\text{at }r=r_{\mathrm{m}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p13.2" class="ltx_p">The same inequalities hold for the outer endpoints with <math id="S3.SS4.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{in}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>in</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{in}</annotation></semantics></math> replaced by <math id="S3.SS4.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{out}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>out</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{out}</annotation></semantics></math>. The first bound follows by integrating the derivative of <math id="S3.SS4.p13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log|q|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log|q|</annotation></semantics></math> along the segment between the endpoints. The second and third follow by subtracting the two ratios <math id="S3.SS4.p13.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v/q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v/q</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="S3.SS4.p13.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma\in\{\mathrm{in},\mathrm{out}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>in</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>out</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma\in\{\mathrm{in},\mathrm{out}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S3.SS4.p13.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\min}^{\sigma},v_{\max}^{\sigma},\delta_{\mathrm{bd}}^{\sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>min</mi><mi>σ</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>max</mi><mi>σ</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mi>bd</mi><mi>σ</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\min}^{\sigma},v_{\max}^{\sigma},\delta_{\mathrm{bd}}^{\sigma}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the corresponding endpoint bounds and define the vector</p>
<table id="S3.Ex107" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex107.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{\sigma}:=\left(\frac{\delta_{\mathrm{bd}}^{\sigma}}{q_{\min}^{\sigma}-\delta_{\mathrm{bd}}^{\sigma}},\frac{r_{\mathrm{m}}\delta_{\mathrm{bd}}^{\sigma}(1+v_{\max}^{\sigma}/q_{\min}^{\sigma})}{q_{\min}^{\sigma}-\delta_{\mathrm{bd}}^{\sigma}},\dfrac{r_{\mathrm{m}}\delta_{\mathrm{bd}}^{\sigma}(1+v_{\max}^{\sigma}/q_{\min}^{\sigma})}{q_{\min}^{\sigma}-\delta_{\mathrm{bd}}^{\sigma}}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>σ</mi></msup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mi>bd</mi><mi>σ</mi></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>min</mi><mi>σ</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mi>bd</mi><mi>σ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mi>bd</mi><mi>σ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>max</mi><mi>σ</mi></msubsup><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>min</mi><mi>σ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>min</mi><mi>σ</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mi>bd</mi><mi>σ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mi>bd</mi><mi>σ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>max</mi><mi>σ</mi></msubsup><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>min</mi><mi>σ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>min</mi><mi>σ</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mi>bd</mi><mi>σ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{\sigma}:=\left(\frac{\delta_{\mathrm{bd}}^{\sigma}}{q_{\min}^{\sigma}-\delta_{\mathrm{bd}}^{\sigma}},\frac{r_{\mathrm{m}}\delta_{\mathrm{bd}}^{\sigma}(1+v_{\max}^{\sigma}/q_{\min}^{\sigma})}{q_{\min}^{\sigma}-\delta_{\mathrm{bd}}^{\sigma}},\dfrac{r_{\mathrm{m}}\delta_{\mathrm{bd}}^{\sigma}(1+v_{\max}^{\sigma}/q_{\min}^{\sigma})}{q_{\min}^{\sigma}-\delta_{\mathrm{bd}}^{\sigma}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p13.3" class="ltx_p">Thus, with <math id="S3.SS4.p13.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|B|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|B|</annotation></semantics></math> denoting the entrywise absolute value of <math id="S3.SS4.p13.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>, the choice</p>
<table id="S3.E50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(50)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E:=\bigl\||B|(e^{\mathrm{in}}+e^{\mathrm{out}})\bigr\|_{\infty}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>:=</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>in</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>out</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E:=\bigl\||B|(e^{\mathrm{in}}+e^{\mathrm{out}})\bigr\|_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p13.4" class="ltx_p">gives a computable bound <math id="S3.SS4.p13.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{D}\|B(\mathcal{M}-\widetilde{\mathcal{M}})\|_{\infty}\leq E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>sup</mo><mi>D</mi></msub><msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{D}\|B(\mathcal{M}-\widetilde{\mathcal{M}})\|_{\infty}\leq E</annotation></semantics></math>. The next lemma states the computer-assisted bounds.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmthm10" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmthm10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3.10</span></span><span id="S3.Thmthm10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Computer-assisted bounds)<span id="S3.Thmthm10.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmthm10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmthm10.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmthm10.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For the cube <math id="S3.Thmthm10.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#S3.E17" title="In 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>), the following statements hold.</span></p>
<ol id="S3.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(i)</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Throughout </span><math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, we have </span><math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\Omega|&lt;\Omega_{\mathrm{bd}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>bd</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\Omega|&lt;\Omega_{\mathrm{bd}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and </span><math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. Moreover, the fixed-point conditions at the origin (</span><a href="#S3.E37" title="In Lemma 3.7. ‣ 3.2. Interior solution at the origin ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">37</span></a><span id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">) and in the exterior (</span><a href="#S3.E31" title="In Proposition 3.4. ‣ 3.1. Exterior solution at infinity ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">31</span></a><span id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">) hold uniformly, and the corresponding ball inclusions are strict.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(ii)</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The bounds in (</span><a href="#S3.E46" title="In 3.4. Computer-assisted proof of the matching conditions ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">46</span></a><span id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">) satisfy </span><math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\varepsilon_{\mathrm{poly}})_{+}+(r_{Q})_{+}+(\delta_{\mathrm{bd}})_{+}&lt;\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>poly</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>bd</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\varepsilon_{\mathrm{poly}})_{+}+(r_{Q})_{+}+(\delta_{\mathrm{bd}})_{+}&lt;\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> on every step, with </span><math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon=10^{-8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon=10^{-8}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, and (</span><a href="#S3.E47" title="In 3.4. Computer-assisted proof of the matching conditions ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">47</span></a><span id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">) holds on every step. Thus the exact and finite inner solutions exist and are nonvanishing on </span><math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[r_{\mathrm{in}},r_{\mathrm{m}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>in</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[r_{\mathrm{in}},r_{\mathrm{m}}]</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, and the exact and finite outer solutions do so on </span><math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[r_{\mathrm{m}},r_{\mathrm{out}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[r_{\mathrm{m}},r_{\mathrm{out}}]</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, for all </span><math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vartheta\in D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϑ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vartheta\in D</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(iii)</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The matrix </span><math id="S3.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is invertible and, for the bounds in Proposition </span><a href="#S3.Thmthm8" title="Proposition 3.8. ‣ 3.3. Matching the inner and outer solutions ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.8</span></a><span id="S3.I1.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, the quantities </span><math id="S3.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y,E,Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y,E,Z</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.i3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> satisfy</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex108" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex108.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y+E+Z\rho&lt;\rho." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y+E+Z\rho&lt;\rho.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS4.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">All the code used for the computer-assisted argument is available in the GitHub repository <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>]</cite>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">The first step is to generate approximate profiles. A broad exploration in the parameters <math id="S3.SS4.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(d,p,A,\Omega,K)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(d,p,A,\Omega,K)</annotation></semantics></math> was carried out to look for solutions of the ODE (<a href="#S2.E8" title="In 2. Self-similar profile equation ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>). Once several candidates had been found, the parameters were refined to improve precision. This is done by <span class="ltx_ref ltx_nolink ltx_path ltx_font_typewriter ltx_ref_self">generate_candidate.py</span> using numerical shooting and continuation. The profile ODE is easier to solve numerically for larger values of <math id="S3.SS4.p15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>, so an initial solution is first found in that regime and then continued to the desired <math id="S3.SS4.p15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> and down to the final value of <math id="S3.SS4.p15.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>, using each solution to initialize the next. The resulting candidate is refined to get low residuals using multiprecision integration with <span id="S3.SS4.p15.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">mpmath</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib68" title="" class="ltx_ref">68</a>]</cite> and Newton corrections. The result is an approximation <math id="S3.SS4.p15.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(A_{0},\Omega_{0},K_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(A_{0},\Omega_{0},K_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> of the desired parameters.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p16" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text">The rest of the code uses the library <span id="S3.SS4.p16.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">python-flint</span> to implement interval arithmetic; see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">36</a>]</cite>. This is a Python module wrapping FLINT and Arb. A precision of 896 bits is chosen to ensure that error enclosures are small enough for the proof to close.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p17" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p17.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p17.1.1" class="ltx_text">The script <span class="ltx_ref ltx_nolink ltx_path ltx_font_typewriter ltx_ref_self">origin.py</span> evaluates the recurrence (<a href="#S3.E35" title="In 3.2. Interior solution at the origin ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">35</span></a>), computes the residual estimate (<a href="#S3.E36" title="In 3.2. Interior solution at the origin ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">36</span></a>), and checks the conditions for the contraction in (<a href="#S3.E37" title="In Lemma 3.7. ‣ 3.2. Interior solution at the origin ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">37</span></a>). The file <span class="ltx_ref ltx_nolink ltx_path ltx_font_typewriter ltx_ref_self">exterior.py</span> evaluates the recurrence (<a href="#S3.E21" title="In 3.1. Exterior solution at infinity ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a>)–(<a href="#S3.E22" title="In 3.1. Exterior solution at infinity ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a>), computes the linear-mode bounds (<a href="#S3.E28" title="In Proof. ‣ 3.1. Exterior solution at infinity ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a>), computes the residual estimate (<a href="#S3.E25" title="In Lemma 3.2. ‣ 3.1. Exterior solution at infinity ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">25</span></a>), checks the restriction <math id="S3.SS4.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, and all three conditions for the contraction in (<a href="#S3.E31" title="In Proposition 3.4. ‣ 3.1. Exterior solution at infinity ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">31</span></a>). These computations give the initial Cauchy-data errors at <math id="S3.SS4.p17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\mathrm{in}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>in</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\mathrm{in}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS4.p17.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\mathrm{out}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\mathrm{out}}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively, and prove item (i).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p18" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p18.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p18.1.1" class="ltx_text">The script <span class="ltx_ref ltx_nolink ltx_path ltx_font_typewriter ltx_ref_self">propagation.py</span> starts from either <math id="S3.SS4.p18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\mathrm{in}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>in</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\mathrm{in}}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="S3.SS4.p18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\mathrm{out}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\mathrm{out}}</annotation></semantics></math>. It constructs the coefficients of <math id="S3.SS4.p18.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P,P_{A},P_{\Omega},P_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P,P_{A},P_{\Omega},P_{K}</annotation></semantics></math> successively from the formal Taylor identities</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex109" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex109X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex109X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex109X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=hf_{\Omega_{0}}(r(u),P)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=hf_{\Omega_{0}}(r(u),P),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex109X.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P_{A}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P_{A}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex109X.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=hDf_{\Omega_{0}}(r(u),P)P_{A}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=hDf_{\Omega_{0}}(r(u),P)P_{A},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex109Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex109Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P_{\Omega}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P_{\Omega}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex109Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=h\{Df_{\Omega_{0}}(r(u),P)P_{\Omega}-(0,p_{q})\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=h\{Df_{\Omega_{0}}(r(u),P)P_{\Omega}-(0,p_{q})\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex109Xa.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P_{K}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P_{K}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex109Xa.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=hDf_{\Omega_{0}}(r(u),P)P_{K}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=hDf_{\Omega_{0}}(r(u),P)P_{K}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p18.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p18.2.1" class="ltx_text">At the chosen Taylor degree the series are truncated and their coefficients are replaced by midpoint values. The program then substitutes the resulting polynomials into the four left-hand sides in (<a href="#S3.E42" title="In 3.4. Computer-assisted proof of the matching conditions ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">42</span></a>) and obtains the bounds <math id="S3.SS4.p18.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{0},\delta_{A},\delta_{\Omega},\delta_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{0},\delta_{A},\delta_{\Omega},\delta_{K}</annotation></semantics></math>. It then applies Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmthm9" title="Lemma 3.9. ‣ 3.4. Computer-assisted proof of the matching conditions ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.9</span></a>, step by step, outward from <math id="S3.SS4.p18.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\mathrm{in}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>in</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\mathrm{in}}</annotation></semantics></math> and inward from <math id="S3.SS4.p18.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\mathrm{out}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\mathrm{out}}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S3.SS4.p18.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\mathrm{m}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\mathrm{m}}</annotation></semantics></math>. At every endpoint, interval evaluation and errors are added to the bounds for the next step. On every step the program verifies (<a href="#S3.E48" title="In Lemma 3.9. ‣ 3.4. Computer-assisted proof of the matching conditions ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">48</span></a>) with <math id="S3.SS4.p18.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon=10^{-8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon=10^{-8}</annotation></semantics></math> and the lower bound (<a href="#S3.E47" title="In 3.4. Computer-assisted proof of the matching conditions ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">47</span></a>). Thus all the hypotheses asserted in item (ii) are verified.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p19" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p19.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p19.1.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, <span class="ltx_ref ltx_nolink ltx_path ltx_font_typewriter ltx_ref_self">matching.py</span> evaluates <math id="S3.SS4.p19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math> from (<a href="#S3.E39" title="In 3.3. Matching the inner and outer solutions ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">39</span></a>) and an interval enclosure of <math id="S3.SS4.p19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D\widetilde{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D\widetilde{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math> using (<a href="#S3.E40" title="In 3.3. Matching the inner and outer solutions ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">40</span></a>). It takes <math id="S3.SS4.p19.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> to be the midpoint of an interval enclosure of the inverse of the Jacobian. Then it computes <math id="S3.SS4.p19.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS4.p19.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> directly and evaluates <math id="S3.SS4.p19.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> from (<a href="#S3.E50" title="In 3.4. Computer-assisted proof of the matching conditions ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">50</span></a>). The final strict check is precisely <math id="S3.SS4.p19.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y+E+Z\rho&lt;\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y+E+Z\rho&lt;\rho</annotation></semantics></math>, proving item (iii).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p20" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p20.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p20.1.1" class="ltx_text">The script <span class="ltx_ref ltx_nolink ltx_path ltx_font_typewriter ltx_ref_self">prove.py</span> runs all the above steps in order, and saves the results indicating whether each condition was verified.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmthm1" title="Theorem 3.1. ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS4.p21" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p21.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p21.1.1" class="ltx_text">The bounds in Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmthm10" title="Lemma 3.10 (Computer-assisted bounds). ‣ 3.4. Computer-assisted proof of the matching conditions ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.10</span></a> are used at several points in the argument. Item (i) verifies the hypotheses of Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmthm7" title="Lemma 3.7. ‣ 3.2. Interior solution at the origin ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.7</span></a> and of Proposition <a href="#S3.Thmthm4" title="Proposition 3.4. ‣ 3.1. Exterior solution at infinity ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a>. Item (ii) provides the hypotheses of Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmthm9" title="Lemma 3.9. ‣ 3.4. Computer-assisted proof of the matching conditions ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.9</span></a> and the nonvanishing needed for the finite inner and outer solutions. Item (iii) supplies the three quantitative hypotheses of Proposition <a href="#S3.Thmthm8" title="Proposition 3.8. ‣ 3.3. Matching the inner and outer solutions ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.8</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p22" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p22.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p22.1.1" class="ltx_text">It follows from the first two items and the cited results that the inner and outer solutions, together with their finite approximations, are defined up to the matching point. Lemma <a href="#S2.Thmthm1" title="Lemma 2.1. ‣ 2. Self-similar profile equation ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a> and Corollary <a href="#S3.Thmthm6" title="Corollary 3.6. ‣ 3.1. Exterior solution at infinity ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.6</span></a> show that <math id="S3.SS4.p22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined and continuous throughout <math id="S3.SS4.p22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>, while the corresponding ODE dependence shows that <math id="S3.SS4.p22.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math> is differentiable there. The third item therefore allows us to apply Proposition <a href="#S3.Thmthm8" title="Proposition 3.8. ‣ 3.3. Matching the inner and outer solutions ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.8</span></a>, which gives a zero of <math id="S3.SS4.p22.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S3.SS4.p22.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>. Joining the inner and outer solutions by the constant phase described above produces a smooth global profile. It is regular at zero and has <math id="S3.SS4.p22.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{f}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{f}=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS4.p22.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|C_{s}|=K^{1/(p-1)}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|C_{s}|=K^{1/(p-1)}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Nonvanishing follows from identity (<a href="#S2.E11" title="In Proof. ‣ 2. Self-similar profile equation ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>). Corollary <a href="#S3.Thmthm5" title="Corollary 3.5. ‣ 3.1. Exterior solution at infinity ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.5</span></a> gives the full slow expansion.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4. </span>Self-similar blow-up</h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Fix the pure slow profile of Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmthm1" title="Theorem 3.1. ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>, and write</p>
<table id="S4.Ex110" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex110.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=A_{*},\qquad\Omega=\Omega_{*},\qquad Q=Q_{A,\Omega}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=A_{*},\qquad\Omega=\Omega_{*},\qquad Q=Q_{A,\Omega}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">All functions and spaces in this section are radial, and constants may depend on the fixed profile. The construction below uses a finite-codimension strategy as in Li <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">46</a>]</cite>, together with the stable/unstable semigroup framework of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>]</cite>. The evolution is studied around the stationary profile, and localization is implemented by a direct finite-dimensional correction to obtain a finite-energy solution.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In the coordinates of (<a href="#S2.E4" title="In 2. Self-similar profile equation ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>), write</p>
<table id="S4.Ex111" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex111.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u(t,x)=(T-t)^{-\frac{1}{p-1}}e^{-i\Omega\tau}V(\tau,y),\qquad\tau=\log\frac{T}{T-t},\qquad y=\frac{x}{\sqrt{T-t}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>x</mi><msqrt><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u(t,x)=(T-t)^{-\frac{1}{p-1}}e^{-i\Omega\tau}V(\tau,y),\qquad\tau=\log\frac{T}{T-t},\qquad y=\frac{x}{\sqrt{T-t}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">The rescaled equation is</p>
<table id="S4.E51" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(51)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial_{\tau}V=\mathcal{A}_{0}V-iN(V),\qquad\mathcal{A}_{0}=i\Delta-\frac{1}{2}y\cdot\nabla_{y}-\frac{1}{p-1}+i\Omega." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>τ</mi></msub><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{\tau}V=\mathcal{A}_{0}V-iN(V),\qquad\mathcal{A}_{0}=i\Delta-\frac{1}{2}y\cdot\nabla_{y}-\frac{1}{p-1}+i\Omega.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p2.3" class="ltx_p">The profile satisfies <math id="S4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{0}Q=iN(Q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{0}Q=iN(Q)</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence <math id="S4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V=Q+v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V=Q+v</annotation></semantics></math> obeys</p>
<table id="S4.E52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(52)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial_{\tau}v=\mathcal{A}_{Q}v+\mathcal{F}(v)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>τ</mi></msub><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{\tau}v=\mathcal{A}_{Q}v+\mathcal{F}(v),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p2.4" class="ltx_p">Set</p>
<table id="S4.E53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(53)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\mathrm{diag}}=\frac{p+1}{2}|Q|^{p-1},\qquad V_{\mathrm{off}}=\frac{p-1}{2}|Q|^{p-3}Q^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>diag</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>off</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\mathrm{diag}}=\frac{p+1}{2}|Q|^{p-1},\qquad V_{\mathrm{off}}=\frac{p-1}{2}|Q|^{p-3}Q^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p2.5" class="ltx_p">Then the linearized operator <math id="S4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{Q}</annotation></semantics></math> and the nonlinear remainder <math id="S4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> are</p>
<table id="S4.Ex112" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex112X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex112X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{A}_{Q}h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{A}_{Q}h</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex112X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathcal{A}_{0}h-iV_{\mathrm{diag}}h-iV_{\mathrm{off}}\overline{h}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>diag</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>off</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathcal{A}_{0}h-iV_{\mathrm{diag}}h-iV_{\mathrm{off}}\overline{h},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex112Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex112Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{F}(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{F}(v)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex112Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-i\bigl[N(Q+v)-N(Q)-V_{\mathrm{diag}}v-V_{\mathrm{off}}\overline{v}\bigr]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>diag</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>off</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-i\bigl[N(Q+v)-N(Q)-V_{\mathrm{diag}}v-V_{\mathrm{off}}\overline{v}\bigr].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p2.6" class="ltx_p">We first translate the asymptotics and nonvanishing of <math id="S4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> into global pointwise bounds for the profile and its derivatives. These bounds place <math id="S4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> in the perturbation spaces used below and ensure that cutting off its tail produces a small perturbation. They also show that the coefficients of the linearized operator decay quadratically, with an additional power of decay for each derivative, as needed for the subsequent spectral estimates.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmthm1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmthm1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 4.1</span></span><span id="S4.Thmthm1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmthm1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmthm1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmthm1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There are constants <math id="S4.Thmthm1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{*}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{*}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.Thmthm1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{Q,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{Q,j}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="S4.E54" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(54)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|Q(y)|\geq c_{*}\langle y\rangle^{-\frac{2}{p-1}},\qquad|\partial^{\nu}Q(y)|\leq C_{Q,j}\langle y\rangle^{-\frac{2}{p-1}-j},\qquad|\nu|=j\geq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>ν</mi></msup><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|Q(y)|\geq c_{*}\langle y\rangle^{-\frac{2}{p-1}},\qquad|\partial^{\nu}Q(y)|\leq C_{Q,j}\langle y\rangle^{-\frac{2}{p-1}-j},\qquad|\nu|=j\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.Thmthm1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmthm1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In particular,</span></p>
<table id="S4.E55" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(55)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\partial^{\nu}V_{\mathrm{diag}}(y)|+|\partial^{\nu}V_{\mathrm{off}}(y)|\leq C_{Q,j}\langle y\rangle^{-2-j}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>ν</mi></msup><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>diag</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>ν</mi></msup><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>off</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\partial^{\nu}V_{\mathrm{diag}}(y)|+|\partial^{\nu}V_{\mathrm{off}}(y)|\leq C_{Q,j}\langle y\rangle^{-2-j}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Nonvanishing and the nonzero leading slow coefficient give the lower bound. Write <math id="S4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=|y|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=|y|</annotation></semantics></math> and take the approximation <math id="S4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)}</annotation></semantics></math> from Corollary <a href="#S3.Thmthm5" title="Corollary 3.5. ‣ 3.1. Exterior solution at infinity ‣ 3. Construction of the self-similar profile ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.5</span></a>, with the phase of <math id="S4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>, and put <math id="S4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{J}=Q-P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{J}=Q-P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)}</annotation></semantics></math>. Its equation is</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex113" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex113X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex113X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle w_{J}^{\prime\prime}={}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>J</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle w_{J}^{\prime\prime}={}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex113X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\left(\frac{d-1}{r}+\frac{ir}{2}\right)w_{J}^{\prime}-\left(\Omega+\frac{i}{p-1}\right)w_{J}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>r</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>J</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>J</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\left(\frac{d-1}{r}+\frac{ir}{2}\right)w_{J}^{\prime}-\left(\Omega+\frac{i}{p-1}\right)w_{J}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex113Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex113Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+N(Q)-N(P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)})-r_{J}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>J</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+N(Q)-N(P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)})-r_{J},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex113Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex113Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r_{J}={}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r_{J}={}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex113Xb.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle L_{\Omega}P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)}-N(P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle L_{\Omega}P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)}-N(P_{\mathrm{out}}^{(J)}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">The explicit residual satisfies <math id="S4.p3.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="r_{J}^{(k)}=O(r^{-2/(p-1)-2J-2-k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>J</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{J}^{(k)}=O(r^{-2/(p-1)-2J-2-k})</annotation></semantics></math>. Starting with the bounds for <math id="S4.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{J},w_{J}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>J</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{J},w_{J}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> in that corollary, differentiation of this equation gives <math id="S4.p3.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="w_{J}^{(j)}=O(r^{-2/(p-1)-2J-4+j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>J</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{J}^{(j)}=O(r^{-2/(p-1)-2J-4+j})</annotation></semantics></math> for each fixed <math id="S4.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, provided <math id="S4.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J\geq j-2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J\geq j-2</annotation></semantics></math>. Increasing <math id="S4.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math> proves the radial derivative bounds; smoothness at zero and the formulas for Cartesian derivatives give (<a href="#S4.E54" title="In Lemma 4.1. ‣ 4. Self-similar blow-up ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">54</span></a>). The coefficient bounds follow by the product rule.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.1. </span>Functional setting</h3>

<div id="S4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recall that <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{c}=d/2-2/(p-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{c}=d/2-2/(p-1)</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{c}&lt;s&lt;d/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{c}&lt;s&lt;d/2</annotation></semantics></math>, let</p>
<table id="S4.Ex114" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex114.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}_{s}=\dot{H}^{s}_{\mathrm{rad}}(\mathbb{R}^{d};\mathbb{C})\cap\dot{H}^{k_{\star}}_{\mathrm{rad}}(\mathbb{R}^{d};\mathbb{C}),\qquad\|h\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}^{2}=\||D|^{s}h\|_{2}^{2}+\||D|^{k_{\star}}h\|_{2}^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>rad</mi><mi>s</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>ℂ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>rad</mi><msub><mi>k</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>ℂ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}_{s}=\dot{H}^{s}_{\mathrm{rad}}(\mathbb{R}^{d};\mathbb{C})\cap\dot{H}^{k_{\star}}_{\mathrm{rad}}(\mathbb{R}^{d};\mathbb{C}),\qquad\|h\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}^{2}=\||D|^{s}h\|_{2}^{2}+\||D|^{k_{\star}}h\|_{2}^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{\star}\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{\star}\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies</p>
<table id="S4.Ex115" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex115.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{\star}\geq 3,\qquad k_{\star}&gt;\frac{d}{2}+2\|V_{\mathrm{off}}\|_{\infty}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>off</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{\star}\geq 3,\qquad k_{\star}&gt;\frac{d}{2}+2\|V_{\mathrm{off}}\|_{\infty}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">This ensures <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s_{c}-k_{\star})/2+\|V_{\mathrm{off}}\|_{\infty}\leq(s_{c}-s)/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>off</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s_{c}-k_{\star})/2+\|V_{\mathrm{off}}\|_{\infty}\leq(s_{c}-s)/2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">We use its underlying real Hilbert space for the scalar perturbation equation, since <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{Q}</annotation></semantics></math> is real-linear. The <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{H}^{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>s</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{H}^{s}</annotation></semantics></math> representative is fixed by the embedding into <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2d/(d-2s)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2d/(d-2s)}</annotation></semantics></math>. Equivalently, it is the completion of radial <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{c}^{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{c}^{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> in the displayed norm. We record the details of the interpolation estimate that will be used below. For <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in C_{c}^{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in C_{c}^{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, Fourier inversion and Cauchy–Schwarz give</p>
<table id="S4.E56" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S4.E56X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_left">(56)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E56X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|h\|_{L^{\infty}}\lesssim\|\widehat{h}\|_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup></msub><mo>≲</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|h\|_{L^{\infty}}\lesssim\|\widehat{h}\|_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E56X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\int_{|\xi|\leq R}|\widehat{h}(\xi)|\,d\xi+\int_{|\xi|&gt;R}|\widehat{h}(\xi)|\,d\xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></msub></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></msub></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\int_{|\xi|\leq R}|\widehat{h}(\xi)|\,d\xi+\int_{|\xi|&gt;R}|\widehat{h}(\xi)|\,d\xi</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.E56Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E56Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\left(\int_{|\xi|\leq R}|\xi|^{-2s}\,d\xi\right)^{1/2}\|h\|_{\dot{H}^{s}}+\left(\int_{|\xi|&gt;R}|\xi|^{-2k_{\star}}\,d\xi\right)^{1/2}\|h\|_{\dot{H}^{k_{\star}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></msub></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>s</mi></msup></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></msub></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><msub><mi>k</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></msup></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\left(\int_{|\xi|\leq R}|\xi|^{-2s}\,d\xi\right)^{1/2}\|h\|_{\dot{H}^{s}}+\left(\int_{|\xi|&gt;R}|\xi|^{-2k_{\star}}\,d\xi\right)^{1/2}\|h\|_{\dot{H}^{k_{\star}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.E56Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E56Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lesssim_{s}R^{\frac{d}{2}-s}\|h\|_{\dot{H}^{s}}+R^{\frac{d}{2}-k_{\star}}\|h\|_{\dot{H}^{k_{\star}}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≲</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mi>R</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>s</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><mi>R</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><msub><mi>k</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></msup></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lesssim_{s}R^{\frac{d}{2}-s}\|h\|_{\dot{H}^{s}}+R^{\frac{d}{2}-k_{\star}}\|h\|_{\dot{H}^{k_{\star}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Choosing <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R=(\|h\|_{\dot{H}^{k_{\star}}}/\|h\|_{\dot{H}^{s}})^{1/(k_{\star}-s)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><msub><mi>k</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></msup></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>s</mi></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R=(\|h\|_{\dot{H}^{k_{\star}}}/\|h\|_{\dot{H}^{s}})^{1/(k_{\star}-s)}</annotation></semantics></math> balances the two terms and yields</p>
<table id="S4.E57" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(57)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E57.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|h\|_{\infty}\lesssim_{s}\|h\|_{\dot{H}^{s}}^{\frac{k_{\star}-\frac{d}{2}}{k_{\star}-s}}\|h\|_{\dot{H}^{k_{\star}}}^{\frac{\frac{d}{2}-s}{k_{\star}-s}}\lesssim_{s}\|h\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0em">≲</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>s</mi></msup></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><msub><mi>k</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></msup></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mfrac><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0em">≲</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|h\|_{\infty}\lesssim_{s}\|h\|_{\dot{H}^{s}}^{\frac{k_{\star}-\frac{d}{2}}{k_{\star}-s}}\|h\|_{\dot{H}^{k_{\star}}}^{\frac{\frac{d}{2}-s}{k_{\star}-s}}\lesssim_{s}\|h\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p2.4" class="ltx_p">Here we used the inequality <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\theta}B^{1-\theta}\leq\theta A+(1-\theta)B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>θ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\theta}B^{1-\theta}\leq\theta A+(1-\theta)B</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmthm2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmthm2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 4.2</span></span><span id="S4.Thmthm2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmthm2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmthm2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmthm2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For every <math id="S4.Thmthm2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{c}&lt;s&lt;d/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{c}&lt;s&lt;d/2</annotation></semantics></math>, the profile <math id="S4.Thmthm2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> belongs to <math id="S4.Thmthm2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Fix a smooth radial cutoff <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>χ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi</annotation></semantics></math>, equal to one on <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|y|\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|y|\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and zero on <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|y|\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|y|\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>, and set <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi_{R}(y)=\chi(y/R)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi_{R}(y)=\chi(y/R)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta(y)=\chi(y)-\chi(2y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta(y)=\chi(y)-\chi(2y)</annotation></semantics></math>. For every <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex116" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex116.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q=\chi_{R}Q+\sum_{j\geq 1}Q_{j,R},\qquad Q_{j,R}(y)=\eta(y/(2^{j}R))Q(y)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>j</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q=\chi_{R}Q+\sum_{j\geq 1}Q_{j,R},\qquad Q_{j,R}(y)=\eta(y/(2^{j}R))Q(y).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=2^{j}R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>j</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=2^{j}R</annotation></semantics></math>, set <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{j,R}(Y)=L^{2/(p-1)}\eta(Y)Q(LY)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{j,R}(Y)=L^{2/(p-1)}\eta(Y)Q(LY)</annotation></semantics></math>. These functions are supported in <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/2\leq|Y|\leq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/2\leq|Y|\leq 2</annotation></semantics></math>, and (<a href="#S4.E54" title="In Lemma 4.1. ‣ 4. Self-similar blow-up ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">54</span></a>) gives <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|g_{j,R}\|_{H^{k_{\star}}}\leq C_{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><msub><mi>k</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></msup></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|g_{j,R}\|_{H^{k_{\star}}}\leq C_{Q}</annotation></semantics></math>, uniformly in <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j,R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j,R</annotation></semantics></math>. Scaling in dimension <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> yields, for <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=s,k_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=s,k_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex117" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex117.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|Q_{j,R}\|_{\dot{H}^{k}}=L^{s_{c}-k}\|g_{j,R}\|_{\dot{H}^{k}}\leq C_{Q}(2^{j}R)^{s_{c}-k}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msup></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msup></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>j</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|Q_{j,R}\|_{\dot{H}^{k}}=L^{s_{c}-k}\|g_{j,R}\|_{\dot{H}^{k}}\leq C_{Q}(2^{j}R)^{s_{c}-k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k&gt;s_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k&gt;s_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>, the series converges in <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> and locally to <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-\chi_{R})Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-\chi_{R})Q</annotation></semantics></math>, with</span></p>
<table id="S4.E58" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(58)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E58.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|(1-\chi_{R})Q\|_{\dot{H}^{k}}\leq\sum_{j\geq 1}\|Q_{j,R}\|_{\dot{H}^{k}}\lesssim_{Q,s}R^{s_{c}-k},\qquad k=s,k_{\star}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>Q</mi><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msup></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.0835em">≲</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|(1-\chi_{R})Q\|_{\dot{H}^{k}}\leq\sum_{j\geq 1}\|Q_{j,R}\|_{\dot{H}^{k}}\lesssim_{Q,s}R^{s_{c}-k},\qquad k=s,k_{\star}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">As <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi_{R}Q\in C_{c}^{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi_{R}Q\in C_{c}^{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math>, this also proves <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q\in\mathcal{X}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q\in\mathcal{X}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Estimate (<a href="#S4.E56" title="In 4.1. Functional setting ‣ 4. Self-similar blow-up ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">56</span></a>) gives <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\widehat{h}\|_{1}\lesssim_{s}\|h\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0em">≲</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\widehat{h}\|_{1}\lesssim_{s}\|h\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, for <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=s,k_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=s,k_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>, the inequality <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="|\xi|^{k}\lesssim_{k}|\eta|^{k}+|\xi-\eta|^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">≲</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>η</mi><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">+</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\xi|^{k}\lesssim_{k}|\eta|^{k}+|\xi-\eta|^{k}</annotation></semantics></math> and Young’s convolution inequality give</p>
<table id="S4.Ex118" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex118.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|fg\|_{\dot{H}^{k}}\lesssim_{k}\|f\|_{\dot{H}^{k}}\|\widehat{g}\|_{1}+\|\widehat{f}\|_{1}\|g\|_{\dot{H}^{k}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>f</mi><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0em">≲</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">+</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|fg\|_{\dot{H}^{k}}\lesssim_{k}\|f\|_{\dot{H}^{k}}\|\widehat{g}\|_{1}+\|\widehat{f}\|_{1}\|g\|_{\dot{H}^{k}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Thus <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> is an algebra:</p>
<table id="S4.E59" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(59)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|fg\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}\leq C_{s}\|f\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}\|g\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|fg\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}\leq C_{s}\|f\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}\|g\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p4.3" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> is odd, <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}(v)</annotation></semantics></math> is a polynomial in <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q,\overline{Q},v,\overline{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q,\overline{Q},v,\overline{v}</annotation></semantics></math> whose terms have degree at least two in <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v,\overline{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v,\overline{v}</annotation></semantics></math>. Lemma <a href="#S4.Thmthm2" title="Lemma 4.2. ‣ 4.1. Functional setting ‣ 4. Self-similar blow-up ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a> and the algebra estimate therefore give</p>
<table id="S4.E60" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(60)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathcal{F}(v)-\mathcal{F}(w)\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}\leq C_{Q,s}\bigl(\|v\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}+\|w\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}+\|v\|^{p}_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}+\|w\|^{p}_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}\bigr)\|v-w\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mi>p</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mi>p</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathcal{F}(v)-\mathcal{F}(w)\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}\leq C_{Q,s}\bigl(\|v\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}+\|w\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}+\|v\|^{p}_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}+\|w\|^{p}_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}\bigr)\|v-w\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmthm3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmthm3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 4.3</span></span><span id="S4.Thmthm3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmthm3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmthm3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S4.Thmthm3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{Q}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.Thmthm3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> generates a strongly continuous group <math id="S4.Thmthm3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{Q}(\tau)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{Q}(\tau)</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, for any <math id="S4.Thmthm3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{0}\in\mathcal{X}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{0}\in\mathcal{X}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists <math id="S4.Thmthm3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that a unique mild solution in <math id="S4.Thmthm3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C([0,T];\mathcal{X}_{s})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C([0,T];\mathcal{X}_{s})</annotation></semantics></math> solves (<a href="#S4.E52" title="In 4. Self-similar blow-up ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">52</span></a>) with initial data <math id="S4.Thmthm3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">The unperturbed operator <math id="S4.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> generates the group <math id="S4.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{0}(\tau)=e^{\tau\mathcal{A}_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{0}(\tau)=e^{\tau\mathcal{A}_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math>, given by</span></p>
<table id="S4.E61" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(61)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(S_{0}(\tau)h)(y)=e^{(-\frac{1}{p-1}+i\Omega)\tau}\bigl(e^{i(1-e^{-\tau})\Delta}h\bigr)(e^{-\frac{\tau}{2}}y),\qquad\tau\in\mathbb{R}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(S_{0}(\tau)h)(y)=e^{(-\frac{1}{p-1}+i\Omega)\tau}\bigl(e^{i(1-e^{-\tau})\Delta}h\bigr)(e^{-\frac{\tau}{2}}y),\qquad\tau\in\mathbb{R}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="S4.SS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=s,k_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=s,k_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>, unitarity of the Schrödinger group on <math id="S4.SS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{H}^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{H}^{k}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS1.p5.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|h(\lambda\cdot)\|_{\dot{H}^{k}}=\lambda^{k-d/2}\|h\|_{\dot{H}^{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em">=</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>h</mi><msub><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|h(\lambda\cdot)\|_{\dot{H}^{k}}=\lambda^{k-d/2}\|h\|_{\dot{H}^{k}}</annotation></semantics></math> give</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex119" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex119.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|S_{0}(\tau)h\|_{\dot{H}^{k}}=e^{\frac{(s_{c}-k)\tau}{2}}\|h\|_{\dot{H}^{k}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msup></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msup></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|S_{0}(\tau)h\|_{\dot{H}^{k}}=e^{\frac{(s_{c}-k)\tau}{2}}\|h\|_{\dot{H}^{k}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">since <math id="S4.SS1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{c}=d/2-2/(p-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{c}=d/2-2/(p-1)</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus we have for <math id="S4.SS1.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex120" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex120.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|S_{0}(\tau)h\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}\leq e^{\frac{(s_{c}-s)\tau}{2}}\|h\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|S_{0}(\tau)h\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}\leq e^{\frac{(s_{c}-s)\tau}{2}}\|h\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text">For radial <math id="S4.SS1.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{c}^{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{c}^{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> data, continuity at <math id="S4.SS1.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=0</annotation></semantics></math> follows from dominated convergence in Fourier space and continuity of dilations. Density and the preceding locally uniform operator bound extend this to every <math id="S4.SS1.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in\mathcal{X}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in\mathcal{X}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>, proving strong continuity.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Moreover, <math id="S4.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\mathrm{diag}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>diag</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\mathrm{diag}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\mathrm{off}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>off</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\mathrm{off}}</annotation></semantics></math> belong to <math id="S4.SS1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> by Lemma <a href="#S4.Thmthm2" title="Lemma 4.2. ‣ 4.1. Functional setting ‣ 4. Self-similar blow-up ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a> and the algebra estimate (<a href="#S4.E59" title="In 4.1. Functional setting ‣ 4. Self-similar blow-up ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">59</span></a>). Thus <math id="S4.SS1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{Q}-\mathcal{A}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{Q}-\mathcal{A}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> is a bounded real-linear operator on <math id="S4.SS1.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>. The bounded perturbation theorem yields a strongly continuous group <math id="S4.SS1.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{Q}(\tau)=e^{\tau\mathcal{A}_{Q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{Q}(\tau)=e^{\tau\mathcal{A}_{Q}}</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="S4.SS1.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D(\mathcal{A}_{Q})=D(\mathcal{A}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D(\mathcal{A}_{Q})=D(\mathcal{A}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>. Now we show the local well-posedness of (<a href="#S4.E52" title="In 4. Self-similar blow-up ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">52</span></a>) in <math id="S4.SS1.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>. Using the Duhamel formula, we consider</span></p>
<table id="S4.E62" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(62)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v(\tau)=S_{Q}(\tau)v_{0}+\int_{0}^{\tau}S_{Q}(\tau-\sigma)\mathcal{F}(v(\sigma))\,d\sigma." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>τ</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v(\tau)=S_{Q}(\tau)v_{0}+\int_{0}^{\tau}S_{Q}(\tau-\sigma)\mathcal{F}(v(\sigma))\,d\sigma.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">Estimate (<a href="#S4.E60" title="In 4.1. Functional setting ‣ 4. Self-similar blow-up ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">60</span></a>) makes <math id="S4.SS1.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> locally Lipschitz near zero. The local bound on <math id="S4.SS1.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{Q}</annotation></semantics></math> thus makes the equation (<a href="#S4.E62" title="In Proof. ‣ 4.1. Functional setting ‣ 4. Self-similar blow-up ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">62</span></a>) a contraction on a suitable ball in <math id="S4.SS1.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C([0,T];\mathcal{X}_{s})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C([0,T];\mathcal{X}_{s})</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S4.SS1.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> small, proving local existence, uniqueness, and continuous dependence for (<a href="#S4.E52" title="In 4. Self-similar blow-up ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">52</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">For the cutoff <math id="S4.SS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> in the proof of Lemma <a href="#S4.Thmthm2" title="Lemma 4.2. ‣ 4.1. Functional setting ‣ 4. Self-similar blow-up ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>, the estimate (<a href="#S4.E58" title="In Proof. ‣ 4.1. Functional setting ‣ 4. Self-similar blow-up ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">58</span></a>) shows that localization is small in <math id="S4.SS1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>. The profile bounds and annular scaling give the estimate for the commutator <math id="S4.SS1.p7.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|[\mathcal{A}_{0},\chi_{R}]Q\|_{\dot{H}^{k}}\lesssim_{Q,s}R^{s_{c}-k}\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>Q</mi><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msup></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.0835em">≲</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|[\mathcal{A}_{0},\chi_{R}]Q\|_{\dot{H}^{k}}\lesssim_{Q,s}R^{s_{c}-k}\to 0</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S4.SS1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=s,k_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=s,k_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>. Differentiating (<a href="#S4.E61" title="In Proof. ‣ 4.1. Functional setting ‣ 4. Self-similar blow-up ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">61</span></a>) on Schwartz data gives <math id="S4.SS1.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\infty}_{c,\mathrm{rad}}\subset D(\mathcal{A}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>rad</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\infty}_{c,\mathrm{rad}}\subset D(\mathcal{A}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>. Also, the algebra estimate and (<a href="#S4.E58" title="In Proof. ‣ 4.1. Functional setting ‣ 4. Self-similar blow-up ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">58</span></a>) imply <math id="S4.SS1.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi_{R}N(Q)\to N(Q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi_{R}N(Q)\to N(Q)</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S4.SS1.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S4.SS1.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi_{R}Q\in D(\mathcal{A}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi_{R}Q\in D(\mathcal{A}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> and</p>
<table id="S4.Ex121" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex121.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{0}(\chi_{R}Q)=i\chi_{R}N(Q)+[\mathcal{A}_{0},\chi_{R}]Q\longrightarrow iN(Q)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{0}(\chi_{R}Q)=i\chi_{R}N(Q)+[\mathcal{A}_{0},\chi_{R}]Q\longrightarrow iN(Q),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p7.2" class="ltx_p">closedness of <math id="S4.SS1.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> yields <math id="S4.SS1.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q\in D(\mathcal{A}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q\in D(\mathcal{A}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS1.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{0}Q=iN(Q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{0}Q=iN(Q)</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus the profile <math id="S4.SS1.p7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> is a mild solution of</p>
<table id="S4.E63" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(63)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q=S_{0}(\tau)Q-i\int_{0}^{\tau}S_{0}(\tau-\sigma)N(Q)\,d\sigma." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>τ</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q=S_{0}(\tau)Q-i\int_{0}^{\tau}S_{0}(\tau-\sigma)N(Q)\,d\sigma.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p7.3" class="ltx_p">Consequently, subtracting <math id="S4.SS1.p7.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> identifies a solution of the full nonlinear equation with the <math id="S4.SS1.p7.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> perturbation.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.2. </span>Spectral theory for the linearized operator</h3>

<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our spectral analysis follows the strategy of obtaining dissipativity
modulo a compact perturbation; see
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib52" title="" class="ltx_ref">52</a>, <a href="#bib.bib54" title="" class="ltx_ref">54</a>, <a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>]</cite>.
We represent the lower-order energy remainder by a compact operator
using the Riesz representation theorem, in a manner analogous to
the construction in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">21</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We use the matrix formulation and the associated
<math id="S4.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{J}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{J}</annotation></semantics></math>-invariance argument; see
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib60" title="" class="ltx_ref">60</a>, <a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">46</a>]</cite>.Fix <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in(s_{c},d/2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in(s_{c},d/2)</annotation></semantics></math> and set <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{s}=(s_{c}-s)/2&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{s}=(s_{c}-s)/2&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
The spectral analysis takes place
on the complex Hilbert space</p>
<table id="S4.Ex122" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex122.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}_{s}=\mathcal{X}_{s}\times\mathcal{X}_{s},\qquad\|(f,g)\|_{\mathbf{X}_{s}}^{2}=\tfrac{1}{2}\bigl(\|f\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}^{2}+\|g\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}^{2}\bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}_{s}=\mathcal{X}_{s}\times\mathcal{X}_{s},\qquad\|(f,g)\|_{\mathbf{X}_{s}}^{2}=\tfrac{1}{2}\bigl(\|f\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}^{2}+\|g\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}^{2}\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Scalar perturbations are identified with the real-linear subspace</p>
<table id="S4.E64" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(64)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota h=\begin{pmatrix}h\\
\overline{h}\end{pmatrix},\qquad\mathbf{X}_{s,+}=\iota\mathcal{X}_{s}=\{\mathbf{h}\in\mathbf{X}_{s}:\mathcal{J}\mathbf{h}=\mathbf{h}\},\qquad\mathcal{J}\begin{pmatrix}f\\
g\end{pmatrix}=\begin{pmatrix}\overline{g}\\
\overline{f}\end{pmatrix}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ι</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mi>h</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ι</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>𝐡</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐡</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐡</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mi>f</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>g</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota h=\begin{pmatrix}h\\
\overline{h}\end{pmatrix},\qquad\mathbf{X}_{s,+}=\iota\mathcal{X}_{s}=\{\mathbf{h}\in\mathbf{X}_{s}:\mathcal{J}\mathbf{h}=\mathbf{h}\},\qquad\mathcal{J}\begin{pmatrix}f\\
g\end{pmatrix}=\begin{pmatrix}\overline{g}\\
\overline{f}\end{pmatrix}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Thus <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ι</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota</annotation></semantics></math> is a real-linear isometry and <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{J}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{J}</annotation></semantics></math> is an antilinear isometric involution.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Ch=\overline{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Ch=\overline{h}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\mathcal{A}_{0}}=C\mathcal{A}_{0}C=-i\Delta-\tfrac{1}{2}y\cdot\nabla_{y}-\frac{1}{p-1}-i\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\mathcal{A}_{0}}=C\mathcal{A}_{0}C=-i\Delta-\tfrac{1}{2}y\cdot\nabla_{y}-\frac{1}{p-1}-i\Omega</annotation></semantics></math>, with domain <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="CD(\mathcal{A}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">CD(\mathcal{A}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>. The matrix linearized operator is</p>
<table id="S4.Ex123" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex123.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}_{Q}=\mathbf{A}_{0}+\mathbf{B},\qquad\mathbf{A}_{0}=\begin{pmatrix}\mathcal{A}_{0}&amp;0\\
0&amp;\overline{\mathcal{A}_{0}}\end{pmatrix},\qquad\mathbf{B}=\begin{pmatrix}-iV_{\mathrm{diag}}&amp;-iV_{\mathrm{off}}\\
i\overline{V_{\mathrm{off}}}&amp;iV_{\mathrm{diag}}\end{pmatrix}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>𝐁</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mover accent="true"><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐁</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>diag</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>off</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>off</mi></msub><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>diag</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}_{Q}=\mathbf{A}_{0}+\mathbf{B},\qquad\mathbf{A}_{0}=\begin{pmatrix}\mathcal{A}_{0}&amp;0\\
0&amp;\overline{\mathcal{A}_{0}}\end{pmatrix},\qquad\mathbf{B}=\begin{pmatrix}-iV_{\mathrm{diag}}&amp;-iV_{\mathrm{off}}\\
i\overline{V_{\mathrm{off}}}&amp;iV_{\mathrm{diag}}\end{pmatrix},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where the coefficients <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\mathrm{diag}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>diag</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\mathrm{diag}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\mathrm{off}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>off</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\mathrm{off}}</annotation></semantics></math> are defined in (<a href="#S4.E53" title="In 4. Self-similar blow-up ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">53</span></a>). Now we apply the bounded perturbation theorem as in the argument of Lemma <a href="#S4.Thmthm3" title="Lemma 4.3. ‣ 4.1. Functional setting ‣ 4. Self-similar blow-up ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a> to the diagonal group</p>
<table id="S4.Ex124" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex124.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}_{0}(\tau)=\begin{pmatrix}S_{0}(\tau)&amp;0\\
0&amp;CS_{0}(\tau)C\end{pmatrix}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐒</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}_{0}(\tau)=\begin{pmatrix}S_{0}(\tau)&amp;0\\
0&amp;CS_{0}(\tau)C\end{pmatrix}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Thus <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}_{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}_{Q}</annotation></semantics></math>, with domain <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D(\mathcal{A}_{0})\times CD(\mathcal{A}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D(\mathcal{A}_{0})\times CD(\mathcal{A}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>, generates a strongly continuous group <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}_{Q}(\tau)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}_{Q}(\tau)</annotation></semantics></math>. Direct computation gives</p>
<table id="S4.Ex125" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex125.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{J}\mathbf{A}_{Q}=\mathbf{A}_{Q}\mathcal{J},\qquad\mathbf{A}_{Q}\iota=\iota\mathcal{A}_{Q},\qquad\mathbf{S}_{Q}(\tau)\iota=\iota S_{Q}(\tau)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ι</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ι</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ι</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ι</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{J}\mathbf{A}_{Q}=\mathbf{A}_{Q}\mathcal{J},\qquad\mathbf{A}_{Q}\iota=\iota\mathcal{A}_{Q},\qquad\mathbf{S}_{Q}(\tau)\iota=\iota S_{Q}(\tau).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p3.4" class="ltx_p">The first identity holds on <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D(\mathbf{A}_{Q})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D(\mathbf{A}_{Q})</annotation></semantics></math>, which <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{J}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{J}</annotation></semantics></math> preserves, and the second on <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D(\mathcal{A}_{Q})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D(\mathcal{A}_{Q})</annotation></semantics></math>; the group identity follows by uniqueness. In particular, the matrix evolution preserves <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}_{s,+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}_{s,+}</annotation></semantics></math> and agrees there with the scalar linearized evolution.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmthm4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmthm4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 4.4</span></span><span id="S4.Thmthm4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmthm4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmthm4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmthm4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There is a bounded compact operator <math id="S4.Thmthm4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math>
on <math id="S4.Thmthm4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="S4.E65" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(65)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Re}\langle\mathbf{A}_{Q}\mathbf{h},\mathbf{h}\rangle_{\mathbf{X}_{s}}\leq\gamma_{s}\|\mathbf{h}\|_{\mathbf{X}_{s}}^{2}+\operatorname{Re}\langle\mathcal{R}\mathbf{h},\mathbf{h}\rangle_{\mathbf{X}_{s}},\qquad\mathbf{h}\in D(\mathbf{A}_{Q})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐡</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐡</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐡</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐡</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐡</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐡</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Re}\langle\mathbf{A}_{Q}\mathbf{h},\mathbf{h}\rangle_{\mathbf{X}_{s}}\leq\gamma_{s}\|\mathbf{h}\|_{\mathbf{X}_{s}}^{2}+\operatorname{Re}\langle\mathcal{R}\mathbf{h},\mathbf{h}\rangle_{\mathbf{X}_{s}},\qquad\mathbf{h}\in D(\mathbf{A}_{Q}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.Thmthm4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmthm4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The operator <math id="S4.Thmthm4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}_{Q}-\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}_{Q}-\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, with domain <math id="S4.Thmthm4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D(\mathbf{A}_{Q})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D(\mathbf{A}_{Q})</annotation></semantics></math>, generates a strongly continuous semigroup <math id="S4.Thmthm4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐔</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{U}</annotation></semantics></math>, and</span></p>
<table id="S4.E66" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(66)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathbf{U}(\tau)\|_{\mathbf{X}_{s}\to\mathbf{X}_{s}}\leq e^{\gamma_{s}\tau},\qquad\tau\geq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐔</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbf{U}(\tau)\|_{\mathbf{X}_{s}\to\mathbf{X}_{s}}\leq e^{\gamma_{s}\tau},\qquad\tau\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">We first establish the compactness of the lower-order error terms <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{B}\mathbf{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐁𝐡</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{B}\mathbf{h}</annotation></semantics></math> in the energy estimate. Let <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi\in C_{c}^{\infty}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi\in C_{c}^{\infty}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math> be radial, equal to one on the unit ball, and supported in the ball of radius two. Let <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h=h_{\mathrm{lo}}+h_{\mathrm{hi}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>lo</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>hi</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h=h_{\mathrm{lo}}+h_{\mathrm{hi}}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\mathrm{lo}}=\mathcal{F}^{-1}\psi(|\xi|)\mathcal{F}h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>lo</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\mathrm{lo}}=\mathcal{F}^{-1}\psi(|\xi|)\mathcal{F}h</annotation></semantics></math> is the low frequency part of <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s&lt;d/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s&lt;d/2</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex126" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex126.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\partial^{\beta}h_{\mathrm{lo}}\|_{\infty}\lesssim_{\beta}\left(\int_{|\xi|\leq 2}|\xi|^{2|\beta|-2s}\,d\xi\right)^{1/2}\|h\|_{\dot{H}^{s}}\lesssim_{\beta}\|h\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∥</mo><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>β</mi></msup><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>lo</mi></msub><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.0835em">≲</mo><mi>β</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ξ</mi><msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>h</mi><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>s</mi></msup></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0em">≲</mo><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>h</mi><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\partial^{\beta}h_{\mathrm{lo}}\|_{\infty}\lesssim_{\beta}\left(\int_{|\xi|\leq 2}|\xi|^{2|\beta|-2s}\,d\xi\right)^{1/2}\|h\|_{\dot{H}^{s}}\lesssim_{\beta}\|h\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">For the high-frequency part, we have <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|h_{\mathrm{hi}}\|_{H^{k_{\star}}}\lesssim\|h\|_{\dot{H}^{k_{\star}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>hi</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><msub><mi>k</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></msup></msub><mo>≲</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><msub><mi>k</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></msup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|h_{\mathrm{hi}}\|_{H^{k_{\star}}}\lesssim\|h\|_{\dot{H}^{k_{\star}}}</annotation></semantics></math>. These estimates give the localization bound below. Let <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi_{L}(y)=\chi(y/L)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi_{L}(y)=\chi(y/L)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi\in C_{c}^{\infty}(B_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi\in C_{c}^{\infty}(B_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> is radial and equals one on <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. For each fixed <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>, localization maps <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> boundedly into <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{k_{\star}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>H</mi><msub><mi>k</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{k_{\star}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, choosing <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max\{s,d/2\}&lt;r&lt;k_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max\{s,d/2\}&lt;r&lt;k_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>, Rellich compactness shows that <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\mapsto\chi_{L}h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\mapsto\chi_{L}h</annotation></semantics></math> is compact into <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>H</mi><mi>r</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{r}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since multiplication by any of the factors <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in\{V_{\mathrm{diag}},V_{\mathrm{off}},\overline{V_{\mathrm{off}}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>diag</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>off</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>off</mi></msub><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in\{V_{\mathrm{diag}},V_{\mathrm{off}},\overline{V_{\mathrm{off}}}\}</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded on <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>H</mi><mi>r</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{r}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\chi_{L}u)h=u(\chi_{L}h)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\chi_{L}u)h=u(\chi_{L}h)</annotation></semantics></math>, the corresponding localized multiplication operators are compact from <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> into <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{H}^{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>s</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{H}^{s}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">For the tails, (<a href="#S4.E55" title="In Lemma 4.1. ‣ 4. Self-similar blow-up ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">55</span></a>) and the same dyadic scaling argument as in Lemma <a href="#S4.Thmthm2" title="Lemma 4.2. ‣ 4.1. Functional setting ‣ 4. Self-similar blow-up ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a> give, for <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in\{V_{\mathrm{diag}},V_{\mathrm{off}},\overline{V_{\mathrm{off}}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>diag</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>off</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>off</mi></msub><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in\{V_{\mathrm{diag}},V_{\mathrm{off}},\overline{V_{\mathrm{off}}}\}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex127" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex127.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|(1-\chi_{L})u\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}\lesssim L^{\frac{d}{2}-2-s}\lesssim L^{s_{c}-s}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msub><mo>≲</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup><mo>≲</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|(1-\chi_{L})u\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}\lesssim L^{\frac{d}{2}-2-s}\lesssim L^{s_{c}-s}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Together with the algebra estimate (<a href="#S4.E59" title="In 4.1. Functional setting ‣ 4. Self-similar blow-up ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">59</span></a>), this gives</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex128" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex128.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|(1-\chi_{L})V_{\mathrm{diag}}h\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}+\|(1-\chi_{L})V_{\mathrm{off}}h\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}\lesssim L^{s_{c}-s}\|h\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>diag</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>off</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo>≲</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|(1-\chi_{L})V_{\mathrm{diag}}h\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}+\|(1-\chi_{L})V_{\mathrm{off}}h\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}\lesssim L^{s_{c}-s}\|h\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="S4.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s&gt;s_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s&gt;s_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>, the right-hand coefficient tends to zero. Therefore</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex129" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex129.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{h}\longmapsto|D|^{s}\mathbf{B}\mathbf{h}\quad\text{is compact from }\mathbf{X}_{s}\text{ into }L^{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d};\mathbb{C}^{2})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐡</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟼</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐁𝐡</mi></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mtext>is compact from </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> into </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{h}\longmapsto|D|^{s}\mathbf{B}\mathbf{h}\quad\text{is compact from }\mathbf{X}_{s}\text{ into }L^{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d};\mathbb{C}^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now let</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex130" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex130.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}\mathbf{h}=[\nabla^{k_{\star}},\mathbf{B}]\mathbf{h}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐡</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐁</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐡</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}\mathbf{h}=[\nabla^{k_{\star}},\mathbf{B}]\mathbf{h}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">Each component is a finite sum of terms <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\partial^{\alpha}u)\partial^{\beta}h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>β</mi></msup><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\partial^{\alpha}u)\partial^{\beta}h</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in\{V_{\mathrm{diag}},V_{\mathrm{off}},\overline{V_{\mathrm{off}}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>diag</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>off</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>off</mi></msub><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in\{V_{\mathrm{diag}},V_{\mathrm{off}},\overline{V_{\mathrm{off}}}\}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\alpha|\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\alpha|\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\alpha|+|\beta|=k_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\alpha|+|\beta|=k_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>. The localized term <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi_{L}(\partial^{\alpha}u)\partial^{\beta}h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>β</mi></msup><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi_{L}(\partial^{\alpha}u)\partial^{\beta}h</annotation></semantics></math> is compact into <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> by local <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{k_{\star}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>H</mi><msub><mi>k</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{k_{\star}}</annotation></semantics></math> control, Rellich compactness, and <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\beta|\leq k_{\star}-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\beta|\leq k_{\star}-1</annotation></semantics></math>. For its tail, (<a href="#S4.E54" title="In Lemma 4.1. ‣ 4. Self-similar blow-up ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">54</span></a>) gives:</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex131"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex131.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|(1-\chi_{L})(\partial^{\alpha}u)\partial^{\beta}h_{\mathrm{lo}}\|_{L^{2}}\lesssim\|(1-\chi_{L})(\partial^{\alpha}u)\|_{L^{2}}\|\partial^{\beta}h_{\mathrm{lo}}\|_{L^{\infty}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>β</mi></msup><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>lo</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><mo>≲</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>β</mi></msup><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>lo</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|(1-\chi_{L})(\partial^{\alpha}u)\partial^{\beta}h_{\mathrm{lo}}\|_{L^{2}}\lesssim\|(1-\chi_{L})(\partial^{\alpha}u)\|_{L^{2}}\|\partial^{\beta}h_{\mathrm{lo}}\|_{L^{\infty}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex131.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lesssim L^{d/2-2-|\alpha|}\|h\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≲</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lesssim L^{d/2-2-|\alpha|}\|h\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex132"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex132.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|(1-\chi_{L})(\partial^{\alpha}u)\partial^{\beta}h_{\mathrm{hi}}\|_{L^{2}}\lesssim\|(1-\chi_{L})(\partial^{\alpha}u)\|_{L^{\infty}}\|\partial^{\beta}h_{\mathrm{hi}}\|_{L^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>β</mi></msup><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>hi</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><mo>≲</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>β</mi></msup><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>hi</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|(1-\chi_{L})(\partial^{\alpha}u)\partial^{\beta}h_{\mathrm{hi}}\|_{L^{2}}\lesssim\|(1-\chi_{L})(\partial^{\alpha}u)\|_{L^{\infty}}\|\partial^{\beta}h_{\mathrm{hi}}\|_{L^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex132.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lesssim L^{-2-|\alpha|}\|h\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≲</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lesssim L^{-2-|\alpha|}\|h\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">Both exponents are negative because <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\leq 5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\leq 5</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\alpha|\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\alpha|\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math> is compact from <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> into <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d};\mathbb{C}^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d};\mathbb{C}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> as well. It follows that</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex133" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex133.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{K}\mathbf{h}=(|D|^{s}\mathbf{B}\mathbf{h},\mathcal{C}\mathbf{h}):\mathbf{X}_{s}\longrightarrow\mathcal{Y}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐡</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐁𝐡</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐡</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}\mathbf{h}=(|D|^{s}\mathbf{B}\mathbf{h},\mathcal{C}\mathbf{h}):\mathbf{X}_{s}\longrightarrow\mathcal{Y}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p7.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p7.4.1" class="ltx_text">is compact, where <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Y}</annotation></semantics></math> is the Hilbert direct sum of these two <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> spaces, with <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|(f,g)\|_{\mathcal{Y}}^{2}=\frac{1}{2}(\|f\|_{L^{2}}^{2}+\|g\|_{L^{2}}^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|(f,g)\|_{\mathcal{Y}}^{2}=\frac{1}{2}(\|f\|_{L^{2}}^{2}+\|g\|_{L^{2}}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Next we work on the energy estimate. The calculations are first made on radial Schwartz pairs. Differentiating the free-group norm identity following (<a href="#S4.E61" title="In Proof. ‣ 4.1. Functional setting ‣ 4. Self-similar blow-up ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">61</span></a>) gives</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex134" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex134.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\operatorname{Re}\langle|D|^{r}\mathbf{A}_{0}\mathbf{h},|D|^{r}\mathbf{h}\rangle_{L^{2}}=\frac{s_{c}-r}{2}\|\mathbf{h}\|_{\dot{H}^{r}}^{2},\qquad r=s,k_{\star}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Re</mi><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>D</mi><msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>r</mi></msup><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>𝐡</mi><mo>,</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>D</mi><msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>r</mi></msup><mi>𝐡</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝐡</mi><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>r</mi></msup><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Re}\langle|D|^{r}\mathbf{A}_{0}\mathbf{h},|D|^{r}\mathbf{h}\rangle_{L^{2}}=\frac{s_{c}-r}{2}\|\mathbf{h}\|_{\dot{H}^{r}}^{2},\qquad r=s,k_{\star}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">At the top order,</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex135" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex135.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla^{k_{\star}}(\mathbf{B}\mathbf{h})=\mathbf{B}\nabla^{k_{\star}}\mathbf{h}+\mathcal{C}\mathbf{h}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐁𝐡</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐁</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></msup><mi>𝐡</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐡</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla^{k_{\star}}(\mathbf{B}\mathbf{h})=\mathbf{B}\nabla^{k_{\star}}\mathbf{h}+\mathcal{C}\mathbf{h}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">Because <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\mathrm{diag}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>diag</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\mathrm{diag}}</annotation></semantics></math> is real, the diagonal terms of <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐁</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{B}</annotation></semantics></math> make zero real contribution. For any pair of tensors <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐰</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{w}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex136" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex136.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Re}\langle\mathbf{B}\mathbf{w},\mathbf{w}\rangle_{L^{2}}\leq\|V_{\mathrm{off}}\|_{\infty}\|\mathbf{w}\|_{L^{2}}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>𝐁𝐰</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>off</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐰</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Re}\langle\mathbf{B}\mathbf{w},\mathbf{w}\rangle_{L^{2}}\leq\|V_{\mathrm{off}}\|_{\infty}\|\mathbf{w}\|_{L^{2}}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p8.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p8.4.1" class="ltx_text">Our choice of <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> implies</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex137" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex137.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{s_{c}-k_{\star}}{2}+\|V_{\mathrm{off}}\|_{\infty}\leq\frac{s_{c}-s}{2}=\gamma_{s}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>off</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{s_{c}-k_{\star}}{2}+\|V_{\mathrm{off}}\|_{\infty}\leq\frac{s_{c}-s}{2}=\gamma_{s}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p8.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p8.5.1" class="ltx_text">Define the bounded isometry</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex138" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex138.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}\mathbf{h}=(|D|^{s}\mathbf{h},\nabla^{k_{\star}}\mathbf{h}):\mathbf{X}_{s}\longrightarrow\mathcal{Y},\qquad\|\mathcal{E}\mathbf{h}\|_{\mathcal{Y}}=\|\mathbf{h}\|_{\mathbf{X}_{s}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐡</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐡</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></msup><mi>𝐡</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐡</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐡</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}\mathbf{h}=(|D|^{s}\mathbf{h},\nabla^{k_{\star}}\mathbf{h}):\mathbf{X}_{s}\longrightarrow\mathcal{Y},\qquad\|\mathcal{E}\mathbf{h}\|_{\mathcal{Y}}=\|\mathbf{h}\|_{\mathbf{X}_{s}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p8.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p8.6.1" class="ltx_text">Combining the two derivative levels gives</span></p>
<table id="S4.E67" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(67)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Re}\langle\mathbf{A}_{Q}\mathbf{h},\mathbf{h}\rangle_{\mathbf{X}_{s}}\leq\gamma_{s}\|\mathbf{h}\|_{\mathbf{X}_{s}}^{2}+\operatorname{Re}\langle\mathcal{K}\mathbf{h},\mathcal{E}\mathbf{h}\rangle_{\mathcal{Y}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐡</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐡</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐡</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐡</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐡</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Re}\langle\mathbf{A}_{Q}\mathbf{h},\mathbf{h}\rangle_{\mathbf{X}_{s}}\leq\gamma_{s}\|\mathbf{h}\|_{\mathbf{X}_{s}}^{2}+\operatorname{Re}\langle\mathcal{K}\mathbf{h},\mathcal{E}\mathbf{h}\rangle_{\mathcal{Y}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p8.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p8.7.1" class="ltx_text">The free energy identity holds for every <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{h}\in D(\mathbf{A}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐡</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{h}\in D(\mathbf{A}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>. The estimate for the bounded perturbation <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐁</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{B}</annotation></semantics></math> extends from radial Schwartz pairs to <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> by density. Since <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D(\mathbf{A}_{Q})=D(\mathbf{A}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D(\mathbf{A}_{Q})=D(\mathbf{A}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>, their combination proves (<a href="#S4.E67" title="In Proof. ‣ 4.2. Spectral theory for the linearized operator ‣ 4. Self-similar blow-up ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">67</span></a>) on <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D(\mathbf{A}_{Q})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D(\mathbf{A}_{Q})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Use inner products linear in the first argument. The sesquilinear form</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex139" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex139.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{k}(\mathbf{h},\mathbf{g})=\langle\mathcal{K}\mathbf{h},\mathcal{E}\mathbf{g}\rangle_{\mathcal{Y}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔨</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐡</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐠</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐡</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐠</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{k}(\mathbf{h},\mathbf{g})=\langle\mathcal{K}\mathbf{h},\mathcal{E}\mathbf{g}\rangle_{\mathcal{Y}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">is bounded, since <math id="S4.SS2.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathfrak{k}(\mathbf{h},\mathbf{g})|\leq\|\mathcal{K}\|\,\|\mathbf{h}\|_{\mathbf{X}_{s}}\|\mathbf{g}\|_{\mathbf{X}_{s}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝔨</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐡</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐠</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐡</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐠</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathfrak{k}(\mathbf{h},\mathbf{g})|\leq\|\mathcal{K}\|\,\|\mathbf{h}\|_{\mathbf{X}_{s}}\|\mathbf{g}\|_{\mathbf{X}_{s}}</annotation></semantics></math>. By Riesz representation, there is a unique bounded complex-linear operator <math id="S4.SS2.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}:\mathbf{X}_{s}\to\mathbf{X}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}:\mathbf{X}_{s}\to\mathbf{X}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex140" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex140.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\mathcal{R}\mathbf{h},\mathbf{g}\rangle_{\mathbf{X}_{s}}=\mathfrak{k}(\mathbf{h},\mathbf{g}),\qquad\mathcal{R}=\mathcal{E}^{*}\mathcal{K}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐡</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐠</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔨</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐡</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐠</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\mathcal{R}\mathbf{h},\mathbf{g}\rangle_{\mathbf{X}_{s}}=\mathfrak{k}(\mathbf{h},\mathbf{g}),\qquad\mathcal{R}=\mathcal{E}^{*}\mathcal{K}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">The operator <math id="S4.SS2.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math> is compact because <math id="S4.SS2.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}</annotation></semantics></math> is compact and <math id="S4.SS2.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded. In particular,</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex141" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex141.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Re}\langle\mathcal{R}\mathbf{h},\mathbf{h}\rangle_{\mathbf{X}_{s}}=\operatorname{Re}\langle\mathcal{K}\mathbf{h},\mathcal{E}\mathbf{h}\rangle_{\mathcal{Y}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐡</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐡</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐡</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐡</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Re}\langle\mathcal{R}\mathbf{h},\mathbf{h}\rangle_{\mathbf{X}_{s}}=\operatorname{Re}\langle\mathcal{K}\mathbf{h},\mathcal{E}\mathbf{h}\rangle_{\mathcal{Y}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">Thus the preceding energy estimate proves (<a href="#S4.E65" title="In Lemma 4.4. ‣ 4.2. Spectral theory for the linearized operator ‣ 4. Self-similar blow-up ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">65</span></a>) directly.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="S4.SS2.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}_{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}_{Q}</annotation></semantics></math> already generates <math id="S4.SS2.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}_{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}_{Q}</annotation></semantics></math>, bounded perturbation by <math id="S4.SS2.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math> gives the auxiliary group <math id="S4.SS2.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐔</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{U}</annotation></semantics></math>, with generator <math id="S4.SS2.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}_{Q}-\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}_{Q}-\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math> and domain <math id="S4.SS2.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D(\mathbf{A}_{Q})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D(\mathbf{A}_{Q})</annotation></semantics></math>. This yields</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex142" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex142.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Re}\langle(\mathbf{A}_{Q}-\mathcal{R})\mathbf{h},\mathbf{h}\rangle_{\mathbf{X}_{s}}\leq\gamma_{s}\|\mathbf{h}\|_{\mathbf{X}_{s}}^{2},\qquad\mathbf{h}\in D(\mathbf{A}_{Q})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐡</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐡</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐡</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐡</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Re}\langle(\mathbf{A}_{Q}-\mathcal{R})\mathbf{h},\mathbf{h}\rangle_{\mathbf{X}_{s}}\leq\gamma_{s}\|\mathbf{h}\|_{\mathbf{X}_{s}}^{2},\qquad\mathbf{h}\in D(\mathbf{A}_{Q}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p11.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p11.2.1" class="ltx_text">Then</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex143" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex143.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{2}\frac{d}{d\tau}\|\mathbf{U}(\tau)\mathbf{h}\|_{\mathbf{X}_{s}}^{2}=\operatorname{Re}\langle(\mathbf{A}_{Q}-\mathcal{R})\mathbf{U}(\tau)\mathbf{h},\mathbf{U}(\tau)\mathbf{h}\rangle_{\mathbf{X}_{s}}\leq\gamma_{s}\|\mathbf{U}(\tau)\mathbf{h}\|_{\mathbf{X}_{s}}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐔</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐡</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐡</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐔</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐡</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐔</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐡</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{2}\frac{d}{d\tau}\|\mathbf{U}(\tau)\mathbf{h}\|_{\mathbf{X}_{s}}^{2}=\operatorname{Re}\langle(\mathbf{A}_{Q}-\mathcal{R})\mathbf{U}(\tau)\mathbf{h},\mathbf{U}(\tau)\mathbf{h}\rangle_{\mathbf{X}_{s}}\leq\gamma_{s}\|\mathbf{U}(\tau)\mathbf{h}\|_{\mathbf{X}_{s}}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p11.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p11.3.1" class="ltx_text">Gronwall’s inequality and density prove (<a href="#S4.E66" title="In Lemma 4.4. ‣ 4.2. Spectral theory for the linearized operator ‣ 4. Self-similar blow-up ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">66</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p13.1" class="ltx_p">We recall the following theorem.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmthm5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_thm">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmthm5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 4.5</span></span><span id="S4.Thmthm5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">32</a>, Corollary IV.2.11]</cite>)<span id="S4.Thmthm5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmthm5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmthm5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmthm5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that <math id="S4.Thmthm5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A:D(A)\subset X\to X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A:D(A)\subset X\to X</annotation></semantics></math> generates a strongly continuous
semigroup <math id="S4.Thmthm5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=(T(t))_{t\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=(T(t))_{t\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math> on a complex Banach space <math id="S4.Thmthm5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>.
Denote its growth bound and essential growth bound by
<math id="S4.Thmthm5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{0}(T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{0}(T)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.Thmthm5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{\mathrm{ess}}(T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>ess</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{\mathrm{ess}}(T)</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex144"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex144.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\omega_{0}(T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\omega_{0}(T)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex144.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\inf\{w\in\mathbb{R}:\exists M_{w}&lt;\infty,\ \|T(\tau)\|\leq M_{w}e^{w\tau}\text{ for all }\tau\geq 0\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">inf</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∃</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo rspace="0.389em">,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0.0835em">≤</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> for all </mtext><mi>τ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\inf\{w\in\mathbb{R}:\exists M_{w}&lt;\infty,\ \|T(\tau)\|\leq M_{w}e^{w\tau}\text{ for all }\tau\geq 0\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex145"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex145.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\omega_{\mathrm{ess}}(T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>ess</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\omega_{\mathrm{ess}}(T)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex145.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\inf\{w\in\mathbb{R}:\exists M_{w}&lt;\infty,\ \|T(\tau)\|_{\mathrm{ess}}\leq M_{w}e^{w\tau}\text{ for all }\tau\geq 0\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">inf</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∃</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo rspace="0.389em">,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mi>ess</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em">≤</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> for all </mtext><mi>τ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\inf\{w\in\mathbb{R}:\exists M_{w}&lt;\infty,\ \|T(\tau)\|_{\mathrm{ess}}\leq M_{w}e^{w\tau}\text{ for all }\tau\geq 0\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.Thmthm5.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmthm5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="S4.Thmthm5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|L\|_{\mathrm{ess}}=\inf\{\|L-K\|:K\text{ compact}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>ess</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">inf</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> compact</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|L\|_{\mathrm{ess}}=\inf\{\|L-K\|:K\text{ compact}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.Thmthm5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(A)</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the full spectrum of <math id="S4.Thmthm5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex146" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex146.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{0}(T)=\max\left\{\omega_{\mathrm{ess}}(T),\sup_{\lambda\in\sigma(A)}\operatorname{Re}\lambda\right\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>ess</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{0}(T)=\max\left\{\omega_{\mathrm{ess}}(T),\sup_{\lambda\in\sigma(A)}\operatorname{Re}\lambda\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.Thmthm5.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmthm5.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For each real number <math id="S4.Thmthm5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w&gt;\omega_{\mathrm{ess}}(T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>ess</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w&gt;\omega_{\mathrm{ess}}(T)</annotation></semantics></math>, the set</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex147" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex147.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(A)\cap\bigl\{\lambda\in\mathbb{C}:\operatorname{Re}\lambda\geq w\bigr\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℂ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(A)\cap\bigl\{\lambda\in\mathbb{C}:\operatorname{Re}\lambda\geq w\bigr\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.Thmthm5.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmthm5.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">is finite, and its associated spectral projection has finite rank. In particular, its elements are isolated eigenvalues of <math id="S4.Thmthm5.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> with finite algebraic multiplicity.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p14.1" class="ltx_p">By <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">32</a>, Proposition IV.2.12]</cite>, compact perturbations preserve the essential growth bound, so</p>
<table id="S4.E68" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(68)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{\mathrm{ess}}(\mathbf{S}_{Q})=\omega_{\mathrm{ess}}(\mathbf{U})\leq\omega_{0}(\mathbf{U})\leq\gamma_{s}&lt;0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>ess</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>ess</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐔</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐔</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{\mathrm{ess}}(\mathbf{S}_{Q})=\omega_{\mathrm{ess}}(\mathbf{U})\leq\omega_{0}(\mathbf{U})\leq\gamma_{s}&lt;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p14.2" class="ltx_p">Then in our case Corollary <a href="#S4.Thmthm5" title="Theorem 4.5 ([, Corollary IV.2.11]). ‣ 4.2. Spectral theory for the linearized operator ‣ 4. Self-similar blow-up ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.5</span></a> gives the following proposition.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmthm6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_prop">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmthm6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 4.6</span></span><span id="S4.Thmthm6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmthm6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmthm6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmthm6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For every <math id="S4.Thmthm6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex148" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex148.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(\mathbf{A}_{Q})\cap\{\lambda:\operatorname{Re}\lambda\geq\gamma_{s}+\delta\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(\mathbf{A}_{Q})\cap\{\lambda:\operatorname{Re}\lambda\geq\gamma_{s}+\delta\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.Thmthm6.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmthm6.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">is a finite set of isolated eigenvalues of finite algebraic multiplicity. In particular, the sum of the generalized eigenspaces with <math id="S4.Thmthm6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Re}\lambda\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Re}\lambda\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> is finite-dimensional.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p15.1" class="ltx_p">We now introduce spectral projections to separate the stable part of the linearized evolution from the finite-dimensional neutral and unstable parts. We denote the stable and unstable projections by <math id="S4.SS2.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\mathrm{st}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>st</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\mathrm{st}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.p15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\mathrm{un}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>un</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\mathrm{un}}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmthm7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_prop">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmthm7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 4.7</span></span><span id="S4.Thmthm7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmthm7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmthm7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmthm7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There are bounded real-linear projections <math id="S4.Thmthm7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\mathrm{un}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>un</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\mathrm{un}}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S4.Thmthm7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\mathrm{st}}=I-P_{\mathrm{un}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>st</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>un</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\mathrm{st}}=I-P_{\mathrm{un}}</annotation></semantics></math>, commuting with <math id="S4.Thmthm7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{Q}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.Thmthm7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{Q}</annotation></semantics></math>, such
that <math id="S4.Thmthm7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Ran}P_{\mathrm{un}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Ran</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>un</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Ran}P_{\mathrm{un}}</annotation></semantics></math> is finite-dimensional. For some
<math id="S4.Thmthm7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.Thmthm7.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S4.E69" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(69)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|S_{Q}(\tau)P_{\mathrm{st}}\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}\to\mathcal{X}_{s}}\leq Ce^{-\omega\tau},\qquad\tau\geq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>st</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|S_{Q}(\tau)P_{\mathrm{st}}\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}\to\mathcal{X}_{s}}\leq Ce^{-\omega\tau},\qquad\tau\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.Thmthm7.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmthm7.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For every <math id="S4.Thmthm7.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, we also have</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex149" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex149.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|S_{Q}(-\tau)P_{\mathrm{un}}\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}\to\mathcal{X}_{s}}\leq C_{\eta}e^{\eta\tau},\qquad\tau\geq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>un</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|S_{Q}(-\tau)P_{\mathrm{un}}\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}\to\mathcal{X}_{s}}\leq C_{\eta}e^{\eta\tau},\qquad\tau\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.SS2.p16" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Proposition <a href="#S4.Thmthm6" title="Proposition 4.6. ‣ 4.2. Spectral theory for the linearized operator ‣ 4. Self-similar blow-up ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.6</span></a>, there exists <math id="S4.SS2.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{s}&lt;-\omega&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{s}&lt;-\omega&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that the set</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex150" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex150.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{\mathrm{un}}=\sigma(\mathbf{A}_{Q})\cap\{\lambda:\operatorname{Re}\lambda\geq-\omega\}=\sigma(\mathbf{A}_{Q})\cap\{\lambda:\operatorname{Re}\lambda\geq 0\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>un</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{\mathrm{un}}=\sigma(\mathbf{A}_{Q})\cap\{\lambda:\operatorname{Re}\lambda\geq-\omega\}=\sigma(\mathbf{A}_{Q})\cap\{\lambda:\operatorname{Re}\lambda\geq 0\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p16.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p16.2.1" class="ltx_text">is finite and consists of isolated eigenvalues of finite algebraic multiplicity. Let <math id="S4.SS2.p16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}_{\mathrm{un}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>un</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}_{\mathrm{un}}</annotation></semantics></math> be the spectral projection associated with <math id="S4.SS2.p16.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{\mathrm{un}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>un</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{\mathrm{un}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and set <math id="S4.SS2.p16.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}_{\mathrm{st}}=I-\mathbf{P}_{\mathrm{un}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>st</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>un</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}_{\mathrm{st}}=I-\mathbf{P}_{\mathrm{un}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The standard spectral argument (e.g., <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>, Lemma 7.11]</cite>) gives the closed invariant decomposition</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex151" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex151.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}_{s}=\operatorname{Ran}\mathbf{P}_{\mathrm{un}}\oplus\operatorname{Ran}\mathbf{P}_{\mathrm{st}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Ran</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>un</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mi>Ran</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>st</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}_{s}=\operatorname{Ran}\mathbf{P}_{\mathrm{un}}\oplus\operatorname{Ran}\mathbf{P}_{\mathrm{st}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p16.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p16.3.1" class="ltx_text">From Corollary <a href="#S4.Thmthm5" title="Theorem 4.5 ([, Corollary IV.2.11]). ‣ 4.2. Spectral theory for the linearized operator ‣ 4. Self-similar blow-up ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.5</span></a> and (<a href="#S4.E68" title="In 4.2. Spectral theory for the linearized operator ‣ 4. Self-similar blow-up ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">68</span></a>), we have for <math id="S4.SS2.p16.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex152" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex152.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathbf{S}_{Q}(\tau)\mathbf{P}_{\mathrm{st}}\|\leq Ce^{-\omega\tau}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>st</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbf{S}_{Q}(\tau)\mathbf{P}_{\mathrm{st}}\|\leq Ce^{-\omega\tau}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p16.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p16.4.1" class="ltx_text">From the definition of <math id="S4.SS2.p16.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{\mathrm{un}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>un</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{\mathrm{un}}</annotation></semantics></math>, all eigenvalues have nonnegative real part. Jordan normal form therefore gives, for all <math id="S4.SS2.p16.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.p16.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex153" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex153.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathbf{S}_{Q}(-\tau)\mathbf{P}_{\mathrm{un}}\|\leq C_{\eta}e^{\eta\tau}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>un</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbf{S}_{Q}(-\tau)\mathbf{P}_{\mathrm{un}}\|\leq C_{\eta}e^{\eta\tau}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p16.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p16.5.1" class="ltx_text">Moreover, since <math id="S4.SS2.p16.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{J}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{J}</annotation></semantics></math> from (<a href="#S4.E64" title="In 4.2. Spectral theory for the linearized operator ‣ 4. Self-similar blow-up ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">64</span></a>) commutes with <math id="S4.SS2.p16.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}_{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}_{Q}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex154" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex154.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{J}(z\mathbf{I}-\mathbf{A}_{Q})^{-1}\mathcal{J}=(\bar{z}\mathbf{I}-\mathbf{A}_{Q})^{-1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{J}(z\mathbf{I}-\mathbf{A}_{Q})^{-1}\mathcal{J}=(\bar{z}\mathbf{I}-\mathbf{A}_{Q})^{-1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p16.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p16.6.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S4.SS2.p16.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}_{\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}_{\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> be the Riesz projection for <math id="S4.SS2.p16.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex155" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex155.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{J}\mathbf{P}_{\lambda}\mathcal{J}=\mathbf{P}_{\bar{\lambda}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{J}\mathbf{P}_{\lambda}\mathcal{J}=\mathbf{P}_{\bar{\lambda}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p16.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p16.7.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="S4.SS2.p16.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{\mathrm{un}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>un</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{\mathrm{un}}</annotation></semantics></math> is invariant under conjugation, we have <math id="S4.SS2.p16.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{J}\mathbf{P}_{\mathrm{un}}\mathcal{J}=\mathbf{P}_{\mathrm{un}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>un</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>un</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{J}\mathbf{P}_{\mathrm{un}}\mathcal{J}=\mathbf{P}_{\mathrm{un}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus <math id="S4.SS2.p16.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{J}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{J}</annotation></semantics></math> commutes with the projection <math id="S4.SS2.p16.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}_{\mathrm{un}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>un</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}_{\mathrm{un}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence <math id="S4.SS2.p16.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}_{\mathrm{un}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>un</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}_{\mathrm{un}}</annotation></semantics></math> preserves <math id="S4.SS2.p16.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}_{s,+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}_{s,+}</annotation></semantics></math> and induces bounded real-linear projections</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex156" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex156.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\alpha}=\iota^{-1}\mathbf{P}_{\alpha}\iota,\qquad\alpha\in\{\mathrm{un},\mathrm{st}\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ι</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ι</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>un</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>st</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\alpha}=\iota^{-1}\mathbf{P}_{\alpha}\iota,\qquad\alpha\in\{\mathrm{un},\mathrm{st}\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p16.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p16.8.1" class="ltx_text">with the required commutation properties.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p17" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p17.1" class="ltx_p">We record the two spectral directions induced by the symmetries of (<a href="#S1.E1" title="In 1. Introduction ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>). Phase invariance and time translation give, respectively,</p>
<table id="S4.Ex157" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex157.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{Q}(iQ)=0,\qquad\mathcal{A}_{Q}\left(-\frac{1}{p-1}Q+i\Omega Q-\frac{1}{2}y\cdot\nabla Q\right)=-\frac{1}{p-1}Q+i\Omega Q-\frac{1}{2}y\cdot\nabla Q." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{Q}(iQ)=0,\qquad\mathcal{A}_{Q}\left(-\frac{1}{p-1}Q+i\Omega Q-\frac{1}{2}y\cdot\nabla Q\right)=-\frac{1}{p-1}Q+i\Omega Q-\frac{1}{2}y\cdot\nabla Q.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p17.2" class="ltx_p">Indeed, the first identity follows by differentiating the constant phase, and the second one follows by differentiating the blow-up time. They can also be checked directly from the profile equation. The symbol bounds of Lemma <a href="#S4.Thmthm1" title="Lemma 4.1. ‣ 4. Self-similar blow-up ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a> show that both eigenfunctions belong to <math id="S4.SS2.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D(\mathcal{A}_{Q})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D(\mathcal{A}_{Q})</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence both directions lie in <math id="S4.SS2.p17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Ran}P_{\mathrm{un}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Ran</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>un</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Ran}P_{\mathrm{un}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and thus this space has dimension at least two. The construction below selects all neutral and unstable components at once, and therefore requires no separate modulation of the blow-up time or of the constant phase. We do not determine whether the two symmetry modes exhaust this space.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.3. </span>Stability and localization</h3>

<div id="S4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The following proposition gives a finite-codimensional stability result for the linearized evolution. This result allows us to construct global solutions to the nonlinear equation.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmthm8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_prop">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmthm8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 4.8</span></span><span id="S4.Thmthm8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmthm8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmthm8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmthm8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For the fixed <math id="S4.Thmthm8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.Thmthm8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega</annotation></semantics></math> above, and every <math id="S4.Thmthm8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\mu&lt;\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\mu&lt;\omega</annotation></semantics></math>,
there is <math id="S4.Thmthm8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{0}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{0}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that, for every
<math id="S4.Thmthm8.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi\in P_{\mathrm{st}}\mathcal{X}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>st</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi\in P_{\mathrm{st}}\mathcal{X}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> with
<math id="S4.Thmthm8.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\xi\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}&lt;\epsilon_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\xi\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}&lt;\epsilon_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, the perturbation equation
(<a href="#S4.E52" title="In 4. Self-similar blow-up ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">52</span></a>) admits a global solution <math id="S4.Thmthm8.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> with</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex158" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex158.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v(0)=\xi-\int_{0}^{\infty}S_{Q}(-\sigma)P_{\mathrm{un}}\mathcal{F}(v(\sigma))\,d\sigma" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>un</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v(0)=\xi-\int_{0}^{\infty}S_{Q}(-\sigma)P_{\mathrm{un}}\mathcal{F}(v(\sigma))\,d\sigma</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.Thmthm8.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmthm8.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and</span></p>
<table id="S4.E70" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(70)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{\tau\geq 0}e^{\mu\tau}\|v(\tau)\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}\lesssim\|\xi\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>≲</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{\tau\geq 0}e^{\mu\tau}\|v(\tau)\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}\lesssim\|\xi\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.Thmthm8.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmthm8.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Moreover, for every sufficiently large <math id="S4.Thmthm8.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>, such data can be chosen with <math id="S4.Thmthm8.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q+v(0)=\chi_{R}Q+g_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q+v(0)=\chi_{R}Q+g_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S4.Thmthm8.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> lies in a fixed finite-dimensional subspace of radial <math id="S4.Thmthm8.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{c}^{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{c}^{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> and tends to zero in every <math id="S4.Thmthm8.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>H</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{m}</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="S4.Thmthm8.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">To establish the decay estimate
(<a href="#S4.E70" title="In Proposition 4.8. ‣ 4.3. Stability and localization ‣ 4. Self-similar blow-up ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">70</span></a>), we follow the classical
Lyapunov–Perron construction; see, for example,
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib67" title="" class="ltx_ref">67</a>, Section 9.2]</cite>. We then obtain smooth compactly
supported initial data by a finite-dimensional localization
argument related to the constructions in
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib49" title="" class="ltx_ref">49</a>, <a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">46</a>]</cite>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">We prescribe the stable component <math id="S4.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ξ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi</annotation></semantics></math> and choose the unstable component to cancel the backward evolution of the nonlinear term.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="S4.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi\in P_{\mathrm{st}}\mathcal{X}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>st</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi\in P_{\mathrm{st}}\mathcal{X}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>, solve the equation</span></p>
<table id="S4.E71" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S4.E71X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_left">(71)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E71X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle v(\tau)={}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle v(\tau)={}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E71X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle S_{Q}(\tau)\xi+\int_{0}^{\tau}S_{Q}(\tau-\sigma)P_{\mathrm{st}}\mathcal{F}(v(\sigma))\,d\sigma-\int_{\tau}^{\infty}S_{Q}(\tau-\sigma)P_{\mathrm{un}}\mathcal{F}(v(\sigma))\,d\sigma." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>τ</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>st</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">d</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>τ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>un</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">d</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle S_{Q}(\tau)\xi+\int_{0}^{\tau}S_{Q}(\tau-\sigma)P_{\mathrm{st}}\mathcal{F}(v(\sigma))\,d\sigma-\int_{\tau}^{\infty}S_{Q}(\tau-\sigma)P_{\mathrm{un}}\mathcal{F}(v(\sigma))\,d\sigma.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">Choose <math id="S4.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\eta&lt;2\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\eta&lt;2\mu</annotation></semantics></math> in Proposition <a href="#S4.Thmthm7" title="Proposition 4.7. ‣ 4.2. Spectral theory for the linearized operator ‣ 4. Self-similar blow-up ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.7</span></a>. We use the norm <math id="S4.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|v\|_{\mu}:=\sup_{\tau\geq 0}e^{\mu\tau}\|v(\tau)\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|v\|_{\mu}:=\sup_{\tau\geq 0}e^{\mu\tau}\|v(\tau)\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="S4.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|v\|_{\mu}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|v\|_{\mu}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, (<a href="#S4.E60" title="In 4.1. Functional setting ‣ 4. Self-similar blow-up ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">60</span></a>) with <math id="S4.SS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w=0</annotation></semantics></math> gives, since <math id="S4.SS3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}(0)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}(0)=0</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex159" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex159.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathcal{F}(v(\sigma))\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}\leq C_{Q,s}\|v(\sigma)\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}^{2}\leq C_{Q,s}e^{-2\mu\sigma}\|v\|_{\mu}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathcal{F}(v(\sigma))\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}\leq C_{Q,s}\|v(\sigma)\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}^{2}\leq C_{Q,s}e^{-2\mu\sigma}\|v\|_{\mu}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">Here we used <math id="S4.SS3.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|v(\sigma)\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}\leq e^{-\mu\sigma}\|v\|_{\mu}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>μ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|v(\sigma)\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}\leq e^{-\mu\sigma}\|v\|_{\mu}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, for every <math id="S4.SS3.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, we have estimates</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex160" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex160X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex160X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle e^{\mu\tau}\left\|\int_{0}^{\tau}S_{Q}(\tau-\sigma)P_{\mathrm{st}}\mathcal{F}(v(\sigma))\,d\sigma\right\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>τ</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>st</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle e^{\mu\tau}\left\|\int_{0}^{\tau}S_{Q}(\tau-\sigma)P_{\mathrm{st}}\mathcal{F}(v(\sigma))\,d\sigma\right\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex160X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq CC_{Q,s}\|v\|_{\mu}^{2}\int_{0}^{\tau}e^{\mu\tau}e^{-\omega(\tau-\sigma)}e^{-2\mu\sigma}\,d\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>τ</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq CC_{Q,s}\|v\|_{\mu}^{2}\int_{0}^{\tau}e^{\mu\tau}e^{-\omega(\tau-\sigma)}e^{-2\mu\sigma}\,d\sigma</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex160Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex160Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{CC_{Q,s}}{\omega-\mu}\|v\|_{\mu}^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{CC_{Q,s}}{\omega-\mu}\|v\|_{\mu}^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex160Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex160Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle e^{\mu\tau}\left\|\int_{\tau}^{\infty}S_{Q}(\tau-\sigma)P_{\mathrm{un}}\mathcal{F}(v(\sigma))\,d\sigma\right\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>τ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>un</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle e^{\mu\tau}\left\|\int_{\tau}^{\infty}S_{Q}(\tau-\sigma)P_{\mathrm{un}}\mathcal{F}(v(\sigma))\,d\sigma\right\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex160Xb.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq C_{\eta}C_{Q,s}\|v\|_{\mu}^{2}\int_{\tau}^{\infty}e^{\mu\tau}e^{\eta(\sigma-\tau)}e^{-2\mu\sigma}\,d\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>τ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq C_{\eta}C_{Q,s}\|v\|_{\mu}^{2}\int_{\tau}^{\infty}e^{\mu\tau}e^{\eta(\sigma-\tau)}e^{-2\mu\sigma}\,d\sigma</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex160Xc"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex160Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{C_{\eta}C_{Q,s}}{2\mu-\eta}\|v\|_{\mu}^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{C_{\eta}C_{Q,s}}{2\mu-\eta}\|v\|_{\mu}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p4.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p4.5.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="S4.SS3.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|v\|_{\mu},\|w\|_{\mu}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|v\|_{\mu},\|w\|_{\mu}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, the same bounds hold with <math id="S4.SS3.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}(v)-\mathcal{F}(w)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}(v)-\mathcal{F}(w)</annotation></semantics></math> in the integrands and <math id="S4.SS3.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|v\|_{\mu}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|v\|_{\mu}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> replaced by <math id="S4.SS3.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\|v\|_{\mu}+\|w\|_{\mu})\|v-w\|_{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>μ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>μ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\|v\|_{\mu}+\|w\|_{\mu})\|v-w\|_{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math>. Together with (<a href="#S4.E69" title="In Proposition 4.7. ‣ 4.2. Spectral theory for the linearized operator ‣ 4. Self-similar blow-up ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">69</span></a>) and (<a href="#S4.E60" title="In 4.1. Functional setting ‣ 4. Self-similar blow-up ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">60</span></a>), this makes the right-hand side of the equation (<a href="#S4.E71" title="In Proof. ‣ 4.3. Stability and localization ‣ 4. Self-similar blow-up ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">71</span></a>) a contraction on a ball of radius <math id="S4.SS3.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\|\xi\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\|\xi\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}</annotation></semantics></math> in</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex161" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex161.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\{v\in C([0,\infty);\mathcal{X}_{s}):\sup_{\tau\geq 0}e^{\mu\tau}\|v(\tau)\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}&lt;\infty\right\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>:</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.111em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\{v\in C([0,\infty);\mathcal{X}_{s}):\sup_{\tau\geq 0}e^{\mu\tau}\|v(\tau)\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}&lt;\infty\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p4.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p4.6.1" class="ltx_text">The contraction mapping theorem therefore gives a fixed point <math id="S4.SS3.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S4.SS3.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,\infty)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,\infty)</annotation></semantics></math>. Subtracting <math id="S4.SS3.p4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{Q}(\tau)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{Q}(\tau)</annotation></semantics></math> times (<a href="#S4.E71" title="In Proof. ‣ 4.3. Stability and localization ‣ 4. Self-similar blow-up ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">71</span></a>) at <math id="S4.SS3.p4.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=0</annotation></semantics></math> from the same equation at time <math id="S4.SS3.p4.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> yields</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex162" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex162.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v(\tau)=S_{Q}(\tau)v(0)+\int_{0}^{\tau}S_{Q}(\tau-\sigma)\mathcal{F}(v(\sigma))\,d\sigma." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>τ</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v(\tau)=S_{Q}(\tau)v(0)+\int_{0}^{\tau}S_{Q}(\tau-\sigma)\mathcal{F}(v(\sigma))\,d\sigma.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p4.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p4.7.1" class="ltx_text">This shows the existence of a global solution to (<a href="#S4.E52" title="In 4. Self-similar blow-up ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">52</span></a>), with the decay estimate (<a href="#S4.E70" title="In Proposition 4.8. ‣ 4.3. Stability and localization ‣ 4. Self-similar blow-up ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">70</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now we work on the localization. For each <math id="S4.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi\in B_{\epsilon_{0}}(0)\cap P_{\mathrm{st}}\mathcal{X}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>st</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi\in B_{\epsilon_{0}}(0)\cap P_{\mathrm{st}}\mathcal{X}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S4.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{\xi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{\xi}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the unique fixed point constructed above for that stable datum. Define the map <math id="S4.SS3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi:B_{\epsilon_{0}}(0)\cap P_{\mathrm{st}}\mathcal{X}_{s}\to P_{\mathrm{un}}\mathcal{X}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>st</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>un</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi:B_{\epsilon_{0}}(0)\cap P_{\mathrm{st}}\mathcal{X}_{s}\to P_{\mathrm{un}}\mathcal{X}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> by</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex163" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex163.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Phi(\xi):=P_{\mathrm{un}}v_{\xi}(0)=-\int_{0}^{\infty}S_{Q}(-\sigma)P_{\mathrm{un}}\mathcal{F}(v_{\xi}(\sigma))\,d\sigma." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>un</mi></msub><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>un</mi></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi(\xi):=P_{\mathrm{un}}v_{\xi}(0)=-\int_{0}^{\infty}S_{Q}(-\sigma)P_{\mathrm{un}}\mathcal{F}(v_{\xi}(\sigma))\,d\sigma.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">The integral converges in <math id="S4.SS3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> by the preceding estimates, and <math id="S4.SS3.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{\xi}(0)=\xi+\Phi(\xi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{\xi}(0)=\xi+\Phi(\xi)</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular, <math id="S4.SS3.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi(0)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi(0)=0</annotation></semantics></math> since <math id="S4.SS3.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{0}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{0}=0</annotation></semantics></math>. The same estimates for differences give</span></p>
<table id="S4.E72" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(72)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E72.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Phi(\xi)-\Phi(\eta)\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}\lesssim\bigl(\|\xi\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}+\|\eta\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}\bigr)\|\xi-\eta\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msub><mo>≲</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Phi(\xi)-\Phi(\eta)\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}\lesssim\bigl(\|\xi\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}+\|\eta\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}\bigr)\|\xi-\eta\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">To localize, choose a finite-dimensional real space <math id="S4.SS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F\subset C^{\infty}_{c,\mathrm{rad}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>rad</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F\subset C^{\infty}_{c,\mathrm{rad}}</annotation></semantics></math> for which <math id="S4.SS3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\mathrm{un}}|_{F}:F\to P_{\mathrm{un}}\mathcal{X}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>un</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>un</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\mathrm{un}}|_{F}:F\to P_{\mathrm{un}}\mathcal{X}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> is an isomorphism. Density of <math id="S4.SS3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\infty}_{c,\mathrm{rad}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>rad</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\infty}_{c,\mathrm{rad}}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S4.SS3.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> ensures such a choice. By (<a href="#S4.E58" title="In Proof. ‣ 4.1. Functional setting ‣ 4. Self-similar blow-up ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">58</span></a>), <math id="S4.SS3.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\chi_{R}-1)Q\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\chi_{R}-1)Q\to 0</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S4.SS3.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>. Now we show that the equation</span></p>
<table id="S4.E73" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(73)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E73.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{R}=(P_{\mathrm{un}}|_{F})^{-1}\left[\Phi\bigl(P_{\mathrm{st}}((\chi_{R}-1)Q+g_{R})\bigr)-P_{\mathrm{un}}((\chi_{R}-1)Q)\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>un</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>st</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>un</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{R}=(P_{\mathrm{un}}|_{F})^{-1}\left[\Phi\bigl(P_{\mathrm{st}}((\chi_{R}-1)Q+g_{R})\bigr)-P_{\mathrm{un}}((\chi_{R}-1)Q)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">is a contraction on a ball in <math id="S4.SS3.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> of radius <math id="S4.SS3.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\|(\chi_{R}-1)Q\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\|(\chi_{R}-1)Q\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="S4.SS3.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> is sufficiently large. Denote the right-hand side of (<a href="#S4.E73" title="In Proof. ‣ 4.3. Stability and localization ‣ 4. Self-similar blow-up ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">73</span></a>) by <math id="S4.SS3.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{R}(g)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{R}(g)</annotation></semantics></math>. By (<a href="#S4.E72" title="In Proof. ‣ 4.3. Stability and localization ‣ 4. Self-similar blow-up ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">72</span></a>), <math id="S4.SS3.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi(0)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi(0)=0</annotation></semantics></math>, and boundedness of the projections and <math id="S4.SS3.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(P_{\mathrm{un}}|_{F})^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>un</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(P_{\mathrm{un}}|_{F})^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, for <math id="S4.SS3.p6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g,h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g,h</annotation></semantics></math> in this ball we have</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex164" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex164.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{aligned} \|T_{R}(g)\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}&amp;\leq K\|(\chi_{R}-1)Q\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}+K(1+C)^{2}\|(\chi_{R}-1)Q\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}^{2},\\
\|T_{R}(g)-T_{R}(h)\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}&amp;\leq K(1+C)\|(\chi_{R}-1)Q\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}\|g-h\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}\end{aligned}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msub></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msub></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{aligned} \|T_{R}(g)\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}&amp;\leq K\|(\chi_{R}-1)Q\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}+K(1+C)^{2}\|(\chi_{R}-1)Q\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}^{2},\\
\|T_{R}(g)-T_{R}(h)\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}&amp;\leq K(1+C)\|(\chi_{R}-1)Q\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}\|g-h\|_{\mathcal{X}_{s}}\end{aligned},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">with <math id="S4.SS3.p6.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> independent of <math id="S4.SS3.p6.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS3.p6.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>. Fixing <math id="S4.SS3.p6.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C&gt;2K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C&gt;2K</annotation></semantics></math> and then taking <math id="S4.SS3.p6.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> large makes <math id="S4.SS3.p6.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> preserve this ball and have Lipschitz constant less than one; its arguments also lie in the domain of <math id="S4.SS3.p6.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math>. Its solution satisfies <math id="S4.SS3.p6.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\mathrm{un}}((\chi_{R}-1)Q+g_{R})=\Phi(P_{\mathrm{st}}((\chi_{R}-1)Q+g_{R}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>un</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>st</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\mathrm{un}}((\chi_{R}-1)Q+g_{R})=\Phi(P_{\mathrm{st}}((\chi_{R}-1)Q+g_{R}))</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="S4.SS3.p6.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v(0)=(\chi_{R}-1)Q+g_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v(0)=(\chi_{R}-1)Q+g_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> lies on the constructed graph and <math id="S4.SS3.p6.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q+v(0)=\chi_{R}Q+g_{R}\in C_{c}^{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q+v(0)=\chi_{R}Q+g_{R}\in C_{c}^{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S4.SS3.p6.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> is fixed and finite-dimensional, <math id="S4.SS3.p6.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{R}\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{R}\to 0</annotation></semantics></math> in every <math id="S4.SS3.p6.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>H</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem <a href="#S1.Thmthm1" title="Theorem 1.1. ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="S4.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Fix <math id="S4.SS3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\mu&lt;\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\mu&lt;\omega</annotation></semantics></math> and choose localized data from Proposition <a href="#S4.Thmthm8" title="Proposition 4.8. ‣ 4.3. Stability and localization ‣ 4. Self-similar blow-up ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.8</span></a>. By (<a href="#S4.E57" title="In 4.1. Functional setting ‣ 4. Self-similar blow-up ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">57</span></a>) and (<a href="#S4.E70" title="In Proposition 4.8. ‣ 4.3. Stability and localization ‣ 4. Self-similar blow-up ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">70</span></a>), <math id="S4.SS3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V=Q+v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V=Q+v</annotation></semantics></math> is uniformly bounded and</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex165" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex165.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|V(\tau)-Q\|_{L^{\infty}}\lesssim e^{-\mu\tau}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup></msub><mo>≲</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|V(\tau)-Q\|_{L^{\infty}}\lesssim e^{-\mu\tau}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">Its initial datum is smooth and compactly supported. Rewriting the Duhamel formula for <math id="S4.SS3.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> relative to <math id="S4.SS3.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and using (<a href="#S4.E63" title="In 4.1. Functional setting ‣ 4. Self-similar blow-up ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">63</span></a>) shows that <math id="S4.SS3.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> solves (<a href="#S4.E51" title="In 4. Self-similar blow-up ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">51</span></a>). Higher regularity persists, and the tame product estimate yields, for every integer <math id="S4.SS3.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math> for which <math id="S4.SS3.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(0)\in H^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(0)\in H^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S4.E74" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(74)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|V(\tau)\|_{H^{m}}\leq\|V(0)\|_{H^{m}}\exp\left(\left(\frac{d}{4}-\frac{1}{p-1}\right)\tau+C_{m}\int_{0}^{\tau}\|V(\sigma)\|_{\infty}^{p-1}\,d\sigma\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>τ</mi></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|V(\tau)\|_{H^{m}}\leq\|V(0)\|_{H^{m}}\exp\left(\left(\frac{d}{4}-\frac{1}{p-1}\right)\tau+C_{m}\int_{0}^{\tau}\|V(\sigma)\|_{\infty}^{p-1}\,d\sigma\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">Consequently, a bounded <math id="S4.SS3.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> norm prevents finite-time breakdown and propagates all initial Sobolev regularity. Uniqueness and (<a href="#S4.E74" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ 4.3. Stability and localization ‣ 4. Self-similar blow-up ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">74</span></a>) therefore give <math id="S4.SS3.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V\in C([0,\infty);H^{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V\in C([0,\infty);H^{m})</annotation></semantics></math> for every integer <math id="S4.SS3.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. For any <math id="S4.SS3.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, undoing (<a href="#S2.E4" title="In 2. Self-similar profile equation ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>) gives</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex166" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex166.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u(t,x)=(T-t)^{-\frac{1}{p-1}}e^{-i\Omega\tau}V(\tau,y)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u(t,x)=(T-t)^{-\frac{1}{p-1}}e^{-i\Omega\tau}V(\tau,y).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p7.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p7.4.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex167" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex167.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\left\|(T-t)^{\frac{1}{p-1}}e^{i\Omega\tau}u\left(t,\sqrt{T-t}\,\cdot\right)-Q\right\|_{\infty}=O((T-t)^{\mu})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.392em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>μ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|(T-t)^{\frac{1}{p-1}}e^{i\Omega\tau}u\left(t,\sqrt{T-t}\,\cdot\right)-Q\right\|_{\infty}=O((T-t)^{\mu}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p7.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p7.5.1" class="ltx_text">and hence</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex168" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex168.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|u(t)\|_{\infty}=(T-t)^{-\frac{1}{p-1}}\left(\|Q\|_{\infty}+O((T-t)^{\mu})\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>μ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|u(t)\|_{\infty}=(T-t)^{-\frac{1}{p-1}}\left(\|Q\|_{\infty}+O((T-t)^{\mu})\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p7.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p7.6.1" class="ltx_text">The resulting solution lies in <math id="S4.SS3.p7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C([0,T);H^{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C([0,T);H^{m})</annotation></semantics></math> for every <math id="S4.SS3.p7.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>, with smooth compactly supported initial data. Since <math id="S4.SS3.p7.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(0)=A&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(0)=A&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="S4.SS3.p7.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|Q\|_{\infty}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|Q\|_{\infty}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S4.SS3.p7.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> is its maximal time of existence. Finally, (<a href="#S4.E54" title="In Lemma 4.1. ‣ 4. Self-similar blow-up ‣ Blow-up for energy supercritical defocusing nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimensions three, four and five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">54</span></a>) gives <math id="S4.SS3.p7.m17" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="|Q(r)|\gtrsim r^{-2/(p-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≳</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|Q(r)|\gtrsim r^{-2/(p-1)}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S4.SS3.p7.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex169" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex169.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}|Q(x)|^{\frac{d(p-1)}{2}}\,dx\gtrsim\int_{1}^{\infty}r^{d-1}r^{-d}\,dr=\int_{1}^{\infty}\frac{dr}{r}=\infty," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mrow><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≳</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mi>r</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}|Q(x)|^{\frac{d(p-1)}{2}}\,dx\gtrsim\int_{1}^{\infty}r^{d-1}r^{-d}\,dr=\int_{1}^{\infty}\frac{dr}{r}=\infty,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p7.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p7.7.1" class="ltx_text">so <math id="S4.SS3.p7.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q\notin L^{d(p-1)/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>∉</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q\notin L^{d(p-1)/2}</annotation></semantics></math>. As <math id="S4.SS3.p7.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(\tau)\to Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(\tau)\to Q</annotation></semantics></math> pointwise, Fatou’s lemma gives <math id="S4.SS3.p7.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|V(\tau)\|_{L^{d(p-1)/2}}\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|V(\tau)\|_{L^{d(p-1)/2}}\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. Sobolev embedding and scaling invariance yield</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex170" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex170.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|u(t)\|_{\dot{H}^{s_{c}}}\gtrsim\|u(t)\|_{L^{\frac{d(p-1)}{2}}}=\|V(\tau)\|_{L^{\frac{d(p-1)}{2}}}\longrightarrow\infty," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></msup></msub><mo>≳</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|u(t)\|_{\dot{H}^{s_{c}}}\gtrsim\|u(t)\|_{L^{\frac{d(p-1)}{2}}}=\|V(\tau)\|_{L^{\frac{d(p-1)}{2}}}\longrightarrow\infty,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p7.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p7.8.1" class="ltx_text">which completes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
